('en', 'CET-4', 'initiate', '/ɪ\'nɪʃɪeɪt/', '开始，发起', 'v', 'They have decided to initiate legal proceedings against the newspaper. (他们决定向该报提起法律诉讼。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'initiative', '/i\'niʃətiv/', '主动权，自主权', 'n', 'I wish my son would show more initiative. (我希望我的儿子能表现得再主动一些。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'injure', '/\'ɪndʒə(r)/', '使受伤', 'v', 'Angus injured his leg playing rugby. (安格斯在打橄榄球时弄伤了腿。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'innocent', '/\'ɪnəs(ə)nt/', '无辜的，天真的；', 'adj', 'Nobody would believe that I was innocent. (没人肯相信我是清白的。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'innovation', '/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn/', '改革，创新', 'n', 'We must encourage innovation if the company is to remain competitive. (公司要想保持竞争力，就必须鼓励革新。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'insecure', '/,ɪnsɪ\'kjʊə;/', '不安全的', 'adj', 'Many of them work in low-paid insecure jobs. (他们当中的许多人都做着薪水低、不稳定的工作。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'insight', '/\'ɪnsaɪt/', '洞察力，洞悉', 'n', 'a woman of great insight (一位极有眼光的妇女)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'inspiration', '/ˌɪnspə\'reɪʃn/', '灵感', 'n', 'The Malvern Hills have provided inspiration for many artists and musicians over the decades. (几十年来，莫尔文丘陵为很多艺术家和音乐家提供了灵感。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'inspire', '/in\'spaɪə/', '激发；鼓舞；使产生灵感', 'v', 'We need someone who can inspire the team. (我们需要一个能鼓舞团队士气的人。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'install', '/ɪnˈstɔ:l/', '安装', 'v', 'They’ve installed the new computer network at last. (他们终于安装了新电脑网络。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'installation', '/,ɪnstə\'leɪʃən/', '安装，就任', 'n', 'the installation and maintenance of alarm systems (警报系统的安装和维护)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'installment', '/ɪn\'stɔ:lmənt/', '安装，分期付款', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'instant', '/\'ɪnstənt/', '立即的；紧急的；速溶的，方便的', 'adj', 'an instant success (马到成功)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'institute', '/\'ɪnstɪtju:t/', '建立', 'n & v', 'We will institute a number of measures to better safeguard the public. (我们将制定许多措施更好地保护公众。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'institution', '/,insti\'tju:ʃən/', '社会公共机构；制度，习俗；设立，制定', 'n', 'powerful institutions such as world banks (诸如世界银行之类的强大机构)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'instruction', '/ɪn\'strʌkʃən/', '命令，指示，用法说明', 'n', 'Press ‘Enter’ and follow the on-screen instructions. (按回车键，然后按照电脑屏幕上的指示来操作。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'instruct', '/ɪn\'strʌkt/', '指导；通知；命令；教授', 'v', 'Eva went straight to the hotel, as instructed (= as she had been told ). (伊娃按照指示径直去了宾馆。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'instrument', '/\'ɪnstrumənt/', '仪器，器械，工具', 'n', 'surgical instruments (外科(手术)器械)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'intake', '/ˈɪnteɪk/', '摄入', 'n', 'Your intake of alcohol should not exceed two units per day. (你每天酒精摄入量不能超过两个单位。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'integrity', '/ɪn\'tegrɪtɪ/', '完整，综合', 'n', 'the territorial integrity of the country (国家的领土完整)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'intelligence', '/in\'telidʒəns/', '智力，智慧，理解力', 'n', 'To be good at the game, you need a reasonable level of intelligence. (要想把这种游戏玩好，需要一定的智力水平。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'intelligent', '/ɪn\'telɪdʒ(ə)nt/', '智能的', 'adj', 'a group of highly intelligent (= very intelligent )students (一组聪明异常的学生)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'intend', '/ɪn\'tend/', '打算', 'v', 'Oddly enough, that is precisely what I intend. (说也奇怪， 那正是我的打算。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'interconnect', '/ɪntəkə\'nekt/', '相互联系', 'v', 'In Freud’s theory, the two areas of sexuality and violence are interconnected. (按照弗洛伊德的理论，性和暴力这两个方面是相互关联的。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'interdependence', '/,ɪntədɪ\'pendəns/', '相互依靠', 'n', '...the interdependence of nations. (…国家间的相互依赖。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'interpret', '/ɪn\'tɜ:prɪt/', '解释', 'v', 'Freud’s attempts to interpret the meaning of dreams (弗洛伊德对梦的含义的解析)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'interracial', '/ɪntə\'reɪʃ(ə)l/', '种族间的', 'adj', 'interracial marriage (种族间的通婚)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'intervention', '/ˌɪntə\'venʃn/', '干涉', 'n', 'government intervention to regulate prices (政府介入控制物价)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'interview', '/\'intəvju:/', '会见；面谈（试）；采访', 'n', 'a portfolio of work presented at interview (在面试时呈递的工作成果样本)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'invade', '/ɪn\'veɪd/', '侵入，侵略', 'v', 'The Romans invaded Britain 2,000 years ago. (2,000年前古罗马人入侵了英国。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'invalid', '/ɪn\'vælɪd/', '无效的', 'adj', 'Without the right date stamped on it, your ticket will be invalid. (票上若没有加盖正确日期就是废票。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'invest', '/ɪn\'vest/', '投资', 'v', 'I’ve got a few thousand dollars I’m looking to invest. (我有几千美元想作投资。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'involve', '/ɪn\'vɒlv/', '卷入，包含', 'v', 'What will the job involve? (这份工作包括什么？)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'irrationally', '/ɪ\'ræʃnəlɪ/', '不合理地，无理性地', 'adv', NULL, 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'irritate', '/\'ɪrɪteɪt/', '激怒', 'v', 'It really irritates me when he doesn’t help around the house. (家里的事情他一点都不帮忙，真让我恼火。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'issue', '/\'ɪʃu:/', '发行；问题', 'v', 'Silva issued a statement denying all knowledge of the affair. (西尔瓦发表声明，宣称对此事一无所知。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'item', '/\'aɪtəm/', '条，条款', 'n', 'He opened the cardboard box and took out each item. (他打开纸板箱把里面的物品一一拿出来。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'joint', '/dʒɒɪnt/', '联合的', 'adj', 'The two ministers have issued a joint statement. (两位部长发布了一项联合声明。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'keenly', '/ki:nlɪ/', '敏锐地', 'adv', 'He observes keenly but says very little. (他观察敏锐， 但说得很少。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'launch', '/lɔ:ntʃ/', '发射', 'v', 'The organization has launched a campaign to raise $150,000. (为了筹集15万美元，该组织发起了一场募捐活动。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'laundry', '/\'lɔ:ndrɪ/', '洗衣房；要洗的衣服', 'n', 'She did the laundry (= washed the clothes etc ) and hung it out to dry. (她洗了衣服，然后挂出去晾干。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'legal', '/\'li:ɡl/', '法律的', 'adj', 'What the company has done is perfectly legal. (公司所做的这一切完全合法。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'leisure', '/\'leʒə(r)/', '悠闲，空闲', 'n', 'Most people now enjoy shorter working hours and more leisure time. (现在大多数人都喜欢工作时间短些，闲暇时间多些。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'lengthy', '/\'leŋθɪ/', '长的，漫长的', 'adj', 'A lengthy period of training is required. (需要很长一段时间的培训。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'liability', '/ˌlaɪəˈbɪləti/', '责任', 'n', 'But without the formal business entity, you have no hope of limiting your personal liability. (因为没有正规的商务体制，你就没有希望限制你的个人责任。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'literature', '/\'litərətʃə/', '文学，文学作品；文献', 'n', 'He has read many of the major works of literature. (他读过许多重要的文学作品。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'loan', '/ləʊn/', '贷款', 'n', 'We obtained a loan from the government. (我们得了一笔政府贷款。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'locate', '/lə(ʊ)\'keɪt/', '位于，定位', 'v', 'The business is located right in the center of town. (这家商店就在市中心。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'lodge', '/lɒdʒ/', '住宿，暂住', 'v', 'a building used to lodge prisoners of war (一座关押战俘的建筑物)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'logic', '/\'lɒdʒɪk/', '逻辑', 'n', 'There isa certain logicin their choice of architect. (他们对建筑师的选择是有一定道理的。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'loyalty', '/\'lɔɪəltɪ/', '忠诚，忠实', 'n', 'the agony of divided loyalties (= loyalty to two different or opposing people ) for the children in a divorce (父母离婚过程中孩子两面都要依顺的痛苦)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'mainstream', '/\'meɪnstri:m/', '主流', 'n', 'Genet started as a rebel, but soon became part of the literary mainstream. (热内起初很叛逆，但不久就回归了文学主流。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'maintain', '/meɪn\'teɪn/', '维持，主张', 'v', 'Careers Officers maintain contact with young people when they have left school. (年轻人离开学校以后，职业指导员和他们保持联系。)', 2);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', 'CET-4', 'major', '/\'meɪdʒə(r)/', '主要的；主修', 'adj', 'There are two major political parties in the US. (美国有两大政党。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'majority', '/mə\'dʒɒrətɪ/', '多数', 'n', 'The Labour Party won a huge majority at the last general election. (工党在上次大选中以巨大的票数优势获胜。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'makeup', '/\'meɪkʌp/', '化装', 'n', 'Normally she wore little makeup, but this evening was clearly an exception. (通常她很少化妆，可今晚显然是个例外。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'malfunction', '/mæl\'fʌŋ(k)ʃ(ə)n/', '失灵，故障', 'n', 'a malfunction in one of the engines (其中一个引擎的失灵)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'manufacture', '/ˌmænjʊ\'fæktʃə(r)/', '制造，生产', 'v', 'the company that manufactured the drug (生产这种药的公司)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'margin', '/\'mɑ:dʒɪn/', '边缘，范围', 'n', 'the western margin of southern Africa (非洲南部的西隅)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'marvelous', '/\'mɑ:vɪləs/', '引起惊异的', 'adj', NULL, 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'masculine', '/\'mæskjʊlɪn/', '男性的', 'adj', 'They’re nice curtains, but I’d prefer something a little more masculine. (这些窗帘很好，但我更喜欢男性化一点的。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'massive', '/\'mæsiv/', '巨大的 大量的', 'adj', 'The bell is massive, weighing over 40 tons. (那口钟非常大，有40多吨重。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'matter', '/\'mætə(r)/', '要紧，重要', 'v', 'If I have to stay late at work tonight, it won’t matter because we can go out another night. (如果今晚我必须工作到很晚的话，那也没关系，我们可以改天晚上再出去。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'maximum', '/\'mæksɪməm/', '最大值的，最大量的', 'n & a', 'We might have a third child, but that’s the absolute maximum . (我们可能会要第三个孩子，但这绝对是极限了。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'means', '/mi:nz/', '方法', 'n', 'The only means of communication was sign language. (唯一的交流方法是手语。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'measure', '/\'meʒə/', '分量，尺寸，量具，测量；；测量', 'n', 'She soon got the measure of her opponent. (她很快就掂出了对手的分量。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'mechanic', '/mə\'kænɪk/', '机械师', 'n', 'a garage mechanic (汽车修理厂的技工)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'mechanism', '/\'mekənɪzəm/', '机制，机能', 'n', 'the brake mechanism (刹车装置)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'merit', '/\'merit/', '优点，成绩；值得', 'n', 'The merit of the report is its realistic assessment of the changes required. (这份报告的优点就是它对所要求的变动进行了实事求是的评估。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'migration', '/maɪˈgreɪʃn/', '迁移，移民', 'n', 'What does this migration not do? (这种迁移不能做什么？)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'military', '/\'mɪlətrɪ/', '军队的，军事的', 'adj', 'a military helicopter (军用直升机)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'mineral', '/\'mɪnərəl/', '矿物的，似矿物的', 'adj', 'Or they could be trained to use weeds as indicators of the soil\'s mineral properties to help them manage nutrients. (或者可以训练他们使用杂草作为土壤矿物属性的指示器，从而帮助他们管理营养物质。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'miscalculation', '/ˌmɪskælkjʊ\'leɪʃn/', '算错，误算', 'n', 'KAPLAN: Well, there\'s always the risk of a miscalculation or an accident at sea. (卡普兰：呃，在海上总会有误算的风险，也有发生事故的风险。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'miserable', '/ˈmɪzrəbl/', '痛苦的', 'adj', 'I’ve been so miserable since Pat left me. (自从帕特离我而去后，我十分痛苦。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'misguided', '/ˌmɪs\'ɡaɪdɪd/', '被误导的', 'adj', 'His parents still clung to the misguided belief that his common sense would keep him out of serious trouble. (他的父母依然错误地认为他的常识能让他远离大的麻烦。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'mislead', '/ˌmɪs\'li:d/', '误导', 'v', 'Don’t be misled by appearances, he’s a good worker. (不要被表象迷惑，他工作干得挺不错的。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'mission', '/\'miʃən/', '使命，任务；代表团', 'n', 'He was sent on over 200 missions before being killed in action. (在阵亡之前他奉命执行过200多次军事任务。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'misunderstand', '/,mɪsʌndə\'stænd/', '误解', 'v', 'Rachel, you must have misunderstood her! Ellie would never say something like that. (雷切尔，你一定是误会她了！埃莉绝不会说那样的话。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'monitor', '/\'mɒnɪtə(r)/', '监控，监听', 'v', 'Patients who are given the new drug will be asked to monitor their progress. (使用这种新药的病人将被要求监测病情进展。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'motivate', '/\'məʊtɪveɪt/', '促动，激发，诱导', 'v', 'A good teacher has to be able to motivate her students. (好教师必须能够激发学生的积极性。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'motivation', '/ˌməʊtɪ\'veɪʃn/', '激励，刺激', 'n', NULL, 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'mutual', '/\'mjuːtʃʊəl/', '相互的', 'adj', 'I didn’t like Dev, and the feeling seemed to be mutual. (我不喜欢德夫，他好像也不喜欢我。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'narrow', '/\'nærəʊ/', '限制', 'v', NULL, 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'needy', '/\'ni:dɪ/', '贫穷的', 'adj', 'a needy family (贫困家庭)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'negative', '/\'negətiv/', '否定的；消积的', 'adj', 'students with a negative attitude to school (对上学抱消极态度的学生)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'negotiate', '/nɪ\'ɡəʊʃɪeɪt/', '谈判，协商，交涉', 'v', 'His first aim is to get the warring parties back to the negotiating table (= discussing something ). (他的首要目标就是把交战各方拉回到谈判桌上。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'neighborhood', '/\'neɪbəhʊd/', '地区', 'n', 'Iterates may be categorized into stable and unstable sets depending on whether a neighborhood under iteration converges or diverges. Some move toward stability, others away. (根据一个受迭代影响的社区是聚合还是发散，迭代可以被归类到稳定和不稳定集。有些转向稳定，有些转离。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'obstacle', '/ˈɒbstəkl/', '阻碍', 'n', 'The tax puts obstacles in the way of companies trying to develop trade overseas. (这项税收为想在海外发展贸易的公司设置了障碍。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'obtain', '/əb\'teɪn/', '获得', 'v', 'Evans was trying to obtain a false passport and other documents. (埃文斯当时正试图获取假护照和其他文件。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'occupation', '/ˌɒkjuˈpeɪʃn/', '职业，工作', 'n', 'Please state your name, address and occupation. (请写明你的姓名、地址和职业。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'operation', '/ˌɒpəˈreɪʃn/', '手术；行动', 'n', 'The UN rescue operation started shortly after dawn. (联合国的救援行动在破晓后不久就开始了。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'opposite', '/ˈɔpəzɪt/', '相反的', 'adj', 'I thought the medicine would make him sleep, but it had the opposite effect. (我以为这药会让他睡觉，但是它却起了反作用。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'organ', '/\'ɔ:ɡən/', '器官', 'n', 'the liver, heart, and other internal organs (肝脏、心脏及其他内脏器官)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'original', '/ə\'ridʒənl/', '原始的，最初的', 'adj', 'The land was returned to its original owner. (这块土地归还给了原主。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'originate', '/ə\'rɪdʒɪneɪt/', '开始', 'v', 'How did the plan originate? (这个计划最早是怎么想到的？)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'outline', '/\'aʊtlaɪn/', '梗概，提纲，草稿，要点', 'n', 'a research proposal outline (研究计划梗概)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'overcome', '/ˌəʊvə\'kʌm/', '战胜，克服', 'v', 'He struggled to overcome his shyness. (他努力克服自己的羞怯。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'overestimate', '/ˌəʊvər\'estɪmeɪt/', '对（数量）估计过高', 'v', 'He tends to overestimate his own abilities. (他往往高估自己的能力。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'overflow', '/ˌəʊvə\'fləʊ/', '溢出，淹没', 'v', 'The drains flooded and water overflowed down the main street. (下水道被淹，水溢到了大街上。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'overload', '/ˌəʊvə\'ləʊd/', '使负担太重', 'n', '57 percent complained of work overload. (57%的人抱怨工作负担过重。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'overtake', '/ˌəʊvə\'teɪk/', '超车', 'v', 'He pulled out to overtake the van. (他把车驶出所在车道想超过那辆小货车。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'overweight', '/ˌəʊvə\'weɪt/', '超重的', 'v', 'I wonder if this letter is overweight. (我想知道这封信是否超重。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'overwhelm', '/əʊvə\'welm/', '压倒，战胜', 'v', 'But the various pros and cons should not blindly overwhelm one another. (但是，众多的利弊得失不应盲目的一个压倒另一个。)', 3),
