('en', 'CET-4', 'unrest', '/ʌn\'rest/', '不安定，动荡', 'n', 'There is growing unrest throughout the country. (全国各地日益动荡不安。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'authoritative', '/ɔː\'θɒrɪtətɪv/', '权威的', 'adj', 'the most authoritative work on English surnames (有关英语姓氏的最权威著作)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'neutral', '/\'njuːtr(ə)l/', '中立的', 'adj', 'I always tried to remain neutral when they started arguing. (他们争论起来的时候我总是努力保持中立。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'racially', '/\'reʃəli/', '种族上地', 'adv', 'Mr. Obama is the first president since Richard M. Nixon to be elected while living in a city neighborhood, in his case, Chicago’s racially and economically diverse Hyde Park. (奥巴马是自理查德.尼克松总统以来第一位住在城市社区中当选的总统，奥巴马住在芝加哥种族和经济多元化的海德公园。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'disappointing', '/dɪsə\'pɒɪntɪŋ/', '令人失望的', 'adj', 'disappointing profit figures (令人失望的盈利数字)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'plant', '/plɑːnt/', '工厂', 'n', 'a huge chemical plant (一座大型化工厂)', 2),
