('en', 'CET-4', 'deceit', '/dɪ\'siːt/', '欺骗，欺诈', 'n', 'an atmosphere of hypocrisy and deceit (充满虚伪和欺骗的氛围)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'deceive', '/dɪ\'siːv/', '欺骗，蒙蔽，行骗', 'v', 'He had been deceived by a young man claiming to be the son of a millionaire. (他被一个自称是百万富翁之子的年轻人骗了。)', 2),
