('en', 'CET-4', 'deer', '/dɪə/', '鹿', 'n', 'The hunter wounded the deer. (猎人打伤了鹿。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'defeat', '/dɪ\'fiːt/', '战胜，击败；挫败', 'v', 'They hoped to defeat the enemy at sea. (他们希望在海上击败敌人。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'defect', '/\'diːfekt; dɪ\'fekt/', '缺点，缺陷，欠缺', 'n', 'All the cars are tested for defects before they leave the factory. (所有汽车在出厂前都经过品质检验。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'defence', '/dɪ\'fens/', '防御；防务；辩护', 'n', 'The land was flat, giving no scope for defence. (土地非常平坦，无法做防卫之用。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'defend', '/dɪ\'fend/', '保卫，防守', 'v', 'a struggle to defend our homeland (保卫我们祖国的斗争)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'define', '/dɪ\'faɪn/', '给…下定义；限定', 'v', 'I’ll now try to define the term ‘popular culture’. (我现在来试试给 “通俗文化” 这个词下定义。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'definite', '/\'defɪnɪt/', '明确的；肯定的', 'adj', 'It’s impossible for me to give you a definite answer. (我不可能给你明确的答复。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'definitely', '/\'defɪnɪtlɪ/', '一定地，明确地', 'adv', '‘Do you reckon Margot will be there?’ ‘ Definitely not .’ (“你估计玛戈会在那里吗？” “肯定不会。”)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'definition', '/defɪ\'nɪʃ(ə)n/', '定义，释义；定界', 'n', 'a dictionary definition (词典里的释义)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'degree', NULL, '程度；度；学位', 'n', 'Preheat the oven to 425 degrees. (把烘箱预热至425度。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'delay', '/dɪ\'leɪ/', '推迟；耽搁；延误', 'v', 'Don’t delay – send off for the information now. (别犹豫——即刻去函索取信息。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'delegation', '/delɪ\'geɪʃ(ə)n/', '代表团', 'n', 'A trade delegation will visit Kuwait. (一个贸易代表团将访问科威特。)', 1);
