('en', 'CET-4', 'navigation', '/nævɪ\'geɪʃ(ə)n/', '航行；航海术；导航', 'n', 'compasses and other instruments of navigation (罗盘及其他导航仪器)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'navy', '/\'neɪvɪ/', '海军', 'n', 'the British Navy (英国海军)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'near', '/nɪə/', '近，接近；近的', 'adv', 'They live near London. (他们住在伦敦附近。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'nearby', '/\'nɪəbaɪ/', '附近的；在附近', 'adj', 'Lucy was staying in the nearby town of Hamilton. (露西当时住在附近的汉密尔顿镇。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'nearly', '/\'nɪəlɪ/', '差不多；密切地', 'adv', 'It took nearly two hours to get here. (到这里花了将近两小时。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'neat', '/niːt/', '整洁的；熟练的', 'adj', 'neat handwriting (工整的笔迹)', 3),
('en', 'CET-4', 'necessarily', '/\'nesəs(ə)rɪlɪ; ,nesə\'serɪlɪ/', '必然，必定', 'adv', 'The care of old people necessarily involves quite a lot of heavy lifting. (照顾老年人必定要干很多搬重物的活儿。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'necessary', '/ˈnɛsɪsərɪ/', '必要的；必然的', 'adj', 'The booklet provides all the necessary information about the college. (这本小册子提供了关于那所学院的所有必需信息。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'necessity', '/nɪ\'sesɪtɪ/', '必要性；必然性', 'n', 'I’m afraid it’s become a matter of economic necessity. (恐怕这已成了一个经济需求的问题。)', 3),
