('en', 'CET-4', 'ounce', '/auns/', ' 盎司', 'n', 'How to pronounce the noun "ounce" in the announcement? (布告中的名词“盎司“怎样发音?。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'challenge', '/\'tʃælɪndʒ/', '挑战；邀请比赛；艰巨的任务；怀疑，质问； 反对， 公然反抗； 向…挑战； 对…质疑', 'n', 'They threw down the challenge that he couldn’t wash 40 cars in one hour (= invited him to try to do it ) . (他们激将他，说他不可能在1小时内擦洗40辆汽车。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'emit', '/i\'mɪt/', ' 散发； 发射； 发表', 'vt', 'The kettle emitted a shrill whistle. (水壶发出了刺耳的鸣笛声。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'category', '/\'kætəgəri/', ' 种类， 类， 类别', 'n', 'people in the over-45 age category (属45岁以上年龄组的人)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'rival', '/\'raɪvl/', '竞争的，对抗的；竞争对手，敌手；可与匹敌的人； 与 …竞争； 与…匹敌， 比得上', 'adj', 'He is, in effect, my rival. (实际上他是我的竞争对手。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-4', 'intend', '/ɪn\'tend/', ' 想要， 打算； 意思是； 打算使', 'vt', 'Maybe he intends to leave her. (也许他打算离开她。)', 1),
('en', 'CET-4', 'snap', '/snæp/', '咔嚓折断，啪地绷断；吧嗒一声；猛咬；厉声说话，怒声责骂； 仓促的， 突然的；吧嗒声；快照', 'v', 'A twig snapped under my feet. (一根细枝在我脚下嚓一声断开了。)', 3);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', 'CET-6', 'abandonment', '/əˈbændənmənt/', '放弃', 'n', '...memories of her father\'s complete abandonment of her. (…她父亲对她的彻底抛弃的那些记忆。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'abnormally', '/æb\'nɔ:məlɪ/', '不正常的', 'adv', 'Both were big at birth but were not abnormally large. (这两个孩子出生时都比较大，但并非异常的大。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'absolutely', '/ˈæbsəlu:tli/', '当然', 'adv', '‘Do you let your kids travel alone at night?’ ‘Absolutely not!’ (“你会让孩子们晚上单独外出吗？”“当然不行！”)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'abstract', '/\'æbstrækt/', '抽象的', 'adj', 'By the age of seven, children are capable of thinking in abstract terms . (儿童到了七岁就具有抽象思维的能力。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'abuse', '/ə\'bju:s/', '虐待；滥用', 'n', 'several cases of child abuse (数宗虐待儿童案)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'accelerate', '/ək\'seləreɪt/', '加速', 'v', 'measures to accelerate the rate of economic growth (加快经济增长速度的措施)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'accomplish', '/ə\'kʌmplɪʃ/', '实现', 'v', 'We have accomplished all we set out to do. (所有计划要做的事情，我们都已完成。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'accountant', '/əˈkaʊntənt/', '会计', 'n', 'The boss dropped an accountant from the payroll. (老板把一名会计师从在职人员名单中除了名。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'accrue', '/ə\'kru:/', '积累', 'v', 'Interest will accrue until payment is made. (利息将会累计增加，直至付清款项。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'accurate', '/ˈækjərət/', '精确的', 'adj', 'The brochure tries to give a fair and accurate description of each hotel. (该手册尽量公正、准确地介绍每一家酒店。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'accuse', '/ə\'kju:z/', '指控', 'v', 'The professor stands accused of (=  has been accused of  ) stealing his student’s ideas and publishing them. (那位教授被指控剽窃学生的观点拿去发表。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'accustom', '/ə\'kʌstəm/', '使习惯', 'v', 'She tried to accustom herself to the tight bandages. (她尝试着使自己习惯那些紧绷的绷带。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'achieve', '/ə\'tʃi:v/', '达到，实现', 'v', 'Frances achieved very good exam results. (弗朗西丝考试取得了优异成绩。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'acquaintance', '/ə\'kweɪntəns/', '熟人', 'n', 'She was a casual acquaintance of my family in Vienna. (她是我们家在维也纳的一个交情不深的朋友。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'activate', '/\'æktɪveɪt/', '激活', 'v', 'Cooking fumes may activate the alarm. (烹调时的油烟可能会触发警报器。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'acutely', '/əˈkju:tli/', '敏锐地', 'adv', 'We continue to conduct tests, but increasingly, we conduct long conversations with her, acutely aware that our creation will raise many ethical questions on the part of the public. (我们将继续进行测试，但越来越多地，随着长时间的交谈，我们敏锐地意识到，我们的作品将在公众当中引起许多道德问题。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'addict', '/\'ædɪkt/', '上瘾，沉溺', 'v', 'Meanwhile, Walt\'s meth-business partner, the addict Jesse, is still recovering from the drug-related death of his girlfriend Jane at the end of last season. (而沃特的制毒搭档——瘾君子杰西还未从女朋友之死的痛苦中恢复过来。 他的女朋友简在上一季结尾时死于毒品。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'address', '/ə\'dres/', '解决', 'v', NULL, 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'administration', '/ədˌmɪnɪˈstreɪʃn/', '管理，政府', 'n', 'We’re looking for someone with experience in administration. (我们正在寻找一个有管理经验的人。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'adopt', '/ə\'dɒpt/', '采纳', 'v', 'The courts were asked to adopt a more flexible approach to young offenders. (法庭被要求对少年犯采取更为灵活的处理方法。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'adventure', '/əd\'ventʃə(r)/', '冒险', 'n', 'a great adventure (一大奇遇)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'adventurer', '/ədˈventʃərə(r)/', '冒险者', 'n', 'an adventurer travelling the world (周游世界的冒险家)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'adverse', '/ˈædvɜ:s/', '相反的，敌对的', 'adj', 'They fear it could have an adverse effect on global financial markets. (他们担心这会对全球金融市场产生不利影响。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'adversely', '/əd\'vɜ:slɪ/', '不利地', 'adv', 'I think everyone has something from their past that they\'re worried might adversely affect how they raise their children. (我想每个人都会担心自己过去的某些事可能会对他们如何培养孩子产生不利的影响。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'affection', '/əˈfekʃn/', '喜爱', 'n', 'She looked back on those days with affection . (她深情地回顾那些日子。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'agenda', '/ə\'dʒendə/', '议程', 'n', 'The Republicans have stuck to their conservative agenda. (共和党人坚持自己的保守议题。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'aggravate', '/\'æɡrəveɪt/', '加重，加剧', 'v', 'Their money problems were further aggravated by a rise in interest rates. (由于利率上调，他们的财务问题更加严重。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'agonize', '/\'æɡənaɪz/', '使痛苦', 'v', 'As a mother, I agonize over what my children will inherit. (作为一个母亲，我对我的孩子们将要继承的东西感到极度痛苦。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'aid', '/eɪd/', '援助，有助于', 'v', 'an index to aid the reader (方便读者的索引)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'alert', '/ə\'lɜ:t/', '机警的；提醒', 'adj', 'The animal raised its head, suddenly alert. (那只动物突然警觉地抬起头来。)', 2),
