('en', 'CET-6', 'lack', '/læk/', '缺少', 'v', 'Alex’s real problem is that he lacks confidence. (亚历克斯的真正问题是缺乏信心。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'lag', '/læɡ/', '落后', 'v', 'Western banks still lag behind financial institutions in most other regions of the country. (西部地区的银行仍然落后于这个国家其他大部分地区的金融机构。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'launch', '/lɔ:ntʃ/', '发布，推出', 'v', 'The company hopes to launch the new drug by next October. (公司希望于明年10月前推出这种新药。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'lawn', '/lɔ:n/', '草坪', 'n', 'I spent all morning mowing the lawn (= cutting the grass ). (我整个上午都在修剪草坪。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'layman', '/\'leɪmən/', '门外汉', 'n', 'To the layman (= laymen in general ) all these plants look pretty similar. (对外行的人来说，这些植物看起来都很相似。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'layout', '/ˈleɪaʊt/', '陈列', 'n', NULL, 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'legend', '/\'ledʒənd/', '传奇', 'n', 'Local legend has it that (= says that ) the island was the original Garden of Eden. (当地传说这个岛就是伊甸园的原型。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'legislation', '/ˌledʒɪsˈleɪʃn/', '立法', 'n', 'This is a very important piece of legislation (= law ). (这是一条非常重要的法规。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'legislator', '/ˈledʒɪsleɪtə(r)/', '立法者', 'n', '...an attempt to get U.S. legislators to change the system. (…让美国立法者改变体制的一次努力。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'lest', '/lest/', '以免', 'conj', 'She turned away from the window lest anyone see them. (她转身离开窗边，免得有人看见他们。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'lobby', '/\'lɒbɪ/', '游说', 'n', 'the anti-foxhunting lobby (反对猎狐的游说团体)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'luxurious', '/lʌgˈʒʊəriəs/', '奢侈的，豪华的', 'adj', 'a luxurious 30-room villa (一栋有30个房间的豪华度假别墅)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'magnify', '/\'mæɡnɪfaɪ/', '放大', 'v', 'At the Sheffield arena, the speakers were magnified ten times on a giant screen. (在谢菲尔德体育馆，演讲者在一个巨大的屏幕上被放大了十倍。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'maintenance', '/\'meɪntənəns/', '维修', 'n', 'the cost of repairs and maintenance (维修保养费)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'majority', '/mə\'dʒɒrətɪ/', '大多数', 'n', 'The Labour Party won a huge majority at the last general election. (工党在上次大选中以巨大的票数优势获胜。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'mall', '/mɔ:l/', '商场', 'n', 'In the winter I head for the mall. (在冬日里,我前往这个购物商场。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'manifest', '/\'mænɪfest/', '表明', 'v', 'The shareholders have manifested their intention to sell the shares. (股东们表明了要出售股票的意图。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'manufacture', '/ˌmænjʊ\'fæktʃə(r)/', '生产，制造', 'v', 'the company that manufactured the drug (生产这种药的公司)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'marine', '/mə\'ri:n/', '海洋的', 'adj', 'the enormous variety of marine life (海洋生物繁多的种类)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'markedly', '/\'mɑ:kɪdlɪ/', '显著地', 'adv', 'The relations between our two countries have improved markedly in every aspect. (我们两国的关系在各方面都有了显著的发展。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'mask', '/mɑ:sk/', '面具；掩饰 掩盖', 'n', 'a surgical face mask (外科手术口罩)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'material', '/məˈtɪəriəl/', '材料', 'n', 'curtain material (窗帘布)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'materialize', '/mə\'tɪərɪəlaɪz/', '实现', 'v', 'Problems were expected, but they never materialized. (估计会有问题，但一直没有发生。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'matter', '/\'mætə(r)/', '重要；要紧', 'v', 'If I have to stay late at work tonight, it won’t matter because we can go out another night. (如果今晚我必须工作到很晚的话，那也没关系，我们可以改天晚上再出去。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'maturity', '/mə\'tʃʊərətɪ/', '成熟', 'n', 'Beth shows a maturity way beyond her 16 years. (贝丝表现出一种远远超出她16岁年龄的成熟。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'measure', '/ˈmeʒə(r)/', '措施', 'n', 'New safety measures were being demanded after last night’s horrific train crash. (昨晚发生严重的火车相撞事故后，民众要求制定新的安全措施。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'mechanism', '/\'mekənɪzəm/', '机制', 'n', 'the brake mechanism (刹车装置)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'melt', '/melt/', '融化', 'v', 'It was warmer now, and the snow was beginning to melt. (现在天气暖和了，雪开始融化。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'memo', '/\'meməʊ/', '备忘录', 'n', 'I sent him a memo reminding him about the meeting. (我发给他一个通知，提醒他开会的事。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'memorable', '/ˈmemərəbl/', '值得纪念的', 'adj', 'We want to make this a truly memorable day for the children. (我们想让今天成为孩子们永远难忘的日子。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'mention', '/\'menʃn/', '提及', 'v', 'Was my name mentioned at all? (我的名字被提到过吗？)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'merit', '/\'merɪt/', '值得；优点', 'v', 'The results have been encouraging enough to merit further investigation. (结果令人振奋，值得进一步调查研究。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'migrate', '/maɪ\'ɡreɪt/', '移民，迁徙', 'v', 'People migrate to cities like Jakarta in search of work. (人们移居到雅加达这样的城市找工作。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'milestone', '/\'maɪlstəʊn/', '里程碑', 'n', 'He said the launch of the party represented a milestone in Zambian history. (他说该党的成立代表着赞比亚历史上的一个里程碑。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'minimal', '/ˈmɪnɪməl/', '最低的，最小限度的', 'adj', 'The storm caused only minimal damage. (暴风雨只造成了轻微破坏。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'mining', '/ˈmaɪnɪŋ/', '矿产', 'n', '...traditional industries such as coal mining and steel making. (…像采煤和炼钢这样的传统工业。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'minor', '/\'maɪnə(r)/', '次要的，小的', 'adj', 'We have made some minor changes to the program. (我们对那个程序做了一些小改动。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'minority', '/maɪ\'nɒrətɪ/', '少数，少数民族', 'n', 'Gaelic is still spoken in Ireland by a tiny minority. (爱尔兰仍有极少数人在说盖尔语。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'miracle', '/\'mɪrəkl/', '奇迹', 'n', 'It’s a miracle you weren’t killed! (你没有死真是奇迹！)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'misfortune', '/ˌmɪsˈfɔ:tʃu:n/', '不幸地', 'n', 'It seems the banks always profit from farmers’ misfortunes. (银行似乎总是从农民的不幸中获益。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'misinterpret', '/ˌmɪsɪn\'tɜ:prɪt/', '误解', 'v', 'Some parts of the report could be misinterpreted. (报告的某些部分可能会被误解。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'mobility', '/məʊˈbɪləti/', '活动', 'n', 'It improves the strength and mobility of joints. (它能提高关节的力量和灵活性。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'modernize', '/\'mɒdənaɪz/', '现代化', 'v', 'They need more funds to modernize the country’s telephone system. (他们需要更多的资金将本国的电话系统现代化。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'moist', '/mɔɪst/', '潮湿的', 'adj', 'Make sure the soil is moist before planting the seeds. (播种之前要确保土壤湿润。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'monopoly', '/mə\'nɒpəlɪ/', '垄断', 'n', 'a monopoly in copper trading (对铜交易的垄断)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'mortality', '/mɔ:ˈtæləti/', '死亡率', 'n', 'Mortality from heart disease varies widely across the world. (心脏病死亡率世界各地差异很大。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'motel', '/məʊ\'tel/', '汽车旅馆', 'n', 'The gas station just neighbours to the motel. (加油站就在汽车旅馆的附近。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'motivation', '/ˌməʊtɪ\'veɪʃn/', '激励，刺激', 'n', NULL, 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'mount', '/maʊnt/', '增加', 'v', 'Tension here is mounting , as we await the final result. (我们等待着最终结果，这里的气氛也越来越紧张。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'mourn', '/mɔ:n/', '哀悼', 'v', 'Hundreds of people gathered to mourn the slain president. (成百上千人聚集在一起悼念遇刺的总统。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'municipal', '/mju:ˈnɪsɪpl/', '政府的', 'adj', 'the municipal waste dump (城市垃圾场)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'narrow', '/\'nærəʊ/', '变窄，缩小', 'v', 'He narrowed his eyes and gazed at the horizon. (他眯起眼睛凝望着地平线。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'necessity', '/nəˈsesəti/', '必须，必要性', 'n', 'I’m afraid it’s become a matter of economic necessity. (恐怕这已成了一个经济需求的问题。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'needy', '/\'ni:dɪ/', '贫穷的', 'adj', 'a needy family (贫困家庭)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'neglect', '/nɪ\'ɡlekt/', '忽视', 'v', 'She smoked and drank, neglected the children, and left the clothes unmended. (她抽烟喝酒，既不照顾孩子，也不缝补衣服。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'negotiation', '/nɪˌgəʊʃiˈeɪʃn/', '协商', 'n', 'The trader was obstinate in the negotiation. (这个商人在谈判中拗强固执。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'neighborhood', '/\'neɪbəhʊd/', '附近', 'n', 'What happened in the factory is being whispered about the neighborhood. (工厂里发生的事正在附近居民中私下传说。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'neutrality', '/nju:ˈtræləti/', '中立', 'n', 'Net neutrality, or not? (网络中立或不?)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'nightmare', '/ˈnaɪtmeə(r)/', '噩梦', 'n', 'a recurring nightmare  (一再出现的噩梦)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'nominate', '/\'nɒmɪneɪt/', '提名', 'v', 'This week one of them will be nominated by the Democratic Party for the presidency of the United States. (本周他们中的一人将被民主党提名为美国总统职位的候选人。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'notion', '/ˈnəuʃən/', '想法，观点', 'n', 'She had no notion what he meant. (她根本不明白他是什么意思。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'numerous', '/ˈnju:mərəs/', '无数的', 'adj', NULL, 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'nutritious', '/njuˈtrɪʃəs/', '有营养的', 'adj', 'Wholemeal bread is more nutritious than white bread. (全麦面包比白面包更有营养。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'obesity', '/əʊ\'bi:sətɪ/', '肥胖', 'n', 'So, what of the future of obesity in America? (那么，未来美国的肥胖状况会怎么发展呢？)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'objective', '/əbˈdʒektɪv/', '目标，目的', 'n', 'He vowed to achieve certain objectives before the end of his presidency. (他立誓要在他的总统任期结束之前实现某些目标。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'oblige', '/ə\'blaɪdʒ/', '迫使', 'v', 'The storm got worse and worse. Finally, I was obliged to abandon the car and continue on foot. (暴风雨越来越猛烈。最终，我被迫弃车徒步前行。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'obstacle', '/ˈɒbstəkl/', '阻碍', 'n', 'The tax puts obstacles in the way of companies trying to develop trade overseas. (这项税收为想在海外发展贸易的公司设置了障碍。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'occur', '/əˈkɜ:(r)/', '发生', 'v', 'A third of accidental deaths occur in the home. (有三分之一的意外死亡发生在家里。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'offense', '/əˈfens/', '冒犯', 'n', 'His words gave great offense to everybody present. (他的发言冲犯了在场的所有人。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'oppose', '/ə\'pəʊz/', '反对', 'v', 'Congress is continuing to oppose the President’s health care budget. (国会继续反对总统的医疗保健预算。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'opposition', '/ˌɒpəˈzɪʃn/', '反对', 'n', 'He is confident in his ability to overcome all opposition with his personal charm. (他自信有能力以个人魅力来化解一切反对力量。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'optimistic', '/ˌɒptɪˈmɪstɪk/', '乐观的', 'adj', 'Andrew took a more optimistic view. (安德鲁抱有更为乐观的想法。)', 3);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', 'CET-6', 'organic', '/ɔ:ˈgænɪk/', '有机的', 'adj', 'Organic farming is better for the environment. (有机耕作对环境更有利。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'orient', '/\'ɔ:rɪənt/', '使适应，使确定方向', 'v', 'She looked at the street names, trying to orient herself. (她看看街名，试图确定自己的方位。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'outcome', '/ˈaʊtkʌm/', '结果', 'n', 'People who had heard the evidence at the trial were surprised at the outcome. (在审判过程中听过证词的人都对此结果感到吃惊。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'outdated', '/ˌaʊtˈdeɪtɪd/', '过时的', 'adj', 'outdated teaching methods (不合时宜的教学方法)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'outlive', '/ˌaʊt\'lɪv/', '比……活的时间长', 'v', 'She outlived her husband by 20 years. (她比她丈夫多活了20年。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'outnumber', '/ˌaʊt\'nʌmbə(r)/', '超过', 'v', 'Flats outnumber houses in this area. (这个地区公寓房比独栋房子多。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'outsource', '/ˈaʊtsɔ:s/', '外包', 'v', '...companies that outsource IT functions. (…将信息技术方面的工作外包的公司。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'outweigh', '/ˌaʊt\'weɪ/', '超过', 'v', 'The advantages of this deal largely outweigh the disadvantages. (这笔交易的利远大于弊。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'overcharge', '/ˌəʊvə\'tʃɑ:dʒ/', '多收钱', 'v', 'Sometimes, they overcharge or don’t build those parts I have been paying for. (有时，他们收费过高或者要不给我修我一直在给钱的那些零部件。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'overexcited', '/ˌəʊvərɪkˈsaɪtɪd/', '过于激烈的', 'adj', 'Some of the boys became overexcited. (有些男孩变得兴奋过度了。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'overwhelm', '/ˌəʊvə\'welm/', '压倒，战胜', 'v', 'But the various pros and cons should not blindly overwhelm one another. (但是，众多的利弊得失不应盲目的一个压倒另一个。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'owe', '/əʊ/', '欠钱', 'v', 'How much do I owe you (= often used to show that you want to pay for something )? (我该付你多少钱？)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'owl', '/aʊl/', '猫头鹰', 'n', 'Some of the more extreme contacts give you "cat eyes" or how about "owl eyes"? (一些更酷的隐形眼镜可以给你一双"猫眼"或者是"猫头鹰的眼睛"。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'panic', '/\'pænɪk/', '恐慌的', 'adj', 'Her face distorted in panic. (她的脸因恐慌而变相了。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'paradise', '/\'pærədaɪs/', '天堂', 'n', 'The Koran describes paradise as a place containing a garden of delight. (《古兰经》把天堂描绘成一个拥有快乐花园的地方。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'paralyze', '/\'pærəlaɪz/', '瘫痪，麻痹', 'v', 'You can bet that would truly paralyze the flow of credit: Does anyone believe Washington can manage banks? (你可以打赌，这会使流动的信贷真正限于瘫痪：真有人相信华盛顿可以经营银行吗？)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'pasture', '/\'pɑ:stʃə(r)/', '牧场', 'n', 'large areas of rough upland pasture (大片起伏的山地牧场)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'pattern', '/\'pætn/', '模式', 'n', 'Weather patterns have changed in recent years. (气候模式近年已经发生了变化。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'pause', '/pɔ:z/', '暂停，迟疑', 'n', 'There was a pause while Alice changed the tape. (艾丽斯换磁带的时候出现了短暂的停顿。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'pave', '/peɪv/', '铺路', 'v', 'a paved courtyard (地面铺砌过的院子)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'payroll', '/ˈpeɪrəʊl/', '工资总额', 'n', 'the annual payroll was $88 million (年度工资总支出为8,800万美元)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'peculiar', '/pɪ\'kju:lɪə(r)/', '特有的，奇怪的', 'adj', 'There was a peculiar smell in the kitchen. (厨房里有一股怪味。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'penalty', '/\'penəltɪ/', '惩罚', 'n', 'No littering. Penalty $500. (禁止乱扔垃圾。 违者罚款500美元。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'pension', '/\'penʃn/', '养老金', 'n', 'At what age can you start drawing your pension ? (从多少岁可以开始领取养老金？)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'perish', '/\'perɪʃ/', '死亡', 'v', 'Hundreds perished when the ship went down. (轮船沉没，数百人罹难。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'perspective', '/pə\'spektɪv/', '视角，观点', 'n', 'the artist’s use of perspective (那位画家对透视法的运用)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'pessimist', '/ˈpesɪmɪst/', '悲观主义者', 'n', 'Don’t be such a pessimist! (别这么悲观！)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'phenomenon', '/fə\'nɒmɪnən/', '现象', 'n', 'Homelessness is not a new phenomenon . (无家可归已不是什么新现象。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'philosopher', '/fəˈlɒsəfə(r)/', '哲学家', 'n', 'Plato, Aristotle, and other Greek philosophers (柏拉图、亚里士多德和其他希腊哲学家)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'plot', '/plɒt/', '情节', 'n', 'The plot was a little confusing. (情节有些费解。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'poetry', '/\'pəʊətrɪ/', '诗歌', 'n', 'He reads a lot of poetry. (他大量阅读诗歌。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'polar', '/ˈpəʊlə(r)/', '（南、北）极', 'n', 'Well, what is the equation of this circle in polar coordinates? (那么，这个圆方程在极坐标系下相当于什么呢？)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'poll', '/pəʊl/', '民意测验', 'n', 'A recent poll found that 80% of Californians support the governor. (最近的一项民意调查发现80%的加利福尼亚人支持州长。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'ponder', '/\'pɒndə(r)/', '仔细考虑', 'v', 'He continued to ponder the problem as he walked home. (他一边往家走一边继续思考那个问题。)', 4),
