('en', 'CET-6', 'impart', '/ɪmˈpɑːt/', '传授，教授', 'v', 'She had information that she couldn’t wait to impart. (她得到了消息，迫不及待地想告诉别人。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'provoke', '/prəˈvəʊk/', '激怒', 'v', 'The novel has provoked fierce debate in the US. (那部小说在美国引发了激烈的争论。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'assumption', '/əˈsʌmpʃn/', '假设', 'n', 'You would be making an assumption that\'s not based on any fact that you could report. (你会做出不以你能报道的任何事实为依据的一种假设。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'formula', '/\'fɔːmjʊlə/', '公式', 'n', 'the formula for calculating distance (计算距离的公式)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'overlap', '/ˌəʊvəˈlæp/', '重叠', 'v', 'When the bag is folded, the bottom overlaps one side. (把包折叠起来时，其底部与一边就重合了。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'thrive', '/θraɪv/', '繁荣，兴旺', 'v', 'plants that thrive in tropical rain forests (在热带雨林蓬勃生长的植物)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'chronic', '/ˈkrɒnɪk/', '长期的；慢性的', 'adj', 'chronic arthritis (慢性关节炎)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'adversity', '/ədˈvɜːsəti/', '逆境', 'n', 'his courage in the face of adversity (他面对逆境的勇气)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'endure', '/ɪnˈdjʊə(r)/', '忍受', 'v', 'It seemed impossible that anyone could endure such pain. (似乎谁都不可能忍受这样的疼痛。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'assert', '/əˈsɜːt/', '主张，断言', 'v', 'French cooking, she asserted, is the best in the world. (她坚称法国菜是世界上最好的。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'chew', '/tʃuː/', '咀嚼；深思', 'v', 'This meat’s so tough I can hardly chew it! (这肉太老了，我几乎嚼不动！)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'tradeoff', '/ˈtreɪdˌɒf/', '权衡，交易', 'n', 'However, these elements of risk can be mitigated by spending more effort developing the queries; as with many development options, there is a tradeoff between query complexity and query stability. (但是，可以多花些精力来开发查询，从而减轻这些风险元素；正如许多开发选择一样，在查询的复杂性与查询的稳定性之间会有一个权衡。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'commentator', '/ˈkɒmənteɪtə(r)/', '评论员', 'n', 'political commentators (政治评论员)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'vice', '/vaɪs/', '恶意，恶习', 'n', 'Smoking is my only vice. (吸烟是我唯一的恶习。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'attribute', '/əˈtrɪbjuːt/', '归因于', 'v', 'Women tend to attribute their success to external causes such as luck. (女性往往把她们的成功归因于外因，如运气。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'vivid', '/ˈvɪvɪd/', '生动的', 'adj', 'I’ve got vivid memories of that summer. (我对那年夏天记忆犹新。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'upgrade', '/ˈʌpɡreɪd/', '升级', 'v', 'Helicopters have been upgraded and modernized. (直升机已经升级并且装上现代化设备。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'prospective', '/prəˈspektɪv/', '未来的，预期的', 'adj', 'The story should act as a warning to other prospective buyers. (这篇报道应该可以对其他可能的购买者起到警告作用。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'regime', '/reɪˈʒiːm/', '制度，管理体制', 'n', 'The authorities moved him to the less rigid regime of an open prison. (当局把他移送到管理相对宽松的不设防监狱。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'appeal', '/əˈpiːl/', '请求，呼吁, 上诉', 'n', 'The girl’s family have made a public appeal for help to try and catch her killer. (那名遇害女孩的家人吁请公众协助捉拿凶手。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'weave', '/wiːv/', '织布，编织', 'v', 'hand-woven scarves (手织围巾)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'sew', '/səʊ/', '缝上，缝纫', 'v', 'I learned to sew at school. (我在学校学会了缝纫。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'nap', '/næp/', '小睡', 'n', 'an afternoon nap (午睡)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'row', '/rəʊ/', '划船', 'v', 'Jenny used to row at college (= as a sport ) . (珍妮以前在大学里经常参加划船运动。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'helicopter', '/ˈhelɪkɒptə(r)/', '直升飞机', 'n', 'You can helicopter to the island. (你可以乘坐直升机去那个岛。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'conquer', '/ˈkɒŋkə(r)/', '征服', 'v', 'The Normans conquered England in 1066. (诺曼人于 1066 年征服英格兰。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'memorandum', '/ˌmeməˈrændəm/', '备忘录', 'n', '...a memorandum from the Department of Defense on its role. (…一份来自国防部的有关其角色的备忘录。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'clarity', '/ˈklærəti/', '清晰，清楚', 'n', 'Letters may be edited for length and clarity. (信件可能要加以修改以求篇幅合适，意思明了。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'carpenter', '/ˈkɑːpəntə(r)/', '木匠', 'n', 'He is a carpenter by profession. (他以木工为业。)', 3);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', 'CET-6', 'drummer', '/ˈdrʌmə(r)/', '鼓手', 'n', 'He was a drummer in a rock band. (他是一支摇滚乐队的鼓手。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'discrimination', '/dɪˌskrɪmɪˈneɪʃn/', '歧视', 'n', 'laws to prevent discrimination (防止歧视的法律)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'uninformed', '/ˌʌnɪnˈfɔːmd/', '无知的，未受过教育的', 'adj', 'Parents were left anxious, uninformed, and isolated. (家长们忧心忡忡，不知道情况到底如何，感到孤立无援。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'entitle', '/ɪnˈtaɪtl/', '使具有资格', 'v', 'If the warranty is limited, the terms may entitle you to a replacement or refund. (如果保修单有限制，这些条款可让你有权换货或退款。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'imitate', '/ˈɪmɪteɪt/', '模仿', 'v', 'She was a splendid mimic and loved to imitate Winston Churchill. (她是个出色的模仿者，喜欢模仿温斯顿·丘吉尔。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'subordinate', '/səˈbɔːdɪnət/', '次要的，从属的', 'adj', 'a subordinate officer (下级官员)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'suppress', '/səˈpres/', '镇压，压制', 'v', 'The uprising was ruthlessly suppressed. (起义受到了残酷的镇压。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'throne', '/θrəʊn/', '王位', 'n', 'He is next in line to the throne (= will become king when the present ruler dies ) . (他是第一王位继承人。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'athletics', '/æθˈletɪks/', '体育运动', 'n', '...students who play intercollegiate athletics. (…参加大学校际体育运动的学生们。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'coach', '/kəʊtʃ/', '教练', 'n', 'a tennis coach (网球教练)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'biodiversity', '/ˌbaɪəʊdaɪˈvɜːsəti/', '生物多样性', 'n', 'the biodiversity of the rainforest (热带雨林中的生物多样性)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'accommodate', '/əˈkɒmədeɪt/', '适应，容纳', 'v', 'He bought a huge house to accommodate his library. (他买了一座大房子来放他的藏书。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'ultimate', '/ˈʌltɪmət/', '最终的', 'adj', 'The ultimate outcome of the experiment cannot be predicted. (试验的最后结果无法预测。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'invasive', '/ɪnˈveɪsɪv/', '入侵的', 'adj', 'invasive bladder cancers (扩散性膀胱癌)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'underscore', '/ˌʌndəˈskɔː(r)/', '强调', 'v', 'The Labour Department figures underscore the shaky state of the economic recovery. (劳工部的数字突出显示了经济复苏的不稳定。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'ongoing', '/ˈɒnɡəʊɪŋ/', '持续的，不间断的', 'adj', 'their ongoing search for a new director (他们仍在寻找一个新主任)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'greedy', '/ˈɡriːdi/', '贪婪的', 'adj', 'a greedy and selfish society (一个贪婪自私的社会)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'lessen', '/ˈlesn/', '减少', 'v', 'Gradually her anxiety lessened. (她的焦虑慢慢减轻了。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'incur', '/ɪnˈkɜː(r)/', '引起，导致', 'v', 'And operational downtime caused by reliability or performance problems can incur opportunity costs if customers are unable to access your system or the business is unable to do its work. (并且如果顾客不能访问你的系统或业务不能进行工作，那么由可靠性或性能问题引起的运作停工就会招致机会成本。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'integral', '/ˈɪntɪɡrəl/', '完整的', 'adj', 'Rituals, celebrations, and festivals form an integral part of every human society. (仪式、庆典和节日是每个人类社会不可缺少的组成部分。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'merge', '/mɜːdʒ/', '合并', 'v', 'The company plans to merge its subsidiaries in the US. (该公司计划合并其在美国的几家子公司。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'unintentionally', '/ˌʌnɪnˈtenʃənəli/', '无意地', 'adv', 'I brushed up against him unintentionally. (我无意中碰了他一下。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'grave', '/ɡreɪv/', '严重的', 'adj', 'Matthew’s life is in grave danger . (马修的生命危在旦夕。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'intimate', '/ˈɪntɪmət/', '亲密的', 'adj', 'an intimate friend of Picasso’s (毕加索的一个密友)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'alleviate', '/əˈliːvieɪt/', '减轻，缓解', 'v', 'measures to alleviate poverty (扶贫措施)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'conspicuous', '/kənˈspɪkjuəs/', '显著的', 'adj', 'The notice must be displayed in a conspicuous place. (通告一定要贴在显眼的地方。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'territory', '/ˈterətri/', '领域，领土', 'n', 'Hong Kong is a Chinese territory. (香港是中国的领土。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'displace', '/dɪsˈpleɪs/', '取代', 'v', 'Coal has been displaced by natural gas as a major source of energy. (作为一种主要能源，煤的地位已为天然气所取代。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'regardless', '/rɪˈɡɑːdləs/', '不管，不顾', 'adj', 'The fields give high and stable yields regardless of climatic circumstances. (不管天气条件如何， 这块地总是保持稳产高产。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'duplication', '/ˌdjuːplɪˈkeɪʃn/', '复制品', 'n', 'There could be a serious loss of efficiency through unnecessary duplication of resources. (不必要的资源重复会导致严重的效率损耗。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'overturn', '/ˌəʊvəˈtɜːn/', '推翻', 'v', 'Leslie jumped to her feet, overturning her chair. (莱斯莉一跃而起，碰倒了椅子。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'identical', '/aɪˈdentɪkl/', '相同的', 'adj', 'four identical houses (四幢一模一样的房子)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'miniature', '/ˈmɪnətʃə(r)/', '微型的', 'adj', 'miniature roses (微型玫瑰)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'tempting', '/ˈtemptɪŋ/', '吸引人的', 'adj', 'a tempting job offer (一个诱人的工作机会)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'segregation', '/ˌseɡrɪˈɡeɪʃn/', '隔离', 'n', 'The Supreme Court unanimously ruled that racial segregation in schools was unconstitutional. (最高法院一致裁定学校实施的种族隔离措施违反宪法。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'variance', '/ˈveəriəns/', '不同', 'n', 'a price variance of 5% (5%的价格差异)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'inaction', '/ɪnˈækʃn/', '不作为', 'n', 'He is bitter about the inaction of the other political parties. (他为其他政党的不作为感到愤愤不平。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'conserve', '/kənˈsɜːv/', '保留，保护', 'v', 'We must conserve our woodlands for future generations. (我们必须为子孙后代保护林地。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'renewable', '/rɪˈnjuːəbl/', '可再生的', 'adj', 'It’s a six-month lease but it’s renewable. (租期六个月，但是可以续签。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'embrace', '/ɪmˈbreɪs/', '采纳，接受', 'v', 'We hope these regions will embrace democratic reforms. (我们希望这些地区会乐意接受民主改革。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'counterpart', '/ˈkaʊntəpɑːt/', '对等物', 'n', 'As soon as he heard what was afoot, he telephoned his German and Italian counterparts to protest. (他一听到在进行中的事，马上就给德国和意大利相应人员打电话抗议。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'rival', '/ˈraɪvl/', '对手', 'n', 'This gives the company a competitive advantage over its rivals. (这使该公司与其对手相比具有一项竞争优势。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'intense', '/ɪnˈtens/', '激烈的，强烈的', 'adj', 'Young people today are under intense pressure to succeed. (如今的年轻人面临要出人头地的巨大压力。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'aspirational', '/ˌæspəˈreɪʃənl/', '渴望的', 'adj', 'aspirational young women (有抱负的年轻女性)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'transform', '/trænsˈfɔːm/', '转变', 'v', 'Increased population has transformed the landscape. (人口的增加使景观发生了变化。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'grip', '/ɡrɪp/', '抓住', 'n', 'Hold the microphone in a firm grip and keep it still. (紧紧握住麦克风不要让它动。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'unfold', '/ʌnˈfəʊld/', '展开', 'v', 'As the story unfolds, we learn more about Max’s childhood. (随着故事的展开，我们对马克斯的童年有了更多的了解。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'ideological', '/ˌaɪdiəˈlɒdʒɪkl/', '意识形态的', 'adj', 'The party is split by ideological differences. (意识形态上的差异造成该政党分裂。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'filter', '/ˈfɪltə(r)/', '过滤', 'v', 'The water in the tank is constantly filtered. (鱼缸里的水在不停地被过滤。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'pronoun', '/ˈprəʊnaʊn/', '代词', 'n', 'Now if we could only figure out the pronoun problem. (现在我们可以解决这个代词问题了。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'philosophy', '/fəˈlɒsəfi/', '哲学', 'n', 'Emma studies philosophy at university. (埃玛在大学攻读哲学。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'illuminate', '/ɪˈluːmɪneɪt/', '阐释，阐明', 'v', 'The report illuminated the difficult issues at the heart of science policy. (报告阐明了科学方针核心部分的难点。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'odds', '/ɒdz/', '可能性', 'n', '(= it is likely ) that he will commit the same crime again. (他可能还会犯同样的罪行。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'confess', '/kənˈfes/', '承认', 'v', 'Occasionally people confess to crimes they haven’t committed just to get attention. (偶尔人们会承认自己并未犯过的罪行，那只是为了引人注意。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'manipulate', '/məˈnɪpjuleɪt/', '操纵', 'v', 'He was one of those men who manipulated people. (他是那种要摆布别人的人。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'rhythm', '/ˈrɪðəm/', '节奏', 'n', 'Drums are basic to African rhythm. (非洲音乐节奏少不了鼓。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'hijack', '/ˈhaɪˌdʒæk/', '劫持', 'v', 'The airliner was hijacked by a group of terrorists. (该航班被一帮恐怖分子劫持。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'sweep', '/swi:p/', '扫除，清除', 'v', 'Bert swept the path in front of the house. (伯特清扫了屋前的小路。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'withdraw', '/wɪð\'drɔ/', '撤销，撤退', 'v', 'calls for Britain to withdraw from the European Union (要求英国退出欧盟的呼声)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'flame', '/fleim/', '火焰', 'n', 'Flames poured out of the windows of the building. (火焰从大楼窗口冒出来。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'spark', '/spɑrk/', '火花', 'n', 'sparks from the fire (火里飞出的火星)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'feasibility', '/,fizə\'bɪləti/', '可行', 'n', 'But this is only at an early stage of feasibility study. (但是这仅仅处于可行性研究的初期阶段。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'fascinate', '/\'fæsɪneɪt/', '使着迷', 'v', 'Politics fascinated Franklin\'s father. (政治让富兰克林的父亲着迷。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'crew', '/krʊ/', '机组人员', 'n', 'The plane crashed, killing two of the crew and four passengers. (飞机坠毁，造成两名机组人员和四名乘客死亡。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'cumulative', '/\'kjumjəletɪv/', '积累的', 'adj', 'Learning is a cumulative process. (学习是个逐渐积累的过程。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'awkward', '/\'ɔːkwəd/', '尴尬的，棘手的，笨拙的', 'adj', 'I hoped he would stop asking awkward questions . (我希望他不要再问令人难堪的问题。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'obscurity', '/əb\'skjʊrəti/', '默默无闻', 'n', 'Now, on the eve of the bicentenary of the independence movements, he sets out to rescue San Martín from his relative obscurity. (今天，在那场独立运动二百周年纪念前夕，他再度出手以挽救相对默默无闻的圣·马丁。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'badge', '/bædʒ/', '标记, 徽章', 'n', 'We were each handed a badge with our name on it. (我们每个人都拿到一个徽章，上面有我们的名字。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'distinction', '/dɪ\'stɪŋkʃən/', '区分', 'n', 'There are obvious distinctions between the two wine-making areas. (这两个酿酒区之间有明显的不同。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'formulate', '/\'fɔːmjʊleɪt/', '制定，规划', 'v', 'By visualizing where you want to be, you start helping your mind formulate ways to achieve that next goal in your life. (通过把你想达到的程度形象化，你就开始帮助自己的头脑制定目标——为了达到你生活中的下一个目标。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'monetary', '/\'mʌnɪt(ə)rɪ/', '货币的', 'adj', 'the government’s tight monetary policy (政府从紧的货币政策)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'portray', '/pɔr\'trei/', '描述', 'v', 'Romantic artists portrayed nature as wild and powerful. (浪漫主义艺术家描绘的大自然是狂野而强大的。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'hostility', '/hɒ\'stɪlɪtɪ/', '敌意', 'n', 'The last decade has witnessed a serious rise in the levels of racism and hostility to black and ethnic groups. (过去的10年里，种族主义及对黑人和少数民族的敌意变得更加严重了。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'robust', '/rə(ʊ)\'bʌst/', '强健的', 'adj', 'a robust man of six feet four (一个身高六英尺四英寸的壮汉)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'appropriation', '/ə,prəʊprɪ\'eɪʃ(ə)n/', '挪用', 'n', 'Other charges include fraud and illegal appropriation of land. (其他指控包括诈骗和非法占用土地。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'deforestation', '/,di,fɔrɪ\'steʃən/', '砍伐森林', 'n', 'the deforestation of the tropics (热带森林的毁坏)', 3),
