('en', 'CET-6', 'calculus', '/\'kælkjʊləs/', '微积分；结石', 'n', 'We have to factor that into the calculus. (我们要在微积分学中考虑这些因素。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'gleam', '/gliːm/', '微光；发微光', 'n', 'They saw a sudden gleam of light. (他们看到一道微光一闪而过。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'negligible', '/\'neglɪdʒɪb(ə)l/', '微不足道的', 'adj', 'The damage done to his property was negligible. (对他财产造成的损失微不足道。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'microwave', '/\'maɪkrə(ʊ)weɪv/', '微波', 'n', 'Its molecules can be agitated by microwave energy. (微波能量可以使其分子随之运动。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'awful', '/\'ɔːfʊl/', '威严的；令人崇敬的', 'adj', NULL, 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'majesty', '/\'mædʒɪstɪ/', '雄伟，威严，庄严；陛下', 'n', 'the sheer majesty of St Peter\'s in Rome (罗马圣彼得大教堂的雄伟庄严)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'prestige', '/pre\'stiː(d)ʒ/', '威望，威信，声望', 'n', 'The king wanted to enhance his prestige through war. (国王想通过战争来提高自己的威信。)', 3);
