('en', 'CET-6', 'mercury', NULL, '汞，水银', 'n', 'Mercury is used in batteries, pesticides, and thermometers. (水银用于电池、杀虫剂与温度计中。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'consolidate', '/kən\'sɒlɪdeɪt/', '巩固；合并', 'v', 'The company has consolidated its position as the country’s leading gas supplier. (这家公司巩固了作为该国主要煤气供应商的地位。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'impartial', '/ɪm\'pɑːʃ(ə)l/', '公正的，无偏见的', 'adj', 'We offer impartial advice on tax and insurance. (我们就税收和保险问题提供公充的建议。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'convention', '/kən\'venʃ(ə)n/', '公约，（换俘等）协定', 'n', '...the U.N. convention on climate change. (…关于气候变化的联合国公约。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'duke', '/djuːk/', '公爵；君主', 'n', 'the Duke of Edinburgh (爱丁堡公爵)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'rooster', '/\'ruːstə/', '公鸡', 'n', 'I heard a rooster crow. (我听见雄鸡啼叫。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'studio', '/\'stjuːdɪəʊ/', '播音室；工作室', 'n', 'a recording studio in Nashville (在纳什维尔的一间录音室)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'earnings', '/\'ɜːnɪŋz/', '工资，收入；收益', 'n', 'an employee’s average weekly earnings (雇员的平均周薪)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'implement', '/\'ɪmplɪm(ə)nt/', '工具；贯彻', 'n', '...writing implements. (…书写用具。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'workpiece', NULL, '工（作）件', 'n', 'The workpiece is already on the lathe. (工件已经上了车床。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'combat', '/\'kɒmbæt; \'kʌm-/', '跟…战斗，格斗', 'v', 'to combat crime/terrorism/inflation/disease (打击犯罪／打击恐怖主义／抑制通货膨胀／与疾病作斗争)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'impart', '/ɪm\'pɑːt/', '给予；传递；告诉', 'v', 'Use a piece of fresh ginger to impart a East Asian flavour to simple ingredients. (用一片鲜姜给简单的原料添上东亚的风味。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'energize', '/\'enədʒaɪz/', '供给…能量', 'v', NULL, 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'vaccinate', '/\'væksɪneɪt/', '给…接种疫苗', 'v', 'All children should be vaccinated against measles. (所有儿童都应该接种麻疹疫苗。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'flavour', '/\'fleɪvə/', '给…调味', 'v', 'Lime preserved in salt is a North African speciality which is used to flavour chicken dishes. (用盐腌的酸橙是用来给鸡肉调味的一种北非特产。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'insulator', '/\'ɪnsjʊleɪtə/', '隔离者；绝缘体', 'n', 'Wood is an excellent insulator. (木材是很好的绝缘体。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'lattice', '/\'lætɪs/', '格子结构', 'n', 'We were crawling along the narrow steel lattice of the bridge. (我们沿着大桥窄窄的钢制格子爬行着。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'dove', '/dʌv/', '鸽子，斑鸠', 'n', 'A dove cooed softly. (一只鸽子轻柔地咕咕叫。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'reveal', '/rɪ\'viːl/', '告诉，揭示，泄露', 'v', 'He may be prosecuted for revealing secrets about the security agency. (他可能因泄露安全部门的机密而被起诉。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'plateau', '/\'plætəʊ/', '高原；平稳时期', 'n', 'A broad valley opened up leading to a high, flat plateau of cultivated land. (一个宽阔的山谷展开，通向一片平坦的高原耕地。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'lofty', '/\'lɒftɪ/', '高耸的；高尚的', 'adj', 'He stayed at the Four Seasons Hotel, from whose lofty heights he could see across New York. (他住在四季酒店，从酒店高处可以看到纽约的全景。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'tower', '/\'taʊə/', '高耸，屹立；翱翔', 'v', 'The cliffs towered above them. (悬崖峭壁高耸于他们上方。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'elevation', '/,elɪ\'veɪʃ(ə)n/', '高度，海拔', 'n', 'The city is at an elevation of 2 000 metres. (这座城市海拔2000米。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'intervene', '/ɪntə\'viːn/', '干涉，干预', 'v', 'The army will have to intervene to prevent further fighting. (军队将不得不干预以阻止进一步的战斗。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'dry', '/draɪ/', '干巴巴的，枯燥的', 'adj', 'Government reports tend to make dry reading. (政府报告读起来往往枯燥无味。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'olive', '/\'ɒlɪv/', '橄榄；橄榄树', 'n', '...a pile of black olives. (…一堆黑橄榄。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'sentiment', '/\'sentɪm(ə)nt/', '感情；情绪', 'n', 'the spread of nationalist sentiments (民族主义情绪的传播)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'perception', '/pə\'sepʃ(ə)n/', '感知；理解力', 'n', 'our perception of reality (我们对现实的认识)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'sensation', '/sen\'seɪʃ(ə)n/', '感觉，知觉；轰动', 'n', 'One sign of a heart attack is a tingling sensation in the left arm. (心脏病发作的一个征兆是左臂有刺痛感。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'Thanksgiving', NULL, '感恩节', 'n', 'We always eat turkey on Thanksgiving. (我们过感恩节时总是吃火鸡。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'chill', '/tʃɪl/', '感到寒冷；冷藏', 'v', 'The wind blew across her body, chilling her wet skin. (风吹在她身上，她湿漉漉的皮肤感到非常寒冷。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'outline', '/\'aʊtlaɪn/', '概述，概括', 'v', 'The new president outlined plans to deal with crime, drugs, and education. (新总统概述了解决犯罪、毒品和教育问题的计划。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'notion', '/\'nəʊʃ(ə)n/', '概念；看法', 'n', 'She had no notion what he meant. (她根本不明白他是什么意思。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'conception', '/kən\'sepʃ(ə)n/', '概念，观念，想法', 'n', 'the conception of parliamentary democracy (议会民主的概念)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'summary', '/\'sʌm(ə)rɪ/', '概括的；速决的', 'adj', 'a summary financial statement (财务汇总报表)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'generalize', '/ˈdʒɛnrəˌlaɪz/', '概括出', 'v', 'She has a tendency to generalize from her husband to all men. (她总爱把自己对丈夫的看法推及所有的男人。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'impress', '/ɪm\'pres/', '盖印，在…打记号', 'v', 'patterns impressed in the clay (压印在黏土上的图案)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'mend', '/mend/', '修理；改正', 'v', 'Could you mend my bike for me? (你能帮我修一下自行车吗？)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'duplicate', '/ˈdjuːplɪkeɪt/', '复制品；复制', 'n', 'She kept both the duplicate and the original. (她把复制本和原本都保留着。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'complication', '/kɒmplɪ\'keɪʃ(ə)n/', '复杂，混乱；并发症', 'n', 'The fact that the plane was late added a further complication to our journey. (飞机误点给我们的旅行带来了更大的麻烦。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'complexity', '/kəm\'pleksətɪ/', '复杂（性）', 'n', 'a design of great complexity (一项非常复杂的设计)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'satellite', '/\'sætəlaɪt/', '附属国', 'n', 'a satellite country (卫星国)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'appendix', '/ə\'pendɪks/', '附录；阑尾', 'n', 'See Appendix 2.6. (见附录2.6。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'extra', '/\'ekstrə/', '附加物；额外的东西', 'n', 'I earn extra for working on Sunday. (我星期天工作挣外快。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'incidentally', '/ɪnsɪ\'dent(ə)lɪ/', '附带地；顺便提及', 'adv', 'Incidentally, where were you born? (顺便问一下，你在哪儿出生的？)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'charge', '/tʃɑːdʒ/', '负荷；充电；装满', 'n', 'Leave the battery on charge all night. (让电池充一晚上的电)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'negative', '/\'negətɪv/', '负的；（结果）阴性的', 'adj', 'a negative trade balance (贸易逆差)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'corrosion', '/kə\'rəʊʒ(ə)n/', '腐蚀，侵蚀；锈', 'n', 'They are sprayed with oil to prevent corrosion. (它们被喷了油以防腐蚀。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'erosion', '/ɪ\'rəʊʒ(ə)n/', '腐蚀，侵蚀；糜烂', 'n', 'the problem of soil erosion (水土流失的问题)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'subsidiary', '/səb\'sɪdɪərɪ/', '辅助的，补充的', 'adj', 'The marketing department has always played a subsidiary role to the sales department. (营销部一直都扮演着销售部的辅助角色。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'coach', '/kəʊtʃ/', '指导，训练；辅导', 'v', 'Nigel coaches a cricket team in his spare time. (奈杰尔业余时间担任一个板球队的教练。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'answer', '/\'ɑːnsə/', '符合，适合', 'v', 'Does this answer your requirements? (这个符合你的要求吗？)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'emerge', '/ɪ\'mɜːdʒ/', '浮现，出现；显露', 'v', 'The flowers emerge in the spring. (花儿在春天开放。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'obedient', '/ə\'biːdɪənt/', '服从的，顺从的', 'adj', 'an obedient child (听话的孩子)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'obedience', '/ə\'biːdɪəns/', '服从，顺从', 'n', 'obedience classes for dogs and their owners (为狗和主人安排的服从训练课)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'maintenance', '/\'meɪnt(ə)nəns; -tɪn-/', '扶养费；维持', 'n', 'They have to find the fathers who abandon their children and make them pay maintenance. (他们必须找到那些抛弃子女的父亲，让他们支付抚养费。)', 2);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', 'CET-6', 'veto', '/\'viːtəʊ/', '否决，否决权；禁止', 'n', 'The Senate had a sufficient majority to override the presidential veto (= not accept his refusal ). (参议院有足够的多数票可以推翻总统的否决。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'denial', '/dɪ\'naɪ(ə)l/', '否定；拒绝相信', 'n', 'The government issued an official denial of the rumour. (政府发表了正式声明，否认谣言。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'Buddhism', '/\'bʊdɪz(ə)m/', '佛教，释教', 'n', 'Mr White has converted to Buddhism. (怀特先生已改信佛教。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'dedicate', '/\'dedɪkeɪt/', '奉献；献身', 'v', 'The actress now dedicates herself to children’s charity work. (这名女演员现在致力于儿童慈善工作。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'flatter', '/\'flætə/', '奉承，阿谀，谄媚', 'v', 'Perry would always flatter Mrs. Mitchell by praising her cooking. (佩里常常奉承米切尔太太，称赞她的烹调手艺。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'pineapple', '/\'paɪnæp(ə)l/', '凤梨，波萝', 'n', 'pineapple chunks (菠萝块)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'seam', '/siːm/', '缝口；接缝；骨缝', 'n', 'She was repairing Billy’s trousers, where the seam had come undone. (她在补比利裤子的开线处。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'landscape', '/\'læn(d)skeɪp/', '风景，景色，景致', 'n', 'the beauty of the New England landscape (新英格兰风光之美)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'windmill', '/\'wɪn(d)mɪl/', '风车', 'n', 'The sails of the windmill are now at rest. (风车的帆叶现在静止不动了。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'plump', '/plʌmp/', '丰满的', 'adj', 'The nurse was a cheerful plump woman. (那护士是个性格开朗、体形丰满的女人。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'abundance', '/ə\'bʌnd(ə)ns/', '丰富，充裕', 'n', 'an abundance of wavy red hair (浓密的红色鬈发)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'indignation', '/ɪndɪg\'neɪʃ(ə)n/', '愤怒，愤慨，义愤', 'n', 'To his indignation, Charles found that his name was not on the list. (查尔斯发现他的名字没有出现在名单上，这让他深感愤慨。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'shatter', '/\'ʃætə/', '粉碎，破碎；毁坏', 'v', 'The explosion shattered the building. (这次爆炸把大楼炸成一片废墟。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'molecular', '/mə\'lekjʊlə/', '分子的；克分子的', 'adj', '...the molecular structure of fuel. (…燃料的分子结构。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'limb', '/lɪm/', '肢；手臂；腿', 'n', 'an artificial limb (假肢)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'offset', '/\'ɒfset/', '抵销', 'v', 'He was able to offset his travel expenses against tax. (他可以用旅费抵税。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'fraction', '/\'frækʃ(ə)n/', '分数', 'n', 'The students had a grasp of decimals, percentages and fractions. (学生们掌握了小数、百分数和分数。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'distract', '/dɪ\'strækt/', '分散（心思）；打扰', 'v', 'Try not to distract the other students. (尽量不要让其他学生分心。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'installment', '/ɪn\'stɔ:lmənt/', '分期付款', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'split', '/splɪt/', '分裂，分化，派系', 'n', 'The argument could lead to a damaging split in the party. (这场争吵可能会导致党内出现分裂，对该党产生不利影响。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'detach', '/dɪ\'tætʃ/', '分开；派遣（军队）', 'v', 'Please detach and fill out the application form. (请撕下申请表并填好。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'partition', '/pɑː\'tɪʃ(ə)n/', '分开，分割；隔墙', 'n', 'the partition of Germany after the war (战后对德国的分割)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'interface', '/\'ɪntəfeɪs/', '分界面', 'n', '...the development of better user interfaces. (…更好用户界面的开发。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'relay', '/\'riːleɪ/', '分程传递；使接替；转播', 'v', 'He quickly relayed this news to the other members of staff. (他马上就把这个消息转告给了其他员工。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'diverge', '/daɪ\'vɜːdʒ; dɪ-/', '分岔；分歧', 'v', 'The parallel lines appear to diverge. (这些平行线像是岔开了。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'litter', '/\'lɪtə/', '废物；杂乱；乱扔', 'n', 'People who drop litter can be fined in some cities. (在有些城市，乱扔垃圾的人会被罚款。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'abolish', '/ə\'bɒlɪʃ/', '废除，取消', 'v', 'Slavery was abolished in the US in the 19th century. (美国于19世纪废除了奴隶制。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'gangster', '/\'gæŋstə/', '匪徒，歹徒，暴徒', 'n', '...a gangster film. (…一部黑帮片。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'extraordinarily', '/ɪk\'strɔːd(ə)n(ə)rəlɪ/', '非常地，特别地', 'adv', 'We were extraordinarily lucky. (我们极其幸运。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'fly', '/flaɪ/', '飞跑；逃跑，消失', 'v', 'Ellen flew across the room and greeted her uncle with a kiss. (埃伦从房间那头飞奔过来，给了她叔叔一个吻。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'aviation', '/eɪvɪ\'eɪʃ(ə)n/', '飞行（术）', 'n', '...the aviation industry. (…航空工业。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'indulge', '/ɪn\'dʌldʒ/', '放纵（感情），纵情', 'v', 'He returned to Britain so that he could indulge his passion for football... (他重返英国，为的是可以尽情释放自己对足球的激情。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'herd', '/hɜːd/', '成群；放牧', 'v', 'The prisoners were herded together. (犯人们被集合起来。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'magnify', '/\'mægnɪfaɪ/', '放大，扩大', 'v', 'At the Sheffield arena, the speakers were magnified ten times on a giant screen. (在谢菲尔德体育馆，演讲者在一个巨大的屏幕上被放大了十倍。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'imitation', '/ɪmɪ\'teɪʃ(ə)n/', '仿制品，伪制物', 'n', 'She wore an imitation of a sailor’s hat. (她戴着一顶仿制的水手帽。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'pattern', '/\'pæt(ə)n/', '仿制，仿造，模仿', 'v', 'The exam system is patterned after the one used in Japan. (这种考试制度是仿效日本建立的。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'reproduce', '/riːprə\'djuːs/', '仿造', 'v', 'The effect has proved hard to reproduce. (这种效果经证实很难再造。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'estate', '/ɪ\'steɪt; e-/', '财产，产业；房地产', 'n', 'The property is part of the deceased’s estate. (该产业是死者遗产的一部分。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'hamper', '/\'hæmpə/', '妨碍，阻碍，牵制', 'v', 'She tried to run, but was hampered by her heavy suitcase. (她想跑，但沉重的旅行箱拖累了她。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'handicap', '/\'hændɪkæp/', '妨碍，使不利', 'v', 'The charity is handicapped by lack of funds. (这个慈善机构因为缺乏资金难以开展工作。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'handy', '/\'hændɪ/', '方便的；便于使用的', 'adj', 'a handy little tool (好用的小工具)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'offence', '/ə\'fens/', '犯罪，犯规；冒犯', 'n', 'His solicitor said he committed the offence because he was heavily in debt. (他的律师说他犯罪是因为欠下巨债。)', 2),
('en', 'CET-6', 'blunder', '/\'blʌndə/', '犯大错；大错', 'v', 'They blundered badly when they gave him the job. (他们犯了大错，让他做这份工作。)', 4),
('en', 'CET-6', 'mirror', '/\'mɪrə/', '反映，借鉴', 'n', 'We believe the polls are an accurate mirror of public opinion. (我们相信民意测验是准确反映公众意见的一面镜子。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'reactor', '/rɪ\'æktə/', '反应堆', 'n', 'They shut down the nuclear reactor for safety reasons. (出于安全原因他们关闭了核反应堆。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'echo', '/\'ekəʊ/', '回响', 'v', 'The sound of an engine echoed back from the thick forest. (从茂密的森林里传来引擎的回声。)', 3),
('en', 'CET-6', 'contrary', '/\'kɒntrərɪ/', '反对命题', 'n', NULL, 3),
