('en', '托福', 'precious', '/\'preʃəs/', '宝贵的,珍爱的', 'adj', 'planes delivering precious supplies of medicine and food (运送药品、食品等宝贵物资的飞机)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'velocity', '/vəˈlɒsəti/', '速度, 速率', 'n', 'the velocity of light (光速)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'burst', '/bɜːst/', '爆裂, 炸破', 'v', 'The pipes had burst and the house was under two feet of water. (水管爆裂，房子被水淹了两英尺。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'academy', '/ə\'kædəmɪ/', '学院,学会,专科学校', 'n', 'the American Academy of Arts and Letters (美国艺术和文学学会)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'path', '/pɑːθ/', '小路, 路线', 'n', 'We followed the path along the clifftops. (我们沿着悬崖顶的小径行进。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'refine', '/rɪ\'faɪn/', '精炼, 精制', 'v', 'Oil is refined to remove naturally occurring impurities. (油经过提炼去除天然生成的杂质。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'imprint', '/ɪm\'prɪnt/', '留下烙印', 'v', 'The company carries a variety of binders that can be imprinted with your message or logo. (该公司经营各种可以印上客户所需信息或标识的活页夹。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'intellectual', '/,ɪntə\'lektʃʊəl; -tjʊəl/', '智力的, 有智力的', 'adj', 'Mark’s very intellectual. (马克很聪明。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'impression', '/ɪm\'preʃ(ə)n/', '印象, 感想', 'n', 'When we looked around the school we got a very good impression. (我们参观了学校，对它的印象很好。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'Pennsylvania', '/,pensil\'veinjə/', '宾夕法尼亚州（美国州名）', 'n', 'The letter was mailed from Pennsylvania to me. (信已由宾夕法尼亚州寄到我这里。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'iridium', '/ɪ\'rɪdɪəm; aɪ-/', '[化]铱', 'n', 'Analyzing the fossils at this small site, they counted 52 distinct species just below the iridium layer. (他们分析了这个小地区的化石层，一共计算了在铱层下面的52个不同物种。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'pick', '/pɪk/', '挑选,采摘', 'v', 'Students have to pick three courses from a list of 15. (学生必须从15门课中选修3门。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'cent', '/sent/', '(货币单位)分, 分币', 'n', 'A cup of rice which cost thirty cents a few weeks ago is now being sold for up to one dollar. (几周前价值30美分的1杯米如今卖到了1美元。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'mobility', '/məʊ\'bɪlətɪ/', '活动性, 灵活性', 'n', 'It improves the strength and mobility of joints. (它能提高关节的力量和灵活性。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'inference', '/\'ɪnf(ə)r(ə)ns/', '推论', 'n', 'There were two inferences to be drawn from her letter. (从她的来信可以得到两种推论。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'integrate', '/\'ɪntɪgreɪt/', '使成整体, 结合', 'v', 'He didn\'t integrate successfully into the Italian way of life. (他没有成功融入到意大利的生活方式中去。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'rush', '/rʌʃ/', '冲,匆忙,突袭', 'n&v', 'A small girl rushed past her. (一个小女孩从她身边匆匆经过。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'spray', '/spreɪ/', '喷雾 vt喷射', 'n', 'a new hair styling spray (一种新的定型喷发剂)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'strongly', '/\'strɒŋlɪ/', '强烈地；强有力地', 'adv', 'I’m strongly opposed to capital punishment. (我坚决反对死刑。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'lay', '/leɪ/', '放置,铺设', 'v', 'He laid his hand on my shoulder. (他把一只手搭在我的肩上。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'bite', '/baɪt/', '咬, 刺痛', 'n&v', 'The dog bit him and made his hand bleed. (那只狗把他的手咬出血了。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'harm', '/hɑːm/', '伤害, 损害', 'v', 'chemicals that harm the environment (损害环境的化学品)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'footprint', '/\'fʊtprɪnt/', '足迹', 'n', 'We followed the footprints of a deer in the snow. (我们追踪雪地里一头鹿的足迹。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'herself', '/hɜː\'self/', '她自己', 'pron', 'She cut herself on some broken glass. (碎玻璃把她割伤了。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'sponsor', '/\'spɒnsə/', '发起人 v发起, 主办, 赞助', 'n', 'Race officials announced a handful of new sponsors on Tuesday. (比赛官员们星期二公布了几位新赞助人。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'calorie', '/\'kælərɪ/', '卡路里', 'n', 'A potato has about 90 calories. (一个马铃薯大约有90卡路里的热量。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'unpredictable', '/ʌnprɪ\'dɪktəb(ə)l/', '不可预知的', 'adj', 'He is utterly unpredictable. (他这个人完全让人捉摸不透。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'automobile', '/\'ɔːtəməbiːl/', '汽车', 'n', 'the automobile industry (汽车工业)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'collector', '/kə\'lektə/', '收藏家, 征收者', 'n', 'a stamp collector (集邮者)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'cooperation', '/kəʊ,ɒpə\'reɪʃ(ə)n/', '合作, 协作', 'n', 'the need to strengthen international co-operation (加强国际合作的需要)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'enzyme', '/\'enzaɪm/', '[生化]酶', 'n', 'It is believed that it inhibits an enzyme that promotes cell proliferation in tumours. (据信它能抑制一种能在肿瘤中促进细胞增殖的酶的生成。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'employee', '/emplɒɪ\'iː; em\'plɒɪiː; ɪm-/', '职工, 雇员', 'n', 'a government employee (政府雇员)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'irrigate', '/\'ɪrɪgeɪt/', '灌溉', 'v', 'The water in Lake Powell is used to irrigate the area. (包尔湖的水被用来灌溉该地区。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'dozen', '/\'dʌz(ə)n/', '一打, 十二个', 'n', 'a dozen eggs (一打鸡蛋)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'retrieve', '/rɪ\'triːv/', '恢复,挽回,取回', 'v', 'She bent down to retrieve her earring. (她俯身去捡回耳环。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'printer', '/\'prɪntə/', '印刷工,打印机', 'n', 'a laser printer (激光打印机)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'silt', '/sɪlt/', '淤泥；(使)淤塞', 'n', 'The lake was almost solid with silt and vegetation. (这个湖几乎填满了泥沙和植被。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'roll', '/rəʊl/', '(使)滚动,卷', 'v', 'His sleeves were rolled above his elbows. (他的袖子卷到了胳膊肘的上面。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'surveyor', '/sə\'veɪə/', '测量员, 检查员', 'n', '...the surveyor\'s maps of the Queen Alexandra Range. (…亚历山德拉皇后山脉勘测图。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'worldwide', '/\'wɜːl(d)waɪd; wɜːl(d)\'waɪd/', '全世界的', 'adj', 'We have offices in over 56 countries worldwide. (我们在全世界超过56个国家设有办事处。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'acre', '/\'eɪkə/', '英亩, 地产', 'n', 'They own 200 acres of farmland. (他们拥有200英亩农田。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'nuclear', '/\'njuːklɪə/', '核子的, 原子能的', 'adj', 'France’s reliance on nuclear energy (法国对核能的依赖)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'nutrition', '/njʊ\'trɪʃ(ə)n/', '营养, 营养学', 'n', 'Nutrition and exercise are essential to fitness and health. (营养和运动是保持健康所必不可少的。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'larva', '/\'lɑːvə/', '幼虫', 'n', 'The eggs quickly hatch into larvae. (这些卵很快孵化成幼虫。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'exposition', '/ekspə\'zɪʃ(ə)n/', '展览会, 说明', 'n', '...an art exposition. (…一个艺术展览。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sharp', '/ʃɑːp/', '锐利的,明显的,急剧的', 'adj', 'Make sure you use a good sharp knife. (你一定要用锋利的好刀。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'peasant', '/\'pez(ə)nt/', '农夫', 'n', 'Most villagers are peasant farmers. (大多数村民是农民。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'plastic', '/\'plæstɪk/', '塑料(制品)；塑胶的', 'n', 'children’s toys made of plastic (塑料儿童玩具)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'genetic', '/dʒɪ\'netɪk/', '遗传的, 起源的', 'adj', 'genetic defects (遗传性缺陷)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'page', '/peɪdʒ/', '页,记录', 'n', 'The full address is given on page 15. (详细地址见第15页。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'accumulator', '/ə\'kjuːmjʊleɪtə/', '蓄电池,积聚者', 'n', 'Here is our accumulator which has that nitrogen overpressure which upon loss of pressure in the core would automatically insert coolant into the core should there be a break. (这是我们的蓄电池，那已经氮过度增压,面临着在核心里压力的损失,那会自动的加入冷却剂到,核心去，然后就会产生一个破裂。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'chief', '/tʃiːf/', '首领；主要的, 首要的', 'n', 'Most health chiefs believe the reforms have gone too far. (大多数卫生部领导人都觉得改革搞得过火了。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'imitation', '/ɪmɪ\'teɪʃ(ə)n/', '模仿, 效法', 'n', 'The remake of ‘Casablanca’ was a pale imitation (= something that is much less good than the thing it imitates ) of the original movie. (重拍的《卡萨布兰卡》远不如原版。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'beneficial', '/benɪ\'fɪʃ(ə)l/', '有利的, 有益的', 'adj', 'a drug that has a beneficial effect on the immune system (有益于免疫系统的一种药物)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'lip', '/lɪp/', '嘴唇', 'n', 'She had big eyes and full lips (= large and round lips ). (她眼睛大大的，嘴唇很丰满。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'fertilizer', '/\'fɜːtɪlaɪzə/', '肥料', 'n', '...farming without any purchased chemical, fertilizer or pesticide. (…不使用任何购买的化学品、肥料或杀虫剂的耕作。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'rainwater', '/\'reɪnwɔːtə/', '雨水', 'n', 'Farmers say they need less rainwater if they use fertilizer trees. (农民们说，如果它们使用肥料树，就只需要很少的雨水。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'satire', '/\'sætaɪə/', '讽刺(文学)', 'n', 'the characteristic use of satire in Jonson’s work (琼森作品中讽刺手法的独到运用)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'epoch', '/\'iːpɒk; \'epɒk/', '新纪元, 时代', 'n', 'the Victorian epoch (维多利亚时代)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'impressive', '/ɪm\'presɪv/', '给人深刻印象的, 感人的', 'adj', 'The figures certainly look impressive. (这些数字看上去确实很可观。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'brush', '/brʌʃ/', '刷子, 毛刷, 画笔 vt刷, 掸, 拂', 'n', 'a scrubbing brush (硬毛刷，板刷)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'Massachusetts', NULL, '马萨诸塞(美国州名)', 'n', 'I live in Massachusetts. (我住在马萨诸塞州。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'realism', '/\'rɪəlɪz(ə)m/', '现实主义', 'n', 'the realism of the horses on the carousel (旋转木马上各个木马的逼真形态)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'watch', '/wɒtʃ/', '看,注视,照顾', 'v', 'Do you mind if I watch? (你介意我看着吗？)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'foundation', '/faʊn\'deɪʃ(ə)n/', '基础, 根本', 'n', 'It took the builders three weeks to lay the foundations . (建筑工人花了三星期的时间打地基。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'evident', '/\'evɪd(ə)nt/', '明显的, 显然的', 'adj', 'Bob ate his lunch with evident enjoyment. (显然鲍勃吃午饭吃得津津有味。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'marry', '/\'mærɪ/', '娶, 嫁,和结婚', 'v', 'He married Bea in 1925. (他在1925年娶了贝亚。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'race', '/reɪs/', '种族 v赛跑', 'n', 'The school welcomes children of all races . (该校欢迎各种族的学生就读。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'orient', '/\'ɔːrɪənt; \'ɒr-/', '使适应,使朝向 n东方', 'v', 'You will need the time to orient yourself to your new way of eating. (你需要时间适应新的吃法。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'barren', '/\'bær(ə)n/', '不生育的,贫瘠的；荒地', 'adj', 'Thousands of years ago the surface was barren desert. (很久很久以前，地面还是一片荒漠。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'prosperity', '/prɒ\'sperɪtɪ/', '繁荣', 'n', 'a time of economic prosperity (经济繁荣时期)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'lava', '/\'lɑːvə/', '熔岩, 火山岩', 'n', 'Mexico\'s Mount Colima began spewing lava and ash last night. (墨西哥科利马山昨晚开始喷发熔岩和火山灰。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'pace', '/peɪs/', '步调 v踱步', 'n', 'He moved at a brisk pace down the rue St. Antoine. (他沿着圣安托万街轻快地走着。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'empire', '/\'empaɪə/', '帝国', 'n', 'the Roman empire (罗马帝国)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'contract', '/\'kɒntrækt/', '合同 v缩小,订合同', 'n', 'Employees who refuse to relocate are in breach of contract (= have done something not allowed by their contracts ) . (员工拒绝调动岗位是违反合约的。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'deco', NULL, '装饰派艺术', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'descriptive', '/dɪ\'skrɪptɪv/', '描述的, 叙述的', 'adj', 'the descriptive passages in the novel (小说中的描写性段落)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'ruminant', '/\'ruːmɪnənt/', '反刍动物(的), 沉思的', 'n&a', 'Food chemists probably can improve upon the efficiency and economics of the ruminant’s conversion of cellulose to nutrients. (反刍动物将纤维素转化为营养素的效率和经济性有可能经过食品化学家来改进。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'stoneware', '/\'stəʊnweə/', '瓷器', 'n', '...hand-painted blue-and-white stoneware. (...手绘青花粗陶器。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'mirror', '/\'mɪrə/', '镜子；反映,映出', 'n', 'He spends hours in front of the mirror ! (他老是照镜子！)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'barb', '/bɑːb/', '鱼钩；装倒钩于', 'n', NULL, 4);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', '托福', 'forage', '/\'fɒrɪdʒ/', '草料', 'n', 'Such forage fish already account for nearly a fifth of the world’s total annual catch; another fifth goes to feed pigs and poultry. (这样的饲料鱼已经差不多占每年世界总捕鱼量的五分之一；另有五分之一被用于喂猪和家禽。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'norm', '/nɔːm/', '标准,规范', 'n', 'Joyce’s style of writing was a striking departure from the literary norm. (乔伊斯的写作风格与传统的文学风格大相径庭。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'nitinol', NULL, '[冶]镍钛诺(镍和钛的非磁性合金)', 'n', 'Engineers have produced prototype engines that are driven by the force of nitinol springing from one shape to another as it alternately encounters hot and cold water. (工程师们已制造出一些发动机样机，利用镍钛合金在交替遇热水和冷水时迅速改变形状所产生的力做推动力。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'chick', '/tʃɪk/', '小鸡', 'n', 'a mother hen with her chicks (和小鸡在一起的鸡妈妈)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'condense', '/kən\'dens/', '(使)浓缩, 精简', 'v', 'condensed soup (浓汤)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'cope', '/kəʊp/', '应付,处理', 'v', 'Sometimes I find it hard to cope. (有时候我觉得很难应付。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'frost', '/frɒst/', '霜；结霜', 'n', 'the risk of frost damage to crops (庄稼遭受霜冻灾害的危险)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'client', '/\'klaɪənt/', '[计]顾客, 客户, 委托人', 'n', 'a meeting with an important client (与一位重要客户的会面)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'potentially', '/pə\'tɛnʃəli/', '潜在地', 'adv', 'a potentially dangerous situation (有潜在危险的局势)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'fertile', '/\'fɜːtaɪl/', '肥沃的, 富饶的, 能繁殖的', 'adj', '800 acres of fertile cropland (800英亩的肥沃耕地)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'attain', '/ə\'teɪn/', '达到, 获得', 'v', 'More women are attaining positions of power. (越来越多的女性获得要职。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'background', '/\'bækgraʊnd/', '背景,后台', 'n', 'Students with a background in chemistry will probably find the course easier. (学过化学的学生可能会觉得这门课程容易些。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'facilitate', '/fə\'sɪlɪteɪt/', '促进, 帮助', 'v', 'The new airport will facilitate the development of tourism. (新机场将促进旅游业的发展。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'flexible', '/\'fleksɪb(ə)l/', '易弯曲的,灵活的,柔韧的', 'adj', 'We can be flexible about your starting date. (你具体从哪天开始，我们可以灵活一点。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'precisely', '/prɪ\'saɪslɪ/', '正好', 'adv', 'Women in these jobs are paid less precisely because most of the jobs are held by women rather than men. (从事这些工作的女性报酬之所以较低正是因为做这些工作的人大部分是女性而不是男性。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'egalitarian', '/ɪ,gælɪ\'teərɪən/', '平等主义的', 'adj', 'an egalitarian society (人人平等的社会)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'plover', '/\'plʌvə/', '千鸟', 'n', 'Other species at risk include the red throated diver, golden plover and merlin. (危及到的物种还包括红喉潜鸟（red throated diver）、金斑鸻（golden plover）及灰背隼（merlin）。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'shelve', '/ʃelv/', '搁置', 'v', 'King County has shelved plans to build a driving range. (金郡已搁置了建造一个高尔夫练习场的计划。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'judge', '/dʒʌdʒ/', '法官,裁判员 v断定,裁决', 'n', 'The trial judge specifies the number of years to be spent in prison. (由主审法官确定刑期。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'progressive', '/prə\'gresɪv/', '先进的,前进的；进步分子', 'adj', 'a progressive administration (进步的政府)', 5),
