('en', '托福', 'sector', '/\'sektə/', '部分, 部门', 'n', '...the nation\'s manufacturing sector. (…该国的制造部门。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'bulb', '/bʌlb/', '鳞茎,球形物', 'n', 'tulip bulbs (郁金香球茎)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'trillion', '/\'trɪljən/', '万亿', 'num', 'In a short time the number of cells is more than a trillion. (不久细胞的数量就超过了一万亿。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'isolation', '/aɪsə\'leɪʃ(ə)n/', '隔离，孤立', 'n', 'Because of its geographical isolation, the area developed its own unique culture. (由于地理上的隔绝，该地区发展了自己独特的文化。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'frontality', NULL, '正面描绘', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'Tasmania', '/tæz\'meiniə; -njə/', '塔斯马尼亚岛, 塔斯马尼亚州(澳大利亚州名)', 'n', 'The next partial eclipse of the sun will occur on Nov. 25, 2011, but it will only be visible from Antarctica, Tasmania, New Zealand and southern South Africa. (下一次的太阳日偏食将发生在2011年11月25日，但它只能从南极洲、塔斯马尼亚岛、新西兰和南非的南部可以见到。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'Latin', '/\'lætɪn/', '拉丁文,拉丁语(的)', 'n&a', 'He is well grounded in Latin. (他拉丁语的功底很扎实。)', 4),
