('en', '托福', 'fetus', '/\'fiːtəs/', '胎儿', 'n', 'Pregnant women who are heavy drinkers risk damaging the unborn fetus. (酗酒的孕妇冒有伤害胎儿的危险。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'feeder', '/\'fiːdə/', '饲养员', 'n', 'The feeder fed new feed to pigs so that they laid on fresh. (饲养员用新饲料喂猪好让它们长肉。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'reminder', '/rɪ\'maɪndə/', '提醒物；暗示', 'n', 'The last thing you\'d want is a constant reminder of a bad experience. (你最不想要的就是不断让你想起一段糟糕经历的东西。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'foodstuff', '/\'fuːdstʌf/', '食品, 粮食', 'n', 'a shortage of basic foodstuffs (基本食品短缺)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'shepherd', '/\'ʃepəd/', '牧羊人；带领，引导', 'n', 'In comparison, a German shepherd has a biting pressure of 750 pounds per square inch. (相比较，德国牧羊犬在咬牙时每平方英寸大约有750英镑的压力。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'pine', '/paɪn/', '松(树) vi消瘦', 'n', 'an ancient pine forest (一片古老的松树林)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'informant', '/ɪn\'fɔːmənt/', '通知者, 告密者', 'n', 'One of the witnesses was a paid informant for the FBI. (目击者之一是联邦调查局出钱雇用的线人。)', 4),
