('en', '托福', 'moose', '/muːs/', '[动] 驼鹿', 'n', 'So did we encounter our bear, or a moose? (那么，我们到底遇到了熊或者麋鹿吗？)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'cod', '/kɒd/', '货到付款 (Cash on Delivery) n鳕鱼', 'abbr', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'migrant', '/\'maɪgr(ə)nt/', '移居者, 候鸟', 'n', 'The government divides asylum seekers into economic migrants and genuine refugees. (政府将寻求政治庇护的人划分为经济移民和真正的难民。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'aviation', '/eɪvɪ\'eɪʃ(ə)n/', '航空,飞机制造业', 'n', '...the aviation industry. (…航空工业。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'frontal', '/\'frʌnt(ə)l/', '前沿', 'n', 'By monitoring their brain waves, he saw a pattern of high frequency neural activity in the right frontal cortex that identified in advance who would solve a puzzle through insight and who would not. ( 通过脑电波监测，他发现这些人在解开谜语之前，其右额叶皮质会出现一种高频率的神经活动，通常在得出答案的八秒钟甚至更短的时间内发生。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'hexagonal', '/hek\'sæɡənəl/', '六角形的,六边的', 'adj', 'Instead it is the Desert Express that pulls in, its nine coaches in smart blue, orange and white livery with large hexagonal windows. (然而驶进车站的是沙漠快车，它的九节车厢漆成漂亮的蓝色、橙色和白色，带有六边形的车窗。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'journal', '/\'dʒɜːn(ə)l/', '定期刊物, 杂志', 'n', 'the British Medical Journal (《英国医学杂志》)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'assure', '/ə\'ʃʊə; ə\'ʃɔː/', '使确信, 确保', 'v', 'The document is genuine, I can assure you . (我能向你保证，这文件是真的。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sizable', '/\'saɪzəbl/', '相当大的', 'adj', 'Harry inherited the house and a sizable piece of land that surrounds it. (哈里继承了那座房子和房子周围一块相当大的土地。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'decompose', '/diːkəm\'pəʊz/', '(使)腐烂', 'v', 'a partially decomposed body (部分腐烂的尸体)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'scout', '/skaʊt/', '侦察员 vi侦察', 'n', 'He sent three scouts ahead to take a look at the bridge. (他派出三名侦察兵到前面侦察大桥的情况。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'mineralization', NULL, '矿化作用,成矿作用', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'krypton', '/\'krɪptɒn/', '[化] 氪', 'n', 'Xenon and krypton are not retained by the body so they have little effect. (氙和氪不能在人体内停留所以对人体影响很小。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'diminish', '/dɪ\'mɪnɪʃ/', '(使)减少, (使)变小', 'v', 'The party’s share of the electorate has diminished steadily. (支持这个政党的选民比例持续下降。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'residual', '/rɪ\'zɪdjʊəl/', '剩余的, 残留的', 'adj', 'the residual effects of drug treatment (药物治疗的残留作用)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'chlorophyll', '/\'klɔːrəfɪl; \'klɒ-/', '[生化]叶绿素', 'n', 'The chlorophyll in wheatgrass also helps to purify the liver. (麦草中的叶绿素同样可以帮助净化肝脏。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'xenon', '/\'zenɒn; \'ziː-/', '氙(惰性气体的一种,元素符号Xe)', 'n', 'The krypton and xenon isotope ratios in the gas samples provided a surprising result: They did not match the ratios found in the primordial cloud that spawned the solar system. (气体采样中的氪和氙同位素比值产生了一个令人吃惊的结果：这些比值跟在形成太阳系的原始云团中所发现的比值不一致。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'coil', '/kɒɪl/', '盘绕, 卷', 'v', 'The snake coiled around the branches of the tree. (这条蛇盘在树枝上。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'penicillin', '/penɪ\'sɪlɪn/', '[微]青霉素（一种抗菌素，音译名为盘尼西林）', 'n', 'He reacted well to penicillin. (他对青霉素的反应良好。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'homestead', '/\'həʊmsted/', '家宅，宅基', 'n', 'He looked around, not just up the road but toward the homestead and edge of the woods. (他向四周看了看，看了看路上也看了看宅基地和树林的边缘。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'prestigious', '/pre\'stɪdʒəs/', '享有声望的', 'adj', 'a prestigious literary award (享有盛名的文学奖)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'frustration', '/frʌ\'streɪʃn/', '挫败, 挫折', 'n', 'There are moments when he feels great frustration and it bursts out of him. (会有这样的时刻:当他感觉很好挫折和它爆发出来了。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'servant', '/\'sɜːv(ə)nt/', '仆人', 'n', 'Many young girls became domestic servants . (许多年轻姑娘成了家仆。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'imitative', '/\'ɪmɪtətɪv/', '仿制的,模仿的', 'adj', 'Young people might be provoked into imitative crime by the exploits they see on TV. (年轻人可能会从电视上看到的“英勇行为”中受到启发而仿效电视主人公实施犯罪。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'lesson', '/\'les(ə)n/', '功课', 'n', 'piano lessons (钢琴课)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'incubate', '/\'ɪŋkjʊbeɪt/', '孵卵', 'v', 'The birds returned to their nests and continued to incubate the eggs. (那些鸟儿返巢继续孵卵。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'hectare', '/\'hekteə; -ɑː/', '公顷（等于1万平方米）', 'n', 'Mist rose from a nearby stand of thriving eucalyptus trees she planted after receiving title to more than a hectare of farmland. (雾气从附近生长繁茂的桉树林中升起，这些树是她在获得对一公顷多农田的所有权后栽种的。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'alert', '/ə\'lɜːt/', '警觉的n戒备', 'adj', 'The animal raised its head, suddenly alert. (那只动物突然警觉地抬起头来。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'committee', '/kə\'mɪtɪ/', '委员会', 'n', 'a committee meeting (委员会会议)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'chocolate', '/\'tʃɒk(ə)lət/', '巧克力', 'n', 'a chocolate bar (巧克力条)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'loosely', '/\'lu:slɪ/', '松散地', 'adv', 'If you actually combine the best ideas of both, you end up with an extensible and modular and loosely coupled system. (如果你真的结合二者的最佳思想，就可以得到一个可扩展的、模块化的、松散耦合的系统。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'creator', '/kriː\'eɪtə/', '创建者, 创作者', 'n', '...Ian Fleming, the creator of James Bond. (…伊恩·弗莱明，詹姆斯·邦德的创作者。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'dirt', '/dɜːt/', '污垢, 泥土', 'n', 'You should have seen the dirt on that car! (你没看见那车上沾了多少泥！)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'Asian', '/\'eiʃən/', '亚洲(的), 亚洲人(的)', 'n&a', 'Many of the shops were run by Asians. (这些商店中有许多是由亚洲人经营的。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'enthusiastic', '/ɪn,θjuːzɪ\'æstɪk; en-/', '热心的, 热情的', 'adj', 'an enthusiastic supporter of reform (改革的热心支持者)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'proof', '/pruːf/', '证据，证明', 'n', 'There is no proof that the document is authentic. (没有证据证明这份文件是真的。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'infrastructure', '/\'ɪnfrəstrʌktʃə/', '下部构造,基础下部组织', 'n', 'Some countries lack a suitable economic infrastructure. (一些国家缺乏适当的经济基础设施。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'novelist', '/\'nɒv(ə)lɪst/', '(长篇)小说家', 'n', 'The key to success as a romantic novelist is absolute belief in your story. (一个浪漫派小说家成功的关键在于对自己故事的绝对信念。)', 5),
