('en', '托福', 'remark', '/rɪ\'mɑːk/', '备注,评论 vt评论', 'n', 'Unfortunately, a local journalist overheard the remark. (不巧一名当地记者无意中听到了这些话。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'rote', '/rəʊt/', '死记硬背', 'n', 'In old-fashioned schools, much learning was by rote . (在旧式学校里，很多学习都是靠死记硬背。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'battleship', '/\'bæt(ə)lʃɪp/', '战舰', 'n', 'A new battleship was launched from a shipyard. (一艘新战舰从船坞下水。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'regime', '/reɪ\'ʒiːm/', '政权制度,政权', 'n', 'The regime got rid of most of its opponents. (该政权清除了大多数反对者。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'skepticism', '/\'skeptisizəm/', '怀疑论', 'n', 'I know there are those who don’t believe we can do all these things. I understand the skepticism. (我知道有些人不相信我们可以完成所有这些事情，我理解他们所持的怀疑态度。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'economist', '/ɪ\'kɒnəmɪst/', '经济学者', 'n', 'Do you have some hints for me, how to become a good economist? (如何成为一名好的经济学家，你有什么给我的提示吗？)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'commandment', '/kə\'mɑːndmənt/', '戒律', 'n', 'So you would not break the third commandment. (那么你就不会违反第三条戒律。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'glimpse', '/glɪm(p)s/', '一瞥v瞥见', 'n', 'Some of the fans had waited 24 hours outside the hotel to catch a glimpse of their heroine. (某些追星族为了一睹女杰的风采已在宾馆外守候了24小时。)', 4),
