('en', '托福', 'dissatisfaction', '/dɪssætɪs\'fækʃn/', '不满', 'n', 'She has already expressed her dissatisfaction with this aspect of the policy. (她已对政策的这方面表示了不满。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'knap', '/næp/', '敲击', 'v', NULL, 3),
('en', '托福', 'basaltic', NULL, '玄武岩的', 'adj', 'Frantz Josef Land is a basaltic plateau split into many islands and covered with ice. (法兰仕约瑟夫地的群岛是由一个玄武岩高原分裂而成的，终年覆盖着冰雪。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'plateau', '/\'plætəʊ/', '高地, 高原', 'n', 'A broad valley opened up leading to a high, flat plateau of cultivated land. (一个宽阔的山谷展开，通向一片平坦的高原耕地。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'carbonic', '/kɑː\'bɒnɪk/', '(含)碳的', 'adj', 'Should the carbon dioxide mix with water underground and form carbonic acid, they say, it could leach poisonous materials from rock deep underground that could then seep out. (他们说，一旦二氧化碳与地下水融合极易形成碳酸，而这会把地下岩石中的有毒物质分解出来，从而污染我们的水资源。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'lengthy', '/\'leŋθɪ; \'leŋkθɪ/', '冗长的', 'adj', 'A lengthy period of training is required. (需要很长一段时间的培训。)', 4),
