('en', '托福', 'hatchling', NULL, '人工孵化的鱼苗或小鸟', 'n', 'Lohmann speculates that hatchling turtles may imprint on the magnetic field of their home beach and, if so, such a phenomenon could be the basis of strategies for species preservation. (罗曼推测，人工孵化的海龟也许会留下它们家乡海滩磁场的烙印，如果是这样，这种现象可能会成为物种保护的策略基础。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'specialist', '/\'speʃ(ə)lɪst/', '专门医师, 专家', 'n', 'a heart specialist (心脏专科医生)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'vocal', '/\'vəʊk(ə)l/', '声音的,有声的；元音', 'adj', 'vocal music (声乐)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'hilly', '/\'hɪlɪ/', '多小山的, 多坡的', 'adj', 'The areas where the fighting is taking place are hilly and densely wooded. (战斗发生的地区丘陵起伏，树木茂密。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'elongate', '/\'iːlɒŋgeɪt/', '拉长, (使)伸长；伸长的', 'v', 'Her legs were elongated by the very high heels which she wore. (她穿的高跟鞋非常高，使她的腿显得长了。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'linoleum', '/lɪ\'nəʊlɪəm/', '油布, 油毯', 'n', '...a grey linoleum floor. (...灰色的油毡地面。)', 3),
