('en', '托福', 'caput', '/\'keɪpət/', '头, 首', 'n', 'Chronic portal hypertension may lead to development of collateral circulation , which is manifested as caput medusa in the region of the umbilicus and epigastrium. (慢性门脉高压可导致侧枝循环建立，可出现脐部和上腹部局部水母头样改变。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'receptiveness', NULL, '感受性,接受能力', 'n', 'Group intelligence is correlated, Malone and his colleagues found, with the average social sensitivity — the openness, and receptiveness, to others — of a group\'s constituents. (马龙和他的同事们发现团队智能是和团队成员的平均社会敏感度——开放性，接受能力等等相关联的。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'punish', '/\'pʌnɪʃ/', '惩罚,处罚', 'v', 'Smacking is not an acceptable way of punishing a child. (要惩罚孩子，不应该用打的方式。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'animate', '/\'ænɪmeɪt/', '鼓舞；生气勃勃的', 'v', 'Natural philosophy involved the study of all aspects of the material world, animate and inanimate. (自然哲学涉及到了对包括有生命体与无生命体的物质世界的全面研究。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'militaristic', '/,mɪlɪtə\'rɪstɪk/', '军国主义的', 'adj', '...aggressive militaristic governments. (...侵略性的军国主义政府。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'acreage', '/\'eɪk(ə)rɪdʒ/', '英亩数, 面积', 'n', 'The Palestinians would balk at that as far too much, even if they got the equivalent acreage back, perhaps adjacent to the Gaza Strip. (巴基斯坦方对于这个提议望而却步，即便他们能换回同样多的英亩数，还有可能得到加沙地带的邻近区域。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'impersonation', NULL, '扮演', 'n', 'Convinced of his own righteousness, he was the perfect impersonation of a man of rectitude. (他确信自己很正直，可以完美地扮演刚正不阿的人。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'reabsorb', '/,riːəb\'zɔːb; -\'sɔːb/', '再吸附,重吸收', 'v', 'It could just be a cyst that would either reabsorb itself into the body or need to be surgically removed. (它也有可能仅仅是一个囊肿，能被身体再吸收或者通过手术就可以把它给切除掉。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'interference', '/ɪntə\'fɪər(ə)ns/', '冲突, 干涉', 'n', 'Industrial relations should be free from state interference. (劳资关系应不受政府干预。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'overturn', '/əʊvə\'tɜːn/', '倾覆, 破灭；推翻, 颠倒', 'n', 'We saw the canoe overturn, throwing its passengers into the water. (我们看到独木舟倾覆了，把上面的乘客掀入水中。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'duke', '/djuːk/', '公爵', 'n', 'the Duke of Norfolk (诺福克公爵)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'squarely', '/\'skweəlɪ/', '方形地, 直角地', 'adv', 'He turned and faced her squarely. (他转过身来和她正面相对。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'Henderson', NULL, '亨德森（姓氏）', 'n', 'It was built for one of the Henderson family, right? (它是为了亨德森家族的一个成员建的，对吧？)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'pronoun', '/\'prəʊnaʊn/', '代名词', 'n', 'Now if we could only figure out the pronoun problem. (现在我们可以解决这个代词问题了。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'prisoner', '/\'prɪz(ə)nə/', '囚犯的；战俘', 'adj', 'He was being held prisoner. (他正遭囚禁。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'October', '/ɒk\'təʊbə/', '十月(略作Oct)', 'n', 'Most seasonal hiring is done in early October. (多数季节性招聘是在10月初进行。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'rawhide', '/\'rɔːhaɪd/', '生牛皮；用生牛皮鞭抽打；生牛皮的', 'n', 'At his belt he carried a rawhide whip. (他腰间别着一根生牛皮制作的鞭子。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'nonagricultural', NULL, '非农业的', 'adj', 'Many causes have been proposed for both the intelligence gap and the Flynn effect, including education, income, and even nonagricultural labor. (人们对智力差距和弗林效应提出了许多成因，包括教育、收入，甚至还包括非农业劳动。)', 4),
