('en', '托福', 'devastation', '/,devə\'steɪʃn/', '毁坏,荒废', 'n', 'The war brought massive devastation and loss of life to the region. (战争给该地区造成巨大的破坏以及生命的丧失。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'fletcher', '/\'fletʃə/', '<古>造箭者,弗莱彻', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'paradoxically', '/,pærə\'dɔksikəli/', '相矛盾地,似非而是地', 'adv', 'Paradoxically, the prohibition of liquor caused an increase in alcoholism. (矛盾的是，禁酒反而导致酗酒的增加。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'credible', '/\'kredɪb(ə)l/', '可信的,可靠的', 'adj', 'Her excuse was barely credible. (她的借口无法让人信服。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'flute', '/fluːt/', '长笛；吹长笛,刻槽', 'n', 'The boy trilled on a flute. (男孩在长笛上吹颤音。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'automate', '/\'ɔːtəmeɪt/', '使自动化, 自动操作', 'v', 'Cash machines automate two basic functions of a bank – deposits and withdrawals. (柜员机使银行的两个基本功能——存款和取款自动化了。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'pedagogy', '/\'pedəgɒdʒɪ; -gɒgɪ/', '教学, 教授', 'n', 'I’ve learned as much about teaching from learning about marketing as I have from studying pedagogy – maybe more. (我从销售上学到的有关教育的东西和我研究教育学时候学到的一样多——可能更多。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'pregnant', '/\'pregnənt/', '怀孕的, 重要的', 'adj', 'care for pregnant women (孕妇保健)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'trait', '/treɪt; treɪ/', '显著的特点, 特性', 'n', 'The study found that some alcoholics had clear personality traits showing up early in childhood. (这项研究发现一些酗酒者早在孩童时就表现出明显的个性特征。)', 3),
