('en', '托福', 'narcotic', '/nɑː\'kɒtɪk/', '麻醉药,镇静剂；麻醉的', 'n', 'The truth of Johnson’s comment was recently brought home to me by the serene calm of a resident who was treating a particularly complicated narcotic-dependent patient. (最近，一位住院医生对待一位异常复杂的麻醉药依赖病人的平静态度让我领会到了塞缪尔.约翰逊这句话的真谛。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'narcosis', '/nɑː\'kəʊsɪs/', '昏迷状态, 麻醉', 'n', 'Patient faint shows narcosis , high fever, convulsions, the skin cadaverous or the purple that show blueness. (病人昏倒呈昏迷状态，高烧，惊厥，皮肤苍白或呈青紫色。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'complication', '/kɒmplɪ\'keɪʃ(ə)n/', '复杂化, (使复杂的)因素', 'n', 'The fact that the plane was late added a further complication to our journey. (飞机误点给我们的旅行带来了更大的麻烦。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'embolism', '/\'embəlɪz(ə)m/', '加闰日, 栓塞', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'rupture', '/\'rʌptʃə/', '破裂,裂开；破裂, 决裂', 'v', 'The pipe will rupture at its weakest point. (管道最薄弱的地方会破裂的。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'abrasion', '/ə\'breɪʒ(ə)n/', '磨损', 'n', 'extra protection against abrasion (防止磨损的额外保护)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'proportionally', '/prəu\'pɔ:ʃənəli/', '成比例地,相称地', 'adv', 'However, because of on-chip space limitations, the TLB size can not be increased proportionally. (然而，由于芯片空间的限制，TLB 的大小不能成比例地增加。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'virgo', NULL, '室女宫,室女(星)座', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'freighter', '/\'freɪtə/', '货船,承运人', 'n', 'The artificial reef, the Triangle, was put together from a freighter, a barge and -- this is the Palm Beach area, after all -- an old Rolls Royce. (人工鱼礁、百慕大三角通过货船和驳船装运相连在一起，中间的区域便是棕榈滩。 这卡片终究堪比“一辆古老的劳斯莱斯”。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'thinly', NULL, '稀疏地,瘦', 'adv', 'Sow the radish seeds thinly. (把萝卜籽撒播得稀一些。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'morality', '/məˈræləti/', '道德,品行', 'n', '...standards of morality and justice in society. (…社会中道德和正义的标准。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'Andromeda', '/æn\'drɒmɪdə/', '埃塞俄比亚的公主, 仙女座', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', '托福', 'yardstick', '/\'jɑːdstɪk/', '<美> 码尺, 准绳', 'n', 'The book gives a yardstick for measuring assets. (该书为评估资产提供了一种标准。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'exalt', '/ɪg\'zɔːlt; eg-/', '晋升', 'v', 'But it can also inspire and uplift and exalt, because power can be used to help people accomplish marvelous things. (但是，权力也可以激励人、振奋人和提升人，因为它可以帮助人们成就非同寻常的事业。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'monoxide', '/mə\'nɒksaɪd/', '一氧化物', 'n', 'Then, if the mix of waste is correct, the carbon and oxygen atoms involved recombine to form carbon monoxide and the hydrogen atoms link up into diatomic hydrogen molecules. (接下去，如果废物的组合是合适的，碳原子和氧原子会重新组合形成一氧化碳，而氢原子则结合起来形成双原子的氢分子。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'comply', '/kəm\'plaɪ/', '顺从,答应', 'v', 'The commander said that the army would comply with the ceasefire. (指挥官说过部队会遵从停火协议。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'owe', '/əʊ/', '欠(债等),感激', 'v', 'How much do I owe you (= often used to show that you want to pay for something )? (我该付你多少钱？)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'ingot', '/\'ɪŋgət/', '[冶]锭铁, 工业纯铁', 'n', '...gold ingots. (...金锭。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'premature', '/\'premətjʊə/', '未成熟的,早熟的', 'adj', 'his premature death due to cancer (他因癌症而早逝)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'grievance', '/\'griːv(ə)ns/', '委屈, 冤情, 不平', 'n', 'anyone who has a legitimate grievance against the company (凡是有正当理由对公司感到不满的人)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'conjectural', '/kən\'dʒektʃ(ə)r(ə)l/', '推测的,好推测的', 'adj', 'There is something undeniably conjectural about such claims. (此类声明中绝对有推测的成分。)', 4);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', '托福', 'knot', '/nɒt/', '(绳等的)结；打结', 'n', 'One lace had broken and been tied in a knot. (一根带子已经断了，被打成一个结。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'notch', '/nɒtʃ/', '槽口,刻痕；刻凹痕', 'n', 'Cut a notch near one end of the stick. (在手杖的一端刻一个V形记号。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'oystercatcher', '/\'ɔɪstɚkætʃɚ/', '〈动〉蛎鹬', 'n', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'shorebird', NULL, '岸禽类鸟,沙禽', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'photogrammetry', '/,fəʊtə(ʊ)\'græmɪtrɪ/', '照相测量法', 'n', 'A survey of these surfaces was last undertaken in 1993 using photogrammetry — a technique that combines overlapping images — to achieve a somewhat limited resolution of 2cm. (上一次对这些巨石的表面进行的测量工作是在1993年的时候，使用了摄影测量技术---通过这种技术可以把好多张照片合并起来---其极限分辨率可以达到2厘米。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'mandible', '/\'mændɪb(ə)l/', '下颚, 下颚骨', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'attire', '/ə\'taɪə/', '服装；打扮', 'n', 'business attire (商务着装，正装)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'corrosion', '/kə\'rəʊʒ(ə)n/', '侵蚀,腐蚀状态', 'n', 'They are sprayed with oil to prevent corrosion. (它们被喷了油以防腐蚀。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'upright', '/\'ʌpraɪt/', '正直的；垂直, 竖立', 'adj', 'Katie was still awake, sitting bolt upright(= sitting with her back very straight ) staring at the television. (凯蒂还醒着，坐得笔直，眼睛盯着电视。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'unravel', '/,ʌn\'rævəl/', '拆开,拆开', 'v', 'He could unravel a knot that others wouldn\'t even attempt. (他能解开其他人甚至不敢尝试的绳结。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'glassmaking', NULL, '玻璃(或玻璃器皿等)制造(术)', 'n', 'In 1868, when the industry was still struggling to re-establish other forms of glassmaking, 3,662 tons of beads were exported. (到了1868年，即便岛上的工匠们在埋头对玻璃吹制技术重新探索时，玻璃珠的出口量也达到了3,662吨。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'Katherine', '/\'kæθərin/', '凯瑟琳（女子名）', 'n', 'She chummed around with Katherine. (她与凯瑟琳结为密友。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'malleability', NULL, '有延展性, 柔韧性', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'deft', '/deft/', '敏捷熟练的, 灵巧的', 'adj', 'He sketched her with quick, deft strokes. (他给她画素描，下笔又快又熟练。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'robust', '/rə(ʊ)\'bʌst/', '精力充沛的', 'adj', 'The Secretary of State has made a robust defence of the agreement. (国务卿对这项协议进行了强有力的辩护。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'baedeker', NULL, '旅行指南, 入门手册', 'n', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'sword', '/sɔːd/', '剑', 'n', 'The treaty hung like a sword of Damocles over French politics. (这个条约好像一把达摩克利斯之剑悬在法国政坛之上。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'microfossil', NULL, '微体化石,微化石', 'n', 'This achievement provides the microfossil materials for the study of the lower ordovician in Northern Guizhou. (这一成果对于贵州北部下奥陶统的研究，提供了微体化石资料。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'entomb', '/ɪn\'tuːm; en-/', '埋葬, 成为的坟墓', 'v', 'The city was entombed in volcanic lava. (那个城市被火山熔岩掩埋了。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'burgher', '/\'bɜːgə/', '公民, 市民', 'n', 'Even take the word burgher or bourgeois. (比如说"市民"或称之为"布尔乔亚")', 4),
('en', '托福', 'puffin', '/\'pʌfɪn/', '[鸟]角嘴海雀', 'n', 'Despite 2010 starting and ending with much of the country swathed in snow, threatened species such as the puffin and the rare heath fritillary butterfly enjoyed successful breeding seasons. (尽管2010年开始和结束时，英国的大部分地区都被大雪覆盖，对人们来说不算是好天气。 但英国的国民托管组织声称：在这一年里，英国的很多濒危物种，比如埃克斯莫尔的珍稀希斯豹纹蝶、坎布里亚郡的网纹毛毡衣蝶还有法内尔岛上的海雀，都很享受这适合繁殖的一年，数量大大增加。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'insoluble', '/ɪn\'sɒljʊb(ə)l/', '不能溶解的, 不能解决的', 'adj', 'insoluble conflicts within the department (部门内难以调和的冲突)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'reliability', '/rɪ,laɪə\'bɪlətɪ/', '可靠性', 'n', 'I can assure you of the reliability of the information. (我可以向你保证这消息是可靠的。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'unemployed', '/ʌnɪm\'plɒɪd; -em-/', '失业的, 未被利用的', 'adj', 'an unemployed actor (没戏演的演员)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'immobility', NULL, '牢固,不动', 'n', 'This is due to a stagnation of blood in the veins caused by prolonged immobility, which can promote blood clot formation in veins. (其原因是由于长时间不动，造成静脉血液停滞，促使静脉中血凝块形成。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'preside', '/prɪ\'zaɪd/', '主持,管理', 'v', 'I shall be pleased to preside at your meetings. (我很高兴主持你们的会议。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'spacious', '/\'speɪʃəs/', '广大的,大规模的', 'adj', 'a spacious living area (宽敞的居住空间)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'hydrographic', NULL, '水道测量数的,水道学的', 'adj', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'portraiture', '/\'pɔːtrɪtʃə/', '肖像画法', 'n', 'The dispute illuminates the primitive nature of our attitude to portraiture. (这一争论阐释了我们对肖像画的态度的本性。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'talented', '/\'tæləntɪd/', '有才能的', 'adj', 'a talented actor (一名很有天赋的演员)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'homework', '/\'həʊmwɜːk/', '家庭作业, 副业', 'n', 'For homework, finish the exercise on page 14. (家庭作业是完成第14页的练习。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'filmmaker', '/\'fɪlm,meɪkə/', '电影摄制者', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', '托福', 'understate', '/ʌndə\'steɪt/', '打着折扣说,有意轻描淡写', 'v', 'The press have tended to understate the extent of the problem. (媒体想淡化问题的严重程度。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'narrate', '/nə\'reɪt/', '叙述,作解说', 'v', 'a wildlife film narrated by David Attenborough (一部由大卫•艾登堡解说的野生动物影片)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'lean', '/liːn/', '倾斜,倚靠；依靠,倾斜；贫乏的', 'n', 'trees leaning in the wind (在风中东倒西歪的树木)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'consort', '/\'kɒnsɔːt/', '结交,符合；配偶', 'v', 'The public has accepted Camilla, Prince Charles’s former mistress, as his consort. (公众接受了作为前任情妇的卡米拉成为查尔斯王子的新配偶。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'gannet', '/\'gænɪt/', '塘鹅', 'n', 'Rescue workers carefully clean an oil-soaked northern gannet bird at a facility in Fort Jackson, Louisiana. (救援人员在路易斯安娜州杰克逊堡（ Fort Jackson）的一处救援场所仔细地清理一只浸透了油污的北塘鹅。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'underwing', '/\'ʌndəwɪŋ/', '后翅, 后翅色彩瑰丽的蛾', 'n', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'exorbitant', '/ɪg\'zɔːbɪt(ə)nt/', '（要价等）过高的,（性格等）过分的', 'adj', 'Exorbitant housing prices have created an acute shortage of affordable housing for the poor. (过高的房价使穷人负担得起的房源严重短缺。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'gondwanaland', '/ɡɔnd\'wɑ:nəlænd/', '[地]冈瓦纳大陆', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', '托福', 'gunpowder', '/\'gʌnpaʊdə/', '黑色火药, 有烟火药', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'herring', '/\'herɪŋ/', '青鱼, 鲱', 'n', '...a can of herring. (…鲱鱼罐头。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'earner', '/\'ɜːnə/', '赚钱的人', 'n', 'the country’s biggest export earner (该国利润最高的出口商品)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'angular', '/\'æŋgjʊlə/', '[生物] 有角的,生硬的,笨拙的', 'adj', 'a cubist painting with angular shapes (一幅有棱角图案的立体派绘画)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'wren', '/ren/', '[动] 鹪鹩', 'n', 'And the lion keeps something for you, and the mangrove swamp and the coral and the spider and the wren. (狮子，红树林沼泽、珊瑚，还有蜘蛛和鹪鹩也为你保存了某些东西。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'weary', '/\'wɪərɪ/', '疲倦的,厌倦的；疲倦,厌倦', 'adj', 'She found Rachel in the kitchen, looking old and weary. (她发现雷切尔在厨房里，看上去苍老而疲惫。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'kinglet', '/\'kɪŋlɪt/', '<贬>懦弱的国王,小国君主', 'n', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'uniformity', '/juːnɪ\'fɔːmɪtɪ/', '一致,均匀', 'n', 'There seems to be no uniformity among the various systems. (各系统之间似乎没有统一性。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'screw', '/skruː/', '螺丝钉,螺旋；调节,旋', 'n', 'Fix the frame in position and tighten the screws . (把框子固定在正确位置上，拧紧螺丝。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'priestess', '/\'priːstɪs/', '女祭司, (基督教会以外的)神职人员', 'n', '...the priestess of the temple. (…该寺院里的女祭司。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'neoclassical', '/niːəʊ\'klæsɪk(ə)l/', '新古典主义的', 'adj', 'a palace built in a neoclassical style (新古典主义风格的宫殿)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'thousandfold', '/\'θaʊzəndfəʊld/', '千倍地；千倍的', 'adv', 'He suffers a thousandfold more from his so-called freedom than from his imprisonment in natural existence. (比之人所谓的天赋存在的自由，他遭受千倍的是天赋存在的枷锁。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'enjoyment', '/ɪn\'dʒɒɪmənt/', '享乐, 快乐', 'n', 'Acting has brought me enormous enjoyment. (演戏给我带来莫大的快乐。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'forester', '/\'fɒrɪstə/', '林务官, 森林人', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'spoilage', '/\'spɒɪlɪdʒ/', '损坏', 'n', 'Nutrition education can help with some problems and may prevent improper storage or spoilage. (营养教育可以解决一些问题，并能防止不当的贮存或腐坏发生。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'nonthreatening', NULL, '非胁迫的', 'adj', 'Even when issues have come up in the course of implementation, DeSutter said, the ensuing dialogues always have been carried out in a professional, serious and nonthreatening manner. (德萨特说，即使在执行过程中出现问题，随后开展的对话总是以专业化、严肃和非威胁的方式进行。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'solder', '/\'səʊldə; \'sɒldə/', '焊料；焊接', 'n', 'Each sculptural planter is made-to-order with handmade glass and lead-free solder and comes with everything you need but the plants. (每个艺术花盆都是定制的。 它们由手工制作的玻璃和无铅焊料接合而成，交付使用时，万事俱备，只欠花卉。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'tumble', '/\'tʌmb(ə)l/', '跌倒,翻斤斗；翻倒, 摔倒', 'n', 'It’s possible that stocks could take a tumble next year. (明年股票有可能会大跌。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'harshness', NULL, '粗糙的事物, 严肃, 刺耳', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'collagen', '/\'kɒlədʒ(ə)n/', '胶原质', 'n', 'Lemons, oranges and any other citrus fruit form collagen resulting to holding the skin cells together. It is necessary to drink fruit juices and eat fruit every day. (柠檬，橘子和任何其他柑橘类水果形成胶原蛋白，从而新生皮肤细胞组织，所以每天要多喝果汁多吃水果。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'surgeon', '/\'sɜːdʒ(ə)n/', '外科医生', 'n', '...a heart surgeon. (…一位心脏外科医生。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'idle', '/\'aɪd(ə)l/', '空闲的,懒惰的；虚度, 闲散', 'adj', 'I cannot afford to leave the land lying idle. (我不能让土地闲置。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sumptuous', '/\'sʌm(p)tjʊəs/', '奢侈的,华丽的', 'adj', 'a sumptuous feast (盛宴)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'synchrotron', '/\'sɪŋkrə(ʊ)trɒn/', '同步加速器', 'n', 'The synchrotron accelerator was built at Fermilab and the first patients were treated in 1990. (该同步加速器在费米实验室建造，首例病人于1990年接受治疗。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'landlord', '/\'læn(d)lɔːd/', '房东,地主', 'n', 'His landlord doubled the rent. (他的房东把房租提高了一倍。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'familiarity', '/fəmɪlɪ\'ærɪtɪ/', '熟悉,通晓,精通', 'n', 'I miss the familiarity of home. (我怀念家的那种亲切感。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'stringent', '/\'strɪn(d)ʒ(ə)nt/', '严厉的,迫切的', 'adj', 'stringent anti-noise regulations (严格的防噪音条例)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'signature', '/\'sɪgnətʃə/', '签名,信号', 'n', 'Her signature is totally illegible (= cannot be read ) . (她的签字完全无法辨认。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'cabinetmaker', '/\'kæbɪnɪt,meɪkə/', '家具师,细工木匠', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'chord', '/kɔːd/', '弦,和音', 'n', 'I could play a few chords on the guitar and sing a song. (我能弹一些击他和弦唱一首歌。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'supervisory', '/\'sjuːpə,vaɪzərɪ/', '监督的', 'adj', 'Most supervisory boards meet only twice a year. (大多数监理会一年只开两次会。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'resentment', '/rɪ\'zentm(ə)nt/', '怨恨,愤恨', 'n', 'She expressed resentment at being interviewed by a social worker. (她对于被一个社会工作者面试表示了怨恨。)', 3),
