('en', '托福', 'shopper', '/\'ʃɒpə/', '购物者', 'n', 'The streets were crowded with shoppers. (街上挤满了购物的人。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'correspondingly', '/,kɔris\'pɔndiŋli/', '相应地', 'adv', 'As his political stature has shrunk, he has grown correspondingly more dependent on the army. (随着政治声望不断降低，他相应地变得更依赖于军队了。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'varicolored', '/\'vɛəri,kʌləd/', '杂色的,  多色的', 'adj', 'I hope one day I can sit on the green grassland and watch varicolored fireworks with my girlfriend. (我希望有一天和我的女朋友坐在绿色的草地上看五颜六色的烟花。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'flap', '/flæp/', '片状垂悬物；飘动 v飘动，拍动', 'n', 'the tent flap (帐篷门帘)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'psychoanalyst', '/saɪkəʊ\'ænəlɪst/', '心理分析学者', 'n', 'He\'s a psychologist-or rather, a psychoanalyst. (他是一位心理学家——或者更确切地说，一位心理分析学家。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'stagecraft', '/\'steɪdʒkrɑːft/', '编剧才能,演出技术', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', '托福', 'lifeblood', '/\'laɪfblʌd/', '生命必须的血液, 活力的源泉', 'n', 'Small businesses are the lifeblood of the economy. (小型企业是经济的生力军。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'autobiography', '/ɔːtəbaɪ\'ɒgrəfɪ/', '自传', 'n', 'He published his autobiography last autumn. (他去年秋天出版了他的自传。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'bedpan', '/\'bedpæn/', '便盆, 睡床用脚炉', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'streak', '/striːk/', '条纹vi疾驶 vt加条纹', 'n', 'Sue has blonde streaks in her hair. (休的头发里夹杂着几缕金发。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'duet', '/djuː\'et/', '二重奏', 'n', 'Tonight she sings a duet with first husband Maurice Gibb. (今晚她与第一任丈夫莫里斯∙吉布表演了二重唱。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'daughter', '/\'dɔːtə/', '女儿', 'n', 'She’s got two daughters and one son. (她有两个女儿和一个儿子。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sentimentalized', '/sentɪ\'mentəlaɪz/', '流于感伤,  变多愁善感', 'v', 'He seems either to fear women or to sentimentalize them. (他似乎不是怕女人就是对她们怀有浪漫想法。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'rentable', NULL, '可出租的', 'adj', 'Taller buildings also tended to taper inwards, further reducing rentable space; the cost of moving materials and people also soars. (更高建筑的内部也开始变尖了，进一步减少了可出租的空间；运人运货的成本也直线上升。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'voluminous', '/və\'ljuːmɪnəs/', '卷数多的,大量的', 'adj', 'a voluminous suitcase (一个能装很多东西的手提箱)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'glare', '/gleə/', '闪耀光, 刺眼 v发眩光, 瞪视', 'n', 'a special screen to reduce glare (一种可以减弱刺眼强光的特殊屏幕)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'stint', '/stɪnt/', '紧缩,节省', 'v', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'glory', '/\'glɔːrɪ/', '荣誉, 光荣', 'n', 'She dreamt of future glory as an Olympic champion. (她梦想着将来能得到奥运冠军的荣誉。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'wand', '/wɒnd/', '魔杖；[乐]指挥棒', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'cud', '/kʌd/', '反刍的食物', 'n', 'a cow chewing its cud (在咀嚼反刍食物的母牛)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'inhibition', '/ɪn(h)ɪ\'bɪʃ(ə)n/', '禁止, 阻止', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', '托福', 'innocent', '/\'ɪnəs(ə)nt/', '清白的, 无罪的, 天真的', 'adj', 'Nobody would believe that I was innocent. (没人肯相信我是清白的。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'chomp', '/tʃɒmp/', '大声地咀嚼, 反复咀嚼', 'v', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'civic', '/\'sɪvɪk/', '市的, 市民的', 'adj', 'Jackson spent the day meeting with local religious and civic leaders. (杰克逊那天与当地的宗教领袖和市领导会面。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'stout', '/staʊt/', '发胖的；结实的', 'adj', 'a stout pair of shoes (一双厚实耐穿的鞋子)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'inconsistency', '/ɪnkən\'sɪst(ə)nsɪ/', '矛盾', 'n', 'There were several glaring inconsistencies (= very noticeable differences ) in his report. (他的报告中有几个明显的前后矛盾之处。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'perceivable', NULL, '可知觉的', 'adj', 'Instead of that, the destination is a situation that is perceivable, and declared desirable. (与之相反，目的地是一种可感知、值得期待 的位置。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'posit', '/\'pɒzɪt/', '安置', 'v', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'incompletely', NULL, '不完全地', 'adv', 'Carbon monoxide is released when carbon in fuel—both plants and fossil fuels like gasoline—burns incompletely. (当作为燃料的碳——包括植物和化石燃料比如汽油——不完全燃烧时，就会产生一氧化碳。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'subjugate', '/\'sʌbdʒʊgeɪt/', '使屈服，征服', 'v', 'The native population was subjugated and exploited. (土著人被征服，并遭受剥削。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'lamina', '/\'læmɪnə/', '薄板, 薄层', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'uniformitarianism', '/,juːnɪfɔːmɪ\'teərɪənɪʒ(ə)m/', '[地质]均变论', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'guidance', '/\'gaɪd(ə)ns/', '指导, 领导', 'n', 'a missile with a sophisticated electronic guidance system (有精密电子制导系统的导弹)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'disappoint', '/dɪsə\'pɒɪnt/', '使失望', 'v', 'I hated to disappoint her. (我不愿意让她失望。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'wit', '/wɪt/', '智力, 才智', 'n', 'Alone and penniless, I was forced to live on my wits. (孤身一人又身无分文，我只得靠我的机智来过活。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'contributory', '/kən\'trɪbjʊt(ə)rɪ/', '贡献的, 捐助的', 'adj', 'Smoking is a contributory factor in lung cancer. (抽烟是导致肺癌的一个因素。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'beloved', '/bɪ\'lʌvɪd; -\'lʌvd/', '心爱的 n所爱的人', 'adj', 'He never recovered from the death of his beloved daughter. (他一直没有走出失去爱女的阴影。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'ration', '/\'ræʃ(ə)n/', '定额, 定量', 'n', 'emergency food rations (紧急食物配给)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sunshine', '/\'sʌnʃaɪn/', '阳光', 'n', 'We had three days of spring sunshine. (我们享受了三天的春日阳光。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'exponent', '/ɪk\'spəʊnənt; ek-/', '阐述者,倡导者', 'n', '...a leading exponent of test-tube baby techniques. (…一位试管婴儿技术的主要倡导者。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'intellectually', '/ˌɪntɪˈlektʃʊəli/', '理智地, 与智力(或思维)有关地', 'adv', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'concoct', '/kən\'kɒkt/', '编造；调制', 'v', 'John concocted an elaborate excuse for being late. (约翰为迟到编了一个巧妙的借口。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'darling', '/\'dɑːlɪŋ/', '心爱的人, 亲爱的', 'n', 'Look, darling, there’s Mary. (看呀，亲爱的，玛丽来了。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'leaning', '/\'liːnɪŋ/', '倾斜, 倾向', 'n', 'his radical political leanings (他那激进的政治倾向)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'seclusion', '/sɪ\'kluːʒ(ə)n/', '隔离', 'n', 'They enjoyed ten days of peace and seclusion. (他们享受了十天与世隔绝的宁静生活。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'vulnerability', '/,vʌlnərə\'bɪlətɪ/', '弱点, 攻击', 'n', 'Now that we know the basis of an attack, what can we do to protect ourselves from this vulnerability? (既然我们知道了攻击的基本知识，那么做些什么才能保护我们自己避免这一脆弱性呢？)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'candid', '/\'kændɪd/', '率直的, 坦诚的', 'adj', 'It struck me as an unusually candid confession for a politician. (我觉得这对一个政治家来说是非常坦率的告白了。)', 4);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', '托福', 'puritan', '/\'pjʊərɪt(ə)n/', '清教徒 a清教徒的', 'n', 'Bykov had forgotten that Malinin was something of a puritan. (贝科夫忘记了马利宁是个近乎清教徒式的人。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'regurgitate', '/rɪ\'gɜːdʒɪteɪt/', '反刍,（液体）回流', 'v', 'Some birds and animals regurgitate food to feed their young. (有些鸟兽会回吐食物以喂哺幼崽。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'ruminate', '/\'ruːmɪneɪt/', '反刍, 沉思', 'v', 'One is to see whether you have any worry triggers and to distract yourself when you begin to ruminate. (首先看看你自己是否有担忧的动机，如果当你自己出现“沉思”时，尽量分散自己的注意力。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'flatten', '/\'flæt(ə)n/', '变平, 变单调', 'v', 'Use a rolling pin to flatten the dough. (用擀面杖把面团擀平。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'milkweed', '/\'mɪlkwiːd/', '乳草属植物', 'n', 'This is because their staple food, milkweed, is being used more and more as a garden ornament. (这是因为它们的主要食物乳草被越来越多的用于园林装饰。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'divergent', '/daɪ\'vɜːdʒ(ə)nt; dɪ-/', '分歧的,分开的, 偏离的', 'adj', 'Two people who have divergent views on this question are George Watt and Bob Marr. (在这个问题上意见相左的两个人是乔治·瓦特和鲍勃·马尔。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'unproven', '/ʌn\'prʊvən/', '未经证明的, 未经检验的', 'adj', 'unproven allegations (未经证实的指控)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'permafrost', '/\'pɜːməfrɒst/', '[地]永久冻结带', 'n', 'Yakutsk is the largest city in the world built on permafrost – soil that remains permanently frozen year round. (雅库茨克是世界上建设在永久冻土上最大的城市——土壤在全年都保持冰冻。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'stocky', '/\'stɒkɪ/', '矮壮的, 健壮结实的', 'adj', 'a stocky build (敦实的体格)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'convergence', '/kən\'vɜːdʒəns/', '集中, 收敛', 'n', 'With convergence to an ideal state, you can expect the system to be in or near that ideal state. (通过收敛到一种理想状态，您可以期望系统处于或接近那一理想状态。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'conceivably', '/kən\'siːvəblɪ/', '可想到地, 想象中', 'adv', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'rat', '/ræt/', '老鼠', 'n', 'This was demonstrated in a laboratory experiment with rats. (这点通过在实验室中用老鼠做试验得到证明。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'statistical', '/stə\'tɪstɪk(ə)l/', '统计的, 统计学的', 'adj', 'The report contains a great deal of statistical information. (该报告包含大量统计资料。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'Venice', '/ˈvɛnɪs/', '威尼斯(意大利港市)', 'n', 'They call it “the Venice of the North” and “beauty on water”. (人们把它叫做北方的威尼斯，或者水上美人。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'tiffany', '/\'tɪf(ə)nɪ/', '纱的一种', 'n', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'chase', '/tʃeɪs/', '追赶, 追逐', 'v', 'The dogs saw him running and chased him. (那些狗看到他在跑就追他。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'hardware', '/\'hɑːdweə/', '五金器具', 'n', '...a shop from which an uncle had sold hardware and timber. (…一家叔叔曾经在那里卖五金器具和木材的店铺。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'bunch', '/bʌn(t)ʃ/', '串, 束 v捆成一束', 'n', 'He had left a huge bunch of flowers in her hotel room. (他在她的宾馆房间里留了一大束花。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'uproot', '/ʌp\'ruːt/', '连根拔起, 根除', 'v', 'India\'s evil caste systemremains entrenched in spite of government efforts to uproot it, a racist systemthat condemns darker skinned Indians to a life of penury and servitude. (尽管政府努力根除印度罪恶的等级制度，但其仍然根深蒂固，这是一个种族歧视制度，使得深色皮肤的印度人生活贫苦，受奴役。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'refuge', '/\'refjuːdʒ/', '庇护, 避难所', 'n', 'a wildlife refuge (野生动物保护区)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'unnatural', '/ʌn\'nætʃ(ə)r(ə)l/', '不自然的, 反常的', 'adj', 'It was very cold, which seemed unnatural for late spring. (天很冷，对于晚春来说似乎不正常。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'powerfully', NULL, '非常地,强有力地', 'adv', 'And yet, in many ways, Socrates diagnoses very powerfully an important condition of modern democratic life with which we are all familiar. (但在很多方面，苏格拉底却也诊断了,非常有力且重要的,现在民主生活条件,那是我们都很熟悉的。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'nursing', '/\'nɜːsɪŋ/', '看护, 养育', 'n', 'The elderly at the nursing home have some protections, but not much. (看护之家的老人们已经受到一些保护，但这类措施为数不多。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'enamel', '/ɪ\'næm(ə)l/', '珐琅, 瓷釉', 'n', '...a white enamel saucepan. (…一个白色搪瓷煮锅。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'gossamer', '/\'gɒsəmə/', '蛛丝，薄纱  a轻而薄的', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'unnecessarily', NULL, '不必要地,  徒然', 'adv', 'What you should not do is prevent or override it unnecessarily. (您不应该做的是不必要地阻止或重写它。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'cube', '/kjuːb/', '立方体, 立方', 'n', 'a sugar cube (一块方糖)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'monogamous', '/mɒ\'nɒɡəməs/', '一夫一妻的, 单配的', 'n', 'So birds are monogamous but they cheat as well, within limits. (所以鸟类是一夫一妻制，但它们也背叛，有限度地。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'unwieldy', '/ʌn\'wiːldɪ/', '笨重的，笨拙的', 'adj', 'unwieldy bureaucracy (尾大不掉的官僚机构)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'coloration', '/kʌlə\'reɪʃ(ə)n/', '染色, 着色', 'n', 'That\'s the major reason, why I go great lengths with preparation, scanning, coloration and printing techniques. (这是重要的原因，因此，我花很长时间做准备，扫描、着色和印刷技术。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'butler', '/\'bʌtlə/', '仆役长, 男管家', 'n', 'I called for the butler to clear up the broken crockery. (我叫来男管家清理摔碎的陶瓷。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'Caribbean', NULL, '加勒比海', 'n', 'Then either you go relax on your Caribbean island, or you try to start another one. (你或者可以在你的加勒比海小岛上悠哉游哉下去，或者可以考虑开始下一个生意。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'anatomy', '/ə\'nætəmɪ/', '剖析, 解剖学', 'n', 'a professor of anatomy (解剖学教授)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'flop', '/flɒp/', '猛落，惨败', 'v', 'He flopped down onto the bed. (他一头倒在床上。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'pulse', '/pʌls/', '脉搏, 脉冲', 'n', 'His breathing was shallow and his pulse was weak . (他呼吸很浅，脉搏微弱。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'genuinely', '/\'dʒenjuinli/', '真正地,  由衷地', 'adv', 'They must genuinely like one another, and work well together. (他们必须真诚地喜欢对方，并且能一起有效地工作。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'bomb', '/bɒm/', '炸弹 vt投弹于', 'n', 'The bomb went off at 9.30 in the morning. (炸弹在早上9点半爆炸。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'flint', '/flɪnt/', '打火石, 燧石', 'n', '...a flint arrowhead. (...一个燧石箭头。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'vicissitude', '/vɪ\'sɪsɪtjuːd; vaɪ-/', '变迁兴衰', 'n', 'It reflects the vicissitude of society. (它反映了社会的变迁兴衰。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'quantitative', '/\'kwɒntɪ,tətɪv; -,teɪtɪv/', '数量的, 定量的', 'adj', '...the advantages of quantitative and qualitative research. (…定量和定性研究的优点。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'suitably', '/\'sutəbli/', '合适地, 适宜地', 'adv', '‘He owns three hotels.’ The others looked suitably impressed . (“他拥有三家酒店。”其他人都相应地露出了钦佩之情。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'colorless', '/\'kʌləlɪs/', '无色的, 无趣味的', 'adj', 'As a colorless, sweet-smelling liquid, DCA is used in the production of plastics. (作为一种无色、带着甜蜜香味的液体，常被用于塑料生产。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'cider', '/\'saɪdə/', '苹果酒', 'n', 'At the bar he ordered a cider. (他在酒吧点了一杯苹果汁。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'bard', '/bɑːd/', '吟游诗人', 'n', 'Gnomeo and Juliet is directed and co-written by animation veteran Kelly Asbury, who makes no apologies to William Shakespeare or to the bard\'s, perhaps, most malleable tale. (《格诺米欧和朱丽叶》的导演兼编剧是动漫老手凯利.阿斯博瑞，他对莎翁和古代的吟游诗人没有一丝愧疚之情，这大概是最具改编潜力的故事了。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'chop', '/tʃɒp/', '砍，劈，斩', 'v', 'He went outside to chop some more wood for the fire. (他出去再砍些木材来生火。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'presage', '/\'presɪdʒ/', '预兆 v预示', 'n', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'flatboat', '/\'flætbəʊt/', '(浅水)平底船', 'n', 'Huck was sitting on the gunwale of a flatboat, listlessly dangling his feet in the water and looking very melancholy. (哈克坐在一条平底船的船舷上边，两只脚没精打采地放在水里，看上去忧心忡忡。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'onion', '/\'ʌnjən/', '洋葱', 'n', 'Chop the onions finely. (把洋葱切碎。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'cleanliness', '/\'klenlɪnəs/', '洁癖, 清洁', 'n', 'a high standard of cleanliness (很高的卫生标准)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'peal', '/piːl/', '钟声  v(使)鸣响', 'n', 'A sudden peal of bells broke the silence. (突然响起的铃声打破了寂静。)', 4),
