('en', '托福', 'chronologically', '/krɔnə\'lɔdʒikli/', '按年代的', 'adj', 'Arranged chronologically, it begins with the novel’s primordial period — everything up to 1800 — and then marches century by century into the present. (按年代排列，它开始于小说的产生时期--一切回溯到1800年--然后一个世纪一个世界的进行到现在。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'activate', '/\'æktɪveɪt/', '激活, 使活动', 'v', 'Cooking fumes may activate the alarm. (烹调时的油烟可能会触发警报器。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'episodic', '/,epɪ\'sɒdɪk/', '插曲式的,短暂的', 'adj', '...episodic attacks of fever. (...不定期的发烧。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'fiord', '/fjɔːd/', '(尤指挪威的)海湾, 峡湾', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', '托福', 'esteem', '/ɪ\'stiːm; e-/', '／ vt尊重，敬重', 'n', 'He is held in high esteem by colleagues in the construction industry. (他深受建筑业的同事们的敬重。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'colosseum', '/,kɔlə\'siəm/', '罗马圆形大剧场(建于公元80年,耗时5年,至今大部分尚存)', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'holder', '/\'həʊldə/', '持有者, 占有者', 'n', 'the 800 m world record holder (800米世界纪录保持者)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'achievable', '/ə\'tʃi:vəbəl/', '做得成的, 可完成的', 'adj', 'A 50% market share is achievable. (百分之五十的市场占有率是可实现的。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'fixation', '/fɪk\'seɪʃ(ə)n/', '固定, 注视', 'n', 'Session fixation allows intruders to intercept authenticated sessions or to create new sessions and to capture the session identifier. (会话固定允许入侵者截获验证后的会话，或者创建新会话并捕获会话标识符。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'acknowledge', '/ək\'nɒlɪdʒ/', '承认, 答谢', 'v', 'The family acknowledge the need for change. (全家人都承认需要改变一下。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'uncooperative', '/ʌnkəʊ\'ɒp(ə)rətɪv/', '不合作的, 不配合的', 'adj', 'She became uncooperative: unwilling to do her homework or help with any household chores. (她变得不合作起来：不愿做作业或是帮助分担家务。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'hub', '/hʌb/', '中心,轮轴', 'n', 'the commercial hub of the region (该地区的商业中心)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'meteoroid', '/\'miːtɪərɒɪd/', '流星体', 'n', 'Shortly before the uninhabited space station reached orbit in .May 1973,aeroaynamic pressure ripped off a meteoroid and heat shield. (在1973年5月无人空间站到达轨道前不久，空气动力压力扯破了一个流星体和挡热板。 分析：首先，从逻辑上看，说：“空气动力压力扯破了一个流星体”，是不合事理的，荒谬可笑的。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'threadlike', NULL, '线状的', 'adj', 'Genes are spiraled, threadlike particles made of DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid). (基因是由DNA（脱氧核糖核酸）组成的丝状螺旋微粒。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'pulp', '/pʌlp/', '酱；果肉；纸浆', 'n', 'Halve the melon and scoop out the pulp. (把瓜切成两半，挖出瓜瓤。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'physician', '/fɪ\'zɪʃ(ə)n/', '医师, 内科医师', 'n', '...your family physician. (…你的家庭医生。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sod', '/sɒd/', '草地', 'n', 'But why cover your car in sod? (不过为什么要盖上一层草皮呢？)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'clench', '/klen(t)ʃ/', '捏紧；紧紧握住', 'v', 'Jody was pacing the sidelines, her fists clenched. (乔迪在球场的边线上紧握着拳头来回踱步。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'fist', '/fɪst/', '拳头', 'n', 'She held the money tightly in her fist. (她把钱紧紧地攥在手中。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'supplementation', '/,sʌpləmən\'teʃən/', '增补,补充', 'n', 'The product provided inadequate vitamin and mineral supplementation. (这种产品不能充分补充维生素和矿物质。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'disrepute', '/,dɪsrɪ\'pjuːt/', '坏名声', 'n', 'He faces six charges of bringing the game into disrepute . (他面临六项破坏这项运动声誉的指控。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'syndrome', '/\'sɪndrəʊm/', '综合病症', 'n', 'people who suffer from irritable bowel syndrome (患有肠道过敏综合征的人)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'rectify', '/\'rektɪfaɪ/', '矫正, 调整', 'v', 'I did my best to rectify the situation, but the damage was already done. (我竭尽全力去挽回局面，但损害已经造成了。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'herein', '/hɪər\'ɪn/', '在此处, 此中', 'adv', 'the conditions stated herein (本文所列条件)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'denial', '/dɪ\'naɪ(ə)l/', '否认,谢绝', 'n', 'It seems clear that despite official denials, differences of opinion lay behind the ambassador\'s decision to quit. (很清楚，尽管官方否认，人们对大使决定辞职还是有不同看法。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sugarlike', NULL, '类糖的(糖似的)', 'adj', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'rake', '/reɪk/', '耙子, 斜度', 'n', 'a garden rake (园艺耙)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'survivability', NULL, '残存性', 'n', 'It is an important improvement in the survivability of the crew while maintaining the dynamics and payload of the aircrafts. (这对同时保持飞机的动力、负重以及生存性上是一个重要的提升。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'theological', '/θɪə\'lɒdʒɪk(ə)l/', '神学(上)的', 'adj', 'Did he not offer any reasons for what he did or did he have theological and philosophical discussions with Pilate about his message?  (他没有为他的行为给出任何解释,还是他说了一些神学和哲学的观点,和彼拉多进行了一番讨论呢？)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'dorsal', '/\'dɔːs(ə)l/', '背的, 脊的', 'adj', 'a shark’s dorsal fin (鲨鱼的背鳍)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'irritability', '/,ɪrɪtə\'bɪlɪtɪ/', '过敏性, 兴奋性', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'neurilemmal', NULL, '神经膜的, 神经鞘的', 'adj', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'neuroglia', '/,njʊə\'rɒglɪə/', '[解]神经胶(质)', 'n', 'There are a certain number of neural stem cells, which can be potentially differentiated into the neurons or neuroglia, in the adult mammalian brain. (成年哺乳动物脑内存在有能分化成神经元或神经胶质的神经干细胞，这种神经前体细胞一般位于脑室壁部位。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'mushroom', '/\'mʌʃruːm; -rʊm/', '蘑菇', 'n', 'mushroom soup (蘑菇汤)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'breakdown', '/\'breɪkdaʊn/', '崩溃, 衰弱', 'n', 'I was worried he might have a breakdown if he carried on working so hard. (我担心他这样辛苦地做下去，精神会崩溃的。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'yeast', '/jiːst/', '酵母, 发酵粉', 'n', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'concurrent', '/kən\'kʌr(ə)nt/', '一致的；同时的', 'adj', 'The exhibition reflected concurrent developments abroad. (该展览反映了国外的同期发展情况。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'stratification', '/,strætɪfɪ\'keɪʃən/', '分层, 成层法', 'n', 'The Indian caste system is an example of social stratification . (印度的种姓制度是社会阶层化的一个例子。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'microcosm', '/\'maɪkrə(ʊ)kɒz(ə)m/', '微观世界', 'n', 'In each one of these places you will find a microcosm of molecules which directly impact the look, smell, touch, and sound of everything that you see. (在每一个这样的地方，你都可以发现分子的微观世界，它们会直接影响你所见物质的外观、气味、触感和声音。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'unsureness', NULL, '不确定, 缺乏自信', 'n', 'The public psychosocial status is mostly affected by the unsureness of information in the event of epidemic outbreak. (面对疫情及突发事件，信息的不确定性是影响民众心态变化的主要因素。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'fright', '/fraɪt/', '惊骇, 吃惊', 'n', 'The steam pipes rattled suddenly, and Franklin jumped with fright. (蒸汽管突然发出咯咯的声音，弗兰克林吓得跳了起来。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'belie', '/bɪ\'laɪ/', '掩饰', 'v', 'Her pleasant manner belied her true character. (她讨人喜欢的举止掩饰了她真实的个性。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'hesitant', '/\'hezɪt(ə)nt/', '迟疑的, 犹豫不定的', 'adj', 'Gail gave me a hesitant little smile. (盖尔迟疑地对我微微一笑。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sewer', '/\'suːə; \'sjuːə/', '排水沟，下水道', 'n', '...the city\'s sewer system. (…该城市的下水道系统。)', 5);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', '托福', 'slum', '/slʌm/', '贫民窟', 'n', 'a slum area (贫民区)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'detection', '/dɪ\'tekʃ(ə)n/', '察觉, 侦查', 'n', '...the early detection of breast cancer. (…乳腺癌的早期发现。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'glider', '/\'glaɪdə/', '滑行(或物), 滑翔机', 'n', 'And go for a ride on a glider airplane, because who says planes need motors? (她会去坐滑翔机，因为没人说过飞机一定要有发动机吧？)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'anytime', '/\'enɪtaɪm/', '任何时候, 无论何时', 'adv', 'Call me anytime. I’m always home. (随时给我打电话，我一直在家。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'intuitive', '/ɪn\'tjuːɪtɪv/', '有直觉力的，直觉到的', 'adj', 'He seemed to have an intuitive awareness of how I felt. (他好像凭直觉就知道我的感受。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'undernutrition', '/,ʌndənjuː\'trɪʃən/', '营养不良', 'n', 'Does this mean that all GM foods are fated never to solve the undernutrition of the poor? (这是否意味着所有的转基因食品注定永远不会解决穷人的营养不足？)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'urgent', '/ˈɜːdʒənt/', '急迫的, 紧急的', 'adj', 'He was in urgent need of medical attention. (他急需治疗。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'hohokam', NULL, '霍霍坎文化的', 'adj', 'The hohokam culture disintegrated as they had difficulty maintaining the canals in the dry conditions of the drought. (当干旱的条件使得运河很难被维护好的时候，霍霍坎文化瓦解了。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'irresponsible', '/ˌɪrɪˈspɒnsəbl/', '不负责任的, 不可靠的', 'adj', 'It was highly irresponsible of him to leave the children on their own in the pool. (他把孩子们独自留在游泳池里，真是太不负责任了。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'retrospect', '/\'retrəspekt/', '回顾', 'n', 'In retrospect, I wonder if we should have done more. (回过头看，我在想我们是否应该做得更多些。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'chronic', '/\'krɒnɪk/', '慢性的, 延续很长的', 'adj', 'chronic arthritis (慢性关节炎)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'index', '/\'ɪndeks/', '索引, 指数', 'n', '...the consumer price index. (…消费价格指数。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'flatfish', '/\'flætfɪʃ/', '比目鱼', 'n', 'Recently, she caught a large catfish with the flatfish lures when going on vacation in Ebro River in Spain. The catfish was 97.85 kilograms weight. (日前她在西班牙巴塞罗纳附近的埃布罗河度假时，用大比目鱼鱼饵，逮到一条体重达97.85公斤的淡水鲶鱼。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'attic', '/\'ætɪk/', '阁楼', 'n', 'a small attic room (一间小阁楼)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'sundial', '/\'sʌndaɪəl/', '日昝仪, 日规', 'n', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'butte', '/bjuːt/', '孤立的丘', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'lightly', '/\'laɪtlɪ/', '轻轻地, 轻松地', 'adv', 'I knocked lightly on the door. (我轻轻地敲了敲门。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'uneducated', '/ʌn\'edjʊkeɪtɪd/', '没受教育的；文盲的', 'adj', 'a largely uneducated workforce (大部分人都没受过教育的劳动力)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'securely', '/sɪ\'kjʊəlɪ/', '安全地；无疑地', 'adv', 'Customers can now buy products securely over the Internet. (如今顾客可以安全放心地在网上购物了。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'uncorrupt', '/\'ʌnkə\'rʌpt/', '不腐败的;廉洁的', 'adv', 'We filmed there this summer, and it is deeply touching to see that Collins not only ran a rare, uncorrupt and democratic camp, but had put up a schoolhouse, a library and a meeting hall. (今年夏天我们在那里拍摄时，激动地发现，科林斯不仅管理着一个少见的、廉洁民主的营地，并且建设了校舍、图书馆和大会堂。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'landscapist', '/\'lænd,skeɪpɪst/', '风景画家', 'n', 'The third, draw the art history in the scenery up, the different landscapist has different beauty appreciation. (第三，在风景画艺术史上，不同的风景画家有着不同的审美取向。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'scenery', '/\'siːn(ə)rɪ/', '风景, 景色', 'n', 'The best part of the trip was the fantastic scenery. (此次旅行最精彩之处就是那美妙绝伦的风景。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'complimentary', '/kɒmplɪ\'ment(ə)rɪ/', '称赞的；免费的', 'adj', 'There was a complimentary bottle of champagne in the hotel room. (酒店客房里有一瓶免费赠送的香槟。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'incorporation', '/ɪn,kɔːpə\'reɪʃən/', '合并；组建公司', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'sobriquet', '/\'səʊbrɪkeɪ/', '假名, 绰号', 'n', 'From his staff he earned the sobriquet "Mumbles." (他的员工们给了他“嘟囔”的绰号。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'socialize', '/ˈsəʊʃəlaɪz/', '使社会化, 使社会主义化', 'v', '...an open meeting, where members socialized and welcomed any new members. (…让会员们相互交流、欢迎所有新成员的一次公开集会。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'rename', '/riː\'neɪm/', '重新命名, 改名', 'v', 'Tel Aviv\'s Kings Square was renamed Yitzhak Rabin Square. (特拉维夫的国王广场更名为伊扎克·拉宾广场。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'awaken', '/ə\'weɪk(ə)n/', '唤醒, 醒来', 'v', 'She was awakened by a noise at two in the morning. (凌晨两点，她被一个声音吵醒。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'afflict', '/ə\'flɪkt/', '使痛苦, 折磨', 'v', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'governance', '/\'gʌv(ə)nəns/', '统治, 管理', 'n', '...he will meet with officials from several countries to discuss ways to promote good governance. (...他将与诸国官员会面，讨论如何促进对国家的良性管理。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'methodically', '/məˈθɒdɪkli/', '有条不紊地, 有方法地', 'adv', 'As I methodically explained why each clue revealed too much, my husband dutifully crossed out the words. (我有条不紊地解释为什么每个线索都透露得太多，我丈夫就尽职地划去一些词。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'feverishly', NULL, '兴奋地, 发热地', 'adv', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'personnel', '/pɜːsə\'nel/', '人员, 职员', 'n', 'All personnel are to receive security badges. (所有人员都将拿到安保徽章。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'antifungal', '/,æntɪ\'fʌŋɡəl/', '抗真菌的, 杀真菌的', 'adj', 'It’s treated with nonprescription antifungal creams. (可通过涂抹非处方的抗真菌乳膏进行治疗。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'senior', '/\'siːnɪə; \'siːnjə/', '年长的, 资格较老的', 'adj', 'the senior Democrat on the House committee (众议院委员会中的资深民主党人)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'flashy', '/\'flæʃɪ/', '浮华的', 'adj', 'a flashy dresser (穿着奢华招眼的人)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'dimly', '/\'dimli/', '微暗, 朦胧', 'adv', 'Ecological sciences were only dimly understood in the late 19th century. (19世纪末，人们对生态科学只有朦胧的认识。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'earthward', '/\'ɜːθwəd/', '向地球, 向地面', 'adv', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'justice', '/\'dʒʌstɪs/', '正义, 公平', 'n', 'Children have a strong sense of justice. (儿童有很强的正义感。)', 5),
