('en', '托福', 'disruptive', '/dɪs\'rʌptɪv/', '使破裂的, 分裂性的', 'adj', 'Mike’s parents thought I was a disruptive influence (= a person who causes disruption ) . (迈克的父母认为我是个捣蛋分子。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'girder', '/\'gɜːdə/', '梁', 'n', 'Listen, when you start to feel weak, just tell yourself, ‘I’m as strong as a girder’ . (听着，当你开始觉得虚弱的时候，就对自己说：‘我像 钢梁 一样强壮’。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'bustle', '/\'bʌs(ə)l/', '匆匆忙忙', 'v', 'My mother bustled around the kitchen. (我母亲在厨房里忙得团团转。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'unforeseen', '/ʌnfɔː\'siːn/', '无法预料的', 'adj', 'Radiation may damage cells in a way that was previously unforeseen. (辐射也许会以以前未预见的方式损坏细胞。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'conversational', '/kɒnvə\'seɪʃ(ə)n(ə)l/', '会话的, 对话的', 'adj', 'The article was written in straight-forward, almost conversational language. (这篇文章用简单易懂、几乎是谈话式的语言写成。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'governor', '/\'gʌv(ə)nə/', '统治者, 管理者', 'n', 'the prison governor (监狱长)', 3),
