('en', '托福', 'mania', '/\'meɪnɪə/', '[医]颠狂, 狂躁, 癖好, 狂热', 'n', 'The mania for dinosaurs began in the late 1800s. (恐龙热兴起于19世纪晚期。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'basement', '/\'beɪsm(ə)nt/', '地下室, 墙脚', 'n', 'They bought an old schoolhouse to live in and built a workshop in the basement. (他们买了座旧校舍居住，还在地下室建了个作坊。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'smuggle', '/\'smʌg(ə)l/', '走私, 偷带', 'v', 'My message is "If you try to smuggle drugs you are stupid." (我的讯息是，“你若企图走私毒品，那是犯傻。”)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'stash', '/stæʃ/', '存放 n隐藏处', 'v', 'We went for the bottle of whisky that we had stashed behind the bookcase. (我们去取那瓶我们藏在书柜后面的威士忌。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'quarrelsome', '/\'kwɒr(ə)ls(ə)m/', '喜欢吵架的,好争论的', 'adj', 'He became quarrelsome after drinking too much. (他喝多了就爱找人吵架。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'speedy', '/\'spiːdɪ/', '快的, 迅速的', 'adj', 'a speedy recovery from injury (受伤后的迅速康复)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'prepay', '/priː\'peɪ/', '预付', 'v', 'Participation in the program would be voluntary and participants could prepay the government loan at any time. (参加这以项目是自愿的，参与者可以在任何时间将贷款预付给政府。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'loathsome', '/\'ləʊðs(ə)m/', '讨厌的', 'adj', 'that loathsome little man (那个讨厌的小男人)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'counterfeit', '/\'kaʊntəfɪt; -fiːt/', '赝品  a伪造的 v伪造', 'n', 'Levi Strauss says counterfeits of the company\'s jeans are flooding Europe. (利瓦伊·斯特劳斯说该公司牛仔裤的仿冒品充斥着欧洲市场。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'sender', '/\'sendə/', '寄件人,发送人', 'n', 'a package marked ‘ return to sender ’ (标有“退回寄件人”字样的包裹)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'affix', '/ə\'fɪks/', '使附于, 粘贴 n[语]词缀', 'v', NULL, 3),
('en', '托福', 'obsess', '/əb\'ses/', '迷住, 使困扰', 'v', 'A string of scandals is obsessing America. (一系列丑闻在困扰着美国。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'demolish', '/dɪ\'mɒlɪʃ/', '毁坏, 推翻, 粉碎', 'v', 'He demolished my argument in minutes. (他几分钟内就把我的论点驳倒了。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'golf', '/gɒlf/', '高尔夫球 vi打高尔夫球', 'n', 'He plays golf on Sundays. (他星期天都去打高尔夫球。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'glaciate', '/\'ɡleɪsɪeɪt/', '使结冰, 以冰(或冰河)覆盖', 'v', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'ambience', '/\'æmbɪəns/', '周围环境, 气氛', 'n', 'The overall ambience of the room is cosy. (这个房间的整体氛围是舒适的。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'cab', '/kæb/', '出租汽车', 'n', 'New York’s yellow cabs (纽约的黄色出租车)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'frenzy', '/\'frenzɪ/', '狂暴, 狂怒 vt使发狂', 'n', 'Doreen had worked herself into a frenzy . (多琳一阵狂怒。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'melodrama', '/\'melə(ʊ)drɑːmə/', '情节剧', 'n', 'He was behaving like a character in a Victorian melodrama. (他表现得就像维多利亚时代情节剧里的角色。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'treasure', '/\'treʒə/', '财宝, 财富 vt珍爱', 'n', 'The Book of Kells is Trinity College’s greatest treasure. (《凯尔经》是三一学院的镇院之宝。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'Cincinnati', '/,sinsi\'næti/', '辛辛那提（美国俄亥俄州西南部城市）', 'n', 'We never went back. Instead, we moved to a house near Cincinnati, far from the river. (我们再也没有回去，而是举家迁往离河很远的辛辛那提附近的另一幢房子。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'trove', '/trəʊv/', '被发现的东西, 收藏的东西', 'n', 'But at the stern of the ship, divers found a trove of gold and silver and high-grade ceramics whose significance is more mysterious. (但是潜水人员在船尾部发现了一个由金、银以及高级陶瓷打造的收藏品，这件收藏品的意义更加神秘。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'acronym', '/\'ækrənɪm/', '只取首字母的缩写词', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'bet', '/bet/', '赌, 打赌 v赌, 赌钱', 'n', 'a £50 bet (50英镑的赌注)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'vault', '/vɔːlt/', '拱顶 v做成弧形', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'labyrinth', '/\'læb(ə)rɪnθ/', '迷路, 迷宫, 难解的事物', 'n', '...the labyrinth of corridors. (…迷宫般的走廊。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'rubble', '/\'rʌb(ə)l/', '碎石', 'n', 'Brick rubble is useful as the base for paths and patios. (碎砖可用作道路和天井的基石。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'recipe', '/\'resɪpɪ/', '处方', 'n', 'Large-scale inflation is a recipe for disaster. (大规模的通货膨胀有可能导致灾难。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'rainer', NULL, '人工降雨装置,喷灌装置', 'n', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'yesteryear', '/\'jestəjɪə; -jɜː/', '去年 ad过去不久的岁月', 'n', 'The modern-day sex symbol has now taken the place of the old-fashioned hero of yesteryear. (当今的性感偶像已经取代了往昔过时的英雄形象。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'lore', '/lɔː/', '学问,（动物的）眼光知识', 'n', 'According to local lore, a ghost still haunts the castle. (根据当地人的传说，城堡里至今仍然闹鬼。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'adjoin', '/ə\'dʒɒɪn/', '邻接, 毗连', 'v', 'A vacant plot of land adjoins his house. (有一块空地紧挨着他家。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'mortar', '/\'mɔːtə/', '灰泥,迫击炮 vt用灰泥结合', 'n', 'A cameraman was killed when his vehicle came under mortar fire . (一名摄影师因所乘坐的汽车遭到迫击炮袭击而丧生。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'incongruity', '/,ɪnkɒŋ\'gruːɪtɪ/', '不调和的, 不适宜的', 'n', 'The incongruity of her situation struck Gina with unpleasant force. (吉娜猛然意识到自己处境尴尬，心里很不舒服。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'tableland', '/\'teɪb(ə)llænd/', '高原', 'n', 'The northwestern tableland area has a continental plateau climate with long and chilly winter and cool humid summer. (西北高原地区是大陆高原气候，有漫长而寒冷的冬季，凉爽而湿润的夏季。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'perfection', '/pə\'fekʃ(ə)n/', '尽善尽美, 完美, 完成', 'n', 'My father expected perfection from all of us. (父亲期望我们都尽善尽美。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'fullness', '/\'fʊlnɪs/', '满, 丰富, 成熟', 'n', 'Use a red gloss on your bottom lip to give it fullness. (下唇使用红色唇彩让它显得丰盈饱满。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'recoil', '/rɪ\'kɒɪl/', '畏缩, 弹回 vi退却, 畏缩', 'n', '...his small body jerking in recoil from the volume of his shouting. (…他小小身体在他大声的叫喊中畏缩地抽搐着。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'musicologist', NULL, '音乐学者', 'n', 'Rakae Jamil, a musicologist with the Sanjan Nagar Institute of Philosophy and Arts in Lahore, says there is no doubt that Michael Jackson influenced the pop scene in Pakistan. (拉齐.贾米尔是拉合尔的桑贾恩.纳加尔哲学和艺术研究所的音乐理论家。 他说，迈克尔.杰克逊影响了巴基斯坦的流行歌坛，这点是毫无疑问的。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'forte', '/\'fɔːteɪ; \'fɔːtɪ; fɔːt/', '长处', 'n', 'He found that running long distances was not his forte . (他发现长跑并不是他的强项。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'percussive', '/pə\'kʌsɪv/', '冲击的,叩诊的', 'adj', '...using all manner of percussive effects. (...运用各种打击乐效果。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'multistory', NULL, '多层的,有多层楼的', 'adj', 'The abbey was a maze of multistory wings, each added in a differing century, the architecture conspiring to create a jumbled complex that now housed four hundred brothers. (修道院的结构是迷宫似的多层侧翼，每个侧翼都在不同的世纪里被添上，那建筑拼成一混乱的复合体，里面现在住着四百多个圣殿武士。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'hammerhead', '/\'hæməhed/', '锤头 a锤头状的, 鲁钝的', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'induct', '/ɪn\'dʌkt/', '感应,引导', 'v', 'The government shoulders ethic obligation, she has to induct and maintain the rationalization of the living world. (政府在生活世界中引导和维护生活世界的合理化，肩负著伦理责任；)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'coincident', '/kəʊ\'ɪnsɪd(ə)nt/', '一致的,符合的', 'adj', 'Their aims are coincident with ours. (他们的目标和我们的一致。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'assort', '/ə\'sɔːt/', '分类配全', 'v', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'forgiveness', '/fə\'gɪvnɪs/', '宽恕, 宽仁之心', 'n', '...a spirit of forgiveness and national reconciliation. (…一种宽恕与民族和解的精神。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'spoonful', '/\'spuːnfʊl/', '一匙', 'n', 'He took a spoonful of the stew and ate it. (他舀起一匙炖菜吃了下去。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'oat', '/əʊt/', '[植]燕麦, 麦片粥', 'n', 'Instead of eating hunched pleasurably over a book, I look out of the window and chew every mouthful thoroughly, aware of every single oat and nut and dried bit of apple as it goes down. (送孩子们去学校后，我不再放松地边吃早饭边看书，而是盯着窗外，仔细地嚼着嘴里的食物：每一粒燕麦、每一颗坚果、每一片苹果干。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'differentiating', '/,dɪfə\'renʃɪ,eɪtɪŋ/', '微分的', 'adj', 'So it appears that banks do an unusually lousy job of differentiating themselves. (如此看来，银行业者通常在区分自己的工作上太过糟糕。)', 4);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', '托福', 'symphonic', '/sɪm\'fɒnɪk/', '交响乐的, 和声的', 'adj', 'Of course, anyone knows that it is impossible to play a symphonic work with just three strings. (当然，每个人都知道，只用三根弦来演奏交响乐是不可能的。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sad', '/sæd/', '忧愁的, 悲哀的', 'adj', 'The relationship had been important to me and its loss left me feeling sad and empty. (这种关系对我一直都很重要，失去它让我感到难过而空虚。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'violinist', '/,vaɪə\'lɪnɪst/', '小提琴演奏者, 小提琴家', 'n', 'Rose\'s father was a talented violinist. (罗斯的父亲是一位天才的小提琴手。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'cellist', '/\'tʃelɪst/', '大提琴演奏家', 'n', 'A cellist is always shortening and lengthening the strings. (大提琴演奏家总是在压缩或拉长弦)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'upsurge', '/\'ʌpsɜːdʒ/', '高潮 vi涌起', 'n', 'A new upsurge in construction is in the making. (一个建设的新高潮正在兴起。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'phenomenal', '/fɪ\'nɒmɪn(ə)l/', '现象的,显著的', 'adj', 'the phenomenal success of computer games in recent years (近年来电脑游戏的惊人成功)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'midocean', NULL, '海洋中央', 'n', 'In fact, he wrote his dissertation on the midocean ridge. (实际上，他的博士论文就是关于中央山脊的研究。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'deformation', '/,diːfɔː\'meɪʃ(ə)n/', '变形', 'n', 'B: It occurs when a component reaches its limit for deformation. (B：当一个部件达到了变形的极限时，就会发生断裂。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'omnibus', '/\'ɒmnɪbəs/', '公共汽车, 精选集 a综合性的', 'n', 'the Saturday omnibus edition of ‘Brookside’ (《小溪边》的周六综合版)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'accessibility', '/ək,sesə\'bɪlətɪ/', '易接近, 可到达的', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'unoccupied', '/ʌn\'ɒkjʊpaɪd/', '空闲的,未占领的', 'adj', 'However, to do so, it must find an unoccupied territory and a member of the opposite sex with which to mate. (然而，要想成为领头狼，必须找到一块未被占领的领地和一头能够与之交配的异性狼。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'catalyze', '/\'kætəlaɪz/', '催化, 刺激, 促进', 'v', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'vacant', '/\'veɪk(ə)nt/', '空的, 头脑空虚的,空缺的', 'adj', 'Only a few apartments were still vacant. (只有几套公寓仍然空着。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'suite', '/swiːt/', '(一批)随员, (一套)家具, 组', 'n', 'a honeymoon suite (蜜月套房)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'scavenge', '/\'skævɪn(d)ʒ/', '打扫, 以(腐肉)为食', 'v', 'Pigs scavenged among the rubbish. (猪在垃圾堆里觅食。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'subdivision', '/\'sʌbdɪvɪʒ(ə)n; sʌbdɪ\'vɪʒ(ə)n/', '细分, 一部', 'n', 'Months are a conventional subdivision of the year. (月份是年的常规分支。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'juvenile', '/\'dʒuːvənaɪl/', '青少年的 n青少年, 少年读物', 'adj', 'juvenile crime (少年犯罪)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'betray', '/bɪ\'treɪ/', '出卖, 背叛', 'v', 'He felt that she had betrayed him. (他感觉她背叛了自己。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sensible', '/\'sensɪb(ə)l/', '有感觉的, 明智的', 'adj', 'She seems very sensible. (她好像很明智。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'treetop', '/\'triːtɒp/', '树稍', 'n', 'Boardwalks on the forest floor and the treetop level let visitors experience the rain forest up close. (在树顶上搭建的森林地面走道可以让游客近距离地接触热带雨林。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'ancestry', '/\'ænsestrɪ/', '祖先(集合称), 血统', 'n', 'Most people of European or African ancestry have the "wet" kind: thick and sticky. (大多数欧洲或者非洲血统的人耳垢是湿的，厚的，有粘性的。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'virginal', '/\'vɜːdʒɪn(ə)l/', '处女的, 无瑕的', 'adj', 'Somehow she\'d always been a child in his mind, pure and virginal. (不知何故，她在他心里一直是个天真无邪的孩子。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'dulcimer', '/\'dʌlsɪmə/', '[乐] 洋琴', 'n', 'The ancestry of the piano can be traced to the early keyboard instruments of the fifteenth and sixteenth centuries -- the spinet, the dulcimer, and the virginal. (钢琴的家系可以追溯至15至16世纪早期的键盘乐器，包括小型拨弦琴、洋琴和维金娜琴。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'unpublished', '/ʌn\'pʌblɪʃt/', '未公开出版的,未发表过的', 'adj', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'paddle', '/\'pæd(ə)l/', '短桨, 划桨 v划桨,拌', 'n', 'We might be able to push ourselves across with the paddle. (我们或许可以自己划桨过去。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'twine', '/twaɪn/', '合股线 v织, (使)缠绕', 'n', 'a bundle of papers tied up with twine (用双股线捆扎起来的一摞文件)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'jumble', '/\'dʒʌmb(ə)l/', '混杂, 搞乱 n混乱', 'v', 'The photographs were all jumbled up. (照片乱七八糟地堆在一起。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'bituminous', '/bɪ\'tjuːmɪnəs/', '沥青的,含沥青的', 'adj', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'practicable', '/\'præktɪkəb(ə)l/', '可实行的,可用的', 'adj', 'The only practicable course of action is to sell the company. (唯一可行的做法是把公司卖掉。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'acquaint', '/ə\'kweɪnt/', '使熟知, 通知', 'v', 'Have steps been taken to acquaint breeders with their right to apply for licenses? (已经采取措施让饲养动物者了解他们申请执照的权利了吗？)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'toil', '/tɒɪl/', '苦工, 圈套 v费力地做', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'insurmountable', '/,ɪnsə\'maʊntəb(ə)l/', '不能克服的,不能超越的', 'adj', 'The language difference proved an insurmountable barrier. (语言差异是难以克服的障碍。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'instantaneously', '/,instən\'teinjəsli/', '即刻,突如其来地', 'adv', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'prohibitively', NULL, '禁止地,过分地', 'adv', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'video', '/\'vɪdɪəʊ/', '录象, 视频 a视频的', 'n', 'a video clip shown on the Internet (因特网上的一段视频)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'unprocessed', NULL, '未被加工的', 'adj', 'Reduce packaging by eating more whole, unprocessed foods and using the bulk bins for items that have a long shelf-life. (减少包装，通过吃全食品、未经加工的食品以及对物品使用有很长的保质期的散装箱。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'standardize', '/\'stændədaɪz/', '使符合标准, 使标准化', 'v', 'Attempts to standardize English spelling have never been successful. (统一英语拼写的尝试从未成功过。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'uncooked', '/ʌn\'kʊkt/', '未煮过的', 'adj', 'Always wash your hands after handling uncooked meat. (碰过生肉后一定要洗手。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'forecaster', '/\'fɔːkɑːstə/', '预报员', 'n', 'the weather forecaster (气象预报员)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'stormy', '/\'stɔːmɪ/', '暴风雨的, 激烈的, 暴怒的', 'adj', 'The sky was starting to look stormy. (开始变天了，看上去暴风雨将至。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'untouched', '/ʌn\'tʌtʃt/', '未触及的, 未改变的', 'adj', 'Several papers lay untouched on the desk. (有几份文件原封不动地放在书桌上。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'mennonite', '/\'menənait/', '门诺派教徒', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'police', '/pə\'liːs/', '警察 vt管辖 a警察的', 'n', 'Police surrounded the courthouse. (警察围在法院大楼四周。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'humility', '/hjʊ\'mɪlɪtɪ/', '谦卑', 'n', '...a deep sense of humility. (…深深的谦卑感。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'torrential', '/tə\'renʃ(ə)l/', '猛烈的,汹涌的', 'adj', NULL, 4),
