('en', '托福', 'illustrator', '/\'ɪləstreɪtə/', '插图画家,说明者', 'n', 'Called up for military service, Mr. Marokvia spent the war as an illustrator for the Wehrmacht, applying brush and pencil in Ukraine, Italy, Finland and Yugoslavia. (玛洛克维亚先生被征召入伍，他作为一名德国国防军的插图画家，在乌克兰、意大利、芬兰和南斯拉夫留下了自己的墨迹。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'ectothermic', NULL, '变温动物', 'n', 'Determination of death in ectothermic animals may be more difficult due to differences in their physiology. (断定因安乐死死亡的动物可能更为困难因为不同的动物有不同的生理情况。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'poikilothermic', NULL, '[动]变温的, 冷血动物的', 'adj', 'Unlike most terrestrial animals, aquatic animal species used for human consumption are poikilothermic, meaning their body temperatures vary according to ambient temperatures. (与大多数陆地动物不同，供人类消费的水生动物为冷血品种，也就是说它们的体温会根据环境温度而变化。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'locomote', NULL, '移动, 行动', 'v', 'Since plants cannot locomote , the sensation of experiencing pain would be superfluous. Thus, plants differ completely physiologically from mammals. (由于植物无法移动，它们不太需要具备感知痛苦的能力，因此，植物与哺乳动物在生理上全然不同。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'inadequately', NULL, '不够地,  不够好', 'adv', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'onetime', NULL, '从前的,  一度的；从前', 'adj', 'The onetime heir apparent had played an instrumental role this year in propping up his father\'s rule and his crackdown against the rebellion that ultimately ended his 42-year grip on power. (曾一度作为卡扎菲继承人的赛义夫今年在巩固其父亲的统治并帮助镇压反抗武装一事中起到积极作用。 这场反抗活动最终结束了卡扎菲对利比亚42年的统治。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'citation', '/saɪ\'teɪʃ(ə)n/', '引用,表扬', 'n', '...a 50-minute manifesto with citations from the Koran. (…一段长达50分钟、带有《古兰经》引文的宣言。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'stillness', '/\'stɪlnɪs/', '静止, 沉静', 'n', 'This is your true nature, one of effortless peace and stillness. (这就是你的本质，一个完全不需费力的平静和静止。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'eyesight', '/\'aɪsaɪt/', '视力, 目力', 'n', 'He had a problem with his eyesight. (他的视力有问题。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'comical', '/\'kɒmɪk(ə)l/', '好笑的, 滑稽的', 'adj', 'The note of pure panic in his voice was almost comical. (他那种十分慌张的口气几乎有点滑稽。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'mollusk', '/\'mɒləsk/', '[动]软体动物', 'n', 'Atype of mollusk, the lined chiton has colorful lines on its valves andwhite or yellow spots or bands on its girdle. (条纹石鳖是一种软体动物，瓣膜上有彩色条纹，条带上有白色或黄色斑点或环状物。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'rediscover', '/riːdɪ\'skʌvə/', '重新发现', 'v', '...a one-time rebel who had rediscovered his faith. (...重新发现了自己信仰的一个曾经的反叛者。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'eminent', '/\'emɪnənt/', '著名的,  卓越的', 'adj', 'an eminent lawyer (杰出的律师)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'bleak', '/bliːk/', '寒冷的,荒凉的, 黯淡的', 'adj', 'a bleak January afternoon (一月里一个阴冷的下午)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'silence', '/\'saɪləns/', '寂静, 沉默；使沉默', 'n', 'There was a brief silence before anyone answered. (沉默了片刻才有人回答。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sequester', '/sɪ\'kwestə/', '使隐退, 扣押, 没收', 'v', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'metazoan', '/,metə\'zəʊən/', '[动]后生动物(的)', 'n&a', 'As the scientists conclude: "Our results expand the known metazoan bio-sphere and demonstrate that deep ecosystems are more complex than previously accepted. (科学家总结道：“我们的研究结果扩展了已知的后生生物圈的范围，并揭示出，深层生态系统比我们之前想象的要复杂。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'abreast', '/ə\'brest/', '并肩地, 并排地', 'adv', 'As the car drew abreast of him, Jack suddenly recognised the driver. (那辆车追上来与杰克并行时，他一下子就认出了驾车的人。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'serum', '/\'sɪərəm/', '浆液, 血清', 'n', '...painful injections of anti-cancer serum. (…令人痛苦的抗癌血清注射。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'adrenaline', '/ə\'drenəlɪn/', '肾上腺素(使激动兴奋等)', 'n', 'But for some people merely imagining this scene creates an adrenaline surge. (但是对于某些人但是想象这一幕就会肾上腺素激增。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'milieu', '/\'miːljɜː; mɪ\'ljɜː/', '周围, 环境', 'n', 'Proust’s work reflected his own social and cultural milieu. (普鲁斯特的作品反映了其所在的社会和文化背景。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'compensatory', '/kɒmpen\'seɪtərɪ/', '赔偿的, 补偿的', 'adj', 'She was awarded a large sum in compensatory damages . (她得到了一大笔损失赔偿金。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'unconventional', '/ʌnkən\'venʃ(ə)n(ə)l/', '非传统的, 不合惯例的', 'adj', 'Linus Pauling is an unconventional genius. (莱纳斯·鲍林是个奇才。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'gibe', '/dʒaib/', '嘲笑,讥笑；嘲笑', 'v', '“Please don’t gibe me,” Lydia said. (“请不要嘲笑我，”利迪娅说。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'proprietor', '/prə\'praɪətə/', '所有者, 经营者', 'n', 'For example, many states require a sole proprietor to use their own name for the business name unless they formally file another name as a trade name, or fictitious name. (举例来说，许多国家要求独资经营者使用自己的名称为业务名称，除非他们正式文件中有另一个名字作为商标名或化名。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'mess', '/mes/', '混乱, 脏乱；弄乱', 'n', 'What a mess! (太乱了！)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'silly', '/\'sɪlɪ/', '愚蠢的, 可笑的', 'adj', 'Stop asking silly questions. (别再问傻问题了。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'metric', '/\'metrɪk/', '米制的, 公制的', 'adj', 'a metric tonne (一公吨)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'lintel', '/\'lɪnt(ə)l/', '[建]楣, 过梁', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'untapped', '/ʌn\'tæpt/', '塞子未开的, 未使用的', 'adj', 'Older people are an untapped resource in the employment market. (年龄较大的人是就业市场中有待利用的资源。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'mysteriously', '/mis\'tiəriəsli/', '神秘地,  故弄玄虚地', 'adv', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'corral', '/kə\'rɑːl/', '畜栏；关进畜栏', 'n', 'They corralled the cattle before loading them onto the truck. (他们在把牛装上车以前，先把牛赶入了畜栏。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'prevention', '/prɪ\'venʃn/', '预防, 防止', 'n', 'a fire prevention officer (消防官员)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'playwright', '/\'pleɪraɪt/', '剧作家', 'n', 'The playwright does something remarkable in this scene, but without any impression of straining after an effect. (剧作家在这场中有许多惊人妙笔，但并不给人留下竭力追求表面效果的印象。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'Cuban', '/\'kju:bən/', '古巴人；古巴(人)的', 'n', 'But he says pressure for broad reform on the next Cuban leader, from inside Cuba and outside, will grow. (可是他说，来自古巴境内和境外要求古巴下任领导人进行广泛改革的压力将会增加。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'char', '/tʃɑː/', '烧焦；碳', 'v', 'Roast the peppers until the skin begins to char and blister. (把这些辣椒烤到表皮发黑起泡为止。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'tavernkeeper', NULL, '小餐馆老板', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'upgrade', '/ʌp\'greɪd/', '升级, 上升；使升级, 提升；往上', 'n', '...equipment which needs expensive upgrades. (…需要进行昂贵升级的设备。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'incident', '/\'ɪnsɪd(ə)nt/', '事件；附带的, 易于发生的', 'n', 'Am I at risk because of some incident in my sexual past? (我过去性生活中的某件事会使我处于危险境地吗？)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'slavish', '/\'sleɪvɪʃ/', '奴隶的, 盲从的, 专横的', 'adj', 'a slavish adherence to the rules (对规章的盲目遵从)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'emotive', '/ɪ\'məʊtɪv/', '感情的, 引起强烈感情的', 'adj', 'Embryo research is an emotive issue. (胚胎研究是个让人情绪激动的问题。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'physic', '/\'fɪzɪk/', '医术；治愈', 'n', 'Furthermore, there are entity models created by polygon mesh in many applications such as cartoon, vision environment, network browse, physic scanning, computer games. (此外，在动画、虚拟环境、网络浏览、医学扫描、计算机游戏等领域已经可以看到许多由多边形网格构建的实体模型。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'synapsis', '/sɪ\'næpsɪs/', '[生]染色体结合, 突触', 'n', NULL, 5),
('en', '托福', 'unsophisticated', '/ʌnsə\'fɪstɪkeɪtɪd/', '不谙世故的, 不复杂的', 'adj', 'an unsophisticated audience (老土的观众)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'unspoiled', '/,ʌn\'spɔild/', '未损坏的, 未宠坏的', 'adj', 'unspoiled countryside (未遭到破坏的乡村)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'arthritis', '/ɑː\'θraɪtɪs/', '关节炎', 'n', 'I have a touch of arthritis in the wrist. (我的手腕有轻微关节炎。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'whim', '/wɪm/', '一时的兴致, 奇想', 'n', 'On arrival, she buys a glass factory on a whim, and challenges him to transport a church built entirely of glass by boat from Sydney 250 miles up the coast. (到达目的地后，她突发奇想买了一个玻璃厂，并向他挑战，让他用船沿着 250 英里长的海岸线从悉尼运来建造一整座玻璃教堂。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'hospitable', '/hɒ\'spɪtəb(ə)l; \'hɒspɪt-/', '好客的, 宜人的', 'adj', 'The local people were very kind and hospitable. (当地人非常友好热情。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'carnivorous', '/kɑː\'nɪv(ə)rəs/', '食肉的, 肉食性的', 'adj', 'Snakes are carnivorous. (蛇都是食肉动物。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'depredation', '/,deprɪ\'deɪʃ(ə)n/', '掠夺, 破坏痕迹', 'n', 'Much of the region\'s environmental depredation is a result of poor planning. (这个地区的环境破坏大都是规划不周的结果。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'nostalgia', '/nɒ\'stældʒə/', '乡愁, 怀旧之情', 'n', 'He might be influenced by nostalgia for the surroundings of his happy youth. (他也许被他对快乐青年时代的环境的怀念影响了。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'stewpot', '/\'stjuːpɒt/', '双把炖锅', 'n', 'A hungry wolf\'s attempts to fatten a chicken for his stewpot have unexpected results. (一条饥饿的狼想把鸡养肥来做炖鸡，却产生了意想不到的结果。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'adolescence', '/ædə\'les(ə)ns/', '青春期', 'n', 'Some young people suddenly become self-conscious and tongue-tied in early adolescence. (一些年青人在青春期早期突然变得害羞结舌。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'ministry', '/\'mɪnɪstrɪ/', '(政府的)部门', 'n', '...the Ministry of Justice. (…司法部。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'Toronto', '/təˈrɒntəʊ/', '多伦多（加拿大）', 'n', 'Julia: What can you do in Toronto? (朱莉娅：在多伦多能玩些什么？)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'narrowly', '/\'nærəʊlɪ/', '勉强地, 精细地', 'adv', 'He was narrowly defeated in the election. (他在选举中以微弱差距败北。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'proficiency', '/prə\'fɪʃ(ə)nsɪ/', '熟练, 精通, 熟练程度', 'n', 'I brought her proficiency up to the required level. (我把她的熟练程度提高到所规定的水平。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'spar', '/spɑː/', '争论,园材(如桅,桁等)', 'n', 'Meanwhile, industry, civil society groups and governments continue to spar over the application of intellectual property rights to products and genetic sequences derived from natural resources. (其间，工业、民间社会团体以及政府持续对申请产品和得自自然资源的基因序列的知识产权问题产生争论。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'hometown', '/\'həʊm\'taʊn/', '故乡', 'n', 'Do you like your hometown? (你喜欢你的家乡吗？)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'sociology', '/səʊsɪ\'ɒlədʒɪ; səʊʃɪ-/', '社会学', 'n', 'Out with every theory of human behavior, from linguistics to sociology. (从语言学、社会学的人类行为原理里解脱吧。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'dough', '/dəʊ/', '生面团', 'n', 'Add some raisins to the dough. (在生面团中加一些葡萄干。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'flair', '/fleə/', '才能, 本领', 'n', 'Jo has a flair for languages. (乔有语言天赋。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'esoteric', '/,esə\'terɪk; ,iːsə-/', '秘传的,  神秘的,  难懂的', 'adj', '...esoteric knowledge. (…深奥难懂的知识。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'potion', '/\'pəʊʃ(ə)n/', '一服, 一剂', 'n', '...a magic potion that will make Siegfried forget Brunnhilde and fall in love with Gutrune. (…一种会使齐格弗里德忘掉布伦希德尔德而爱上古特鲁内娜的魔剂。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'laboriously', NULL, '艰难地,  辛勤地', 'adv', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'elixir', '/ɪ\'lɪksə; -sɪə/', '炼金药, 不老长寿药', 'n', 'the search for the elixir of life (寻找长生不老药)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'inextricably', '/ˌɪnɪkˈstrɪkəbli/', '分不开地, 无法摆脱地', 'adv', 'Our survival is inextricably linked to the survival of the rainforest. (我们的生存与雨林的生存息息相关。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'imprecise', '/ɪmprɪ\'saɪs/', '不精确的', 'adj', 'vague imprecise estimates (粗略的、不精确的估计)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'bestow', '/bɪ\'stəʊ/', '给予,利用', 'v', 'The United States bestowed honorary citizenship upon England\'s World War II prime minister, Sir Winston Churchill. (美国授予了二战期间的英国首相温斯顿·丘吉尔爵士荣誉公民的称号。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'bless', '/bles/', '祝福, 保佑', 'v', 'He’s always willing to help. Bless him! (他一向乐于助人，愿上帝保佑他！)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'quaker', '/\'kweikə/', '教友派信徒, 贵格会会员', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'alternately', '/ɔːl\'tɜːnɪtlɪ/', '交替地,轮流地', 'adv', 'The idea is that if a gravitational wave passes through GEO600, it will alternately stretch space in one direction and squeeze it in another. (其基本原理是，当引力波经过GEO600时，它将交替地在一个方向上拉伸空间，在另一个方向上挤压空间。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'thermodynamic', '/,θɜːməʊdaɪ\'næmɪk/', '热力学的, 使用热动力的', 'adj', 'After that, the formalism of statistical mechanics takes over, and calculates partition functions and thermodynamic functions. (从那以后，都是统计力学的内容，计算配分函数,和热力学函数。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'uncrumple', NULL, '去掉…的皱纹,使回复到平整状态', 'vt', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'dinner', '/\'dɪnə/', '正餐, 宴会', 'n', 'What time do you usually have dinner? (你通常什么时候吃饭？)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'untwist', '/ʌn\'twɪst/', '拆开(搓合的绳,线等), 解开', 'v', 'Allow any part of the subtle bodies that is twisted to untwist and separate from any other that one is intertwined with. (允许精细身体中扭曲的任何部分解开扭曲，从混杂在一起的其它部分中分离开来。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'selfless', '/\'selflɪs/', '无私的', 'adj', 'selfless devotion to their work (他们对工作的无私奉献)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'obligation', '/ɒblɪ\'geɪʃ(ə)n/', '义务, 职责, 债务', 'n', 'Employers have an obligation to treat all employees equally. (雇主有责任对所有员工一视同仁。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'fanatical', '/fə\'nætɪkəl/', '狂热的, 入迷的', 'adj', 'He is a fanatical fan of Mozart. (他是一名莫扎特音乐的狂热爱好者。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'coax', '/kəʊks/', '巧妙地（耐心地）处理,哄', 'v', '‘Please, Vic, come with us,’ Nancy coaxed. (“求你了，维克，跟我们一起去吧。”南希哄劝道。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'flue', '/fluː/', '烟道, 暖气管', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', '托福', 'pivot', '/\'pɪvət/', '枢轴；在枢轴上转动', 'n', 'The pedal had sheared off at the pivot. (这个踏板已经在轴处断裂。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'coordination', '/kəu,ɔ:di\'neiʃən/', '协调', 'n', 'Too much alcohol affects your coordination. (喝酒太多会影响你动作的协调。)', 3);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', '托福', 'cancel', '/\'kænsl/', ' 取消， 废除； 删去， 删除； 抵消', 'v', 'Our flight was cancelled. (我们的航班取消了。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'recline', '/rɪ\'klaɪn/', ' 向后倚靠， 斜倚', 'v', 'She proceeded to recline on a chaise longue. (她开始斜靠在一个躺椅上。)', 5),
('en', '托福', 'explosive', '/ɪk\'splousɪv/', '爆炸的，爆发的；使人冲动的； 炸药', 'adj', 'Because the gas is highly explosive, it needs to be kept in high-pressure containers. (由于这种气体极易爆炸，因此需要保存在高压容器内。)', 3),
('en', '托福', 'prepare', '/prɪ\'per/', ' 准备， 预备', 'v', 'The prosecution wanted more time to prepare their case. (原告想要有更多的时间来准备诉讼。)', 4),
('en', '托福', 'crusade', '/kruː\'seɪd/', ' 加入十字军， 投身正义运动；十字军；斗争，运动', 'v', NULL, 3),
('en', '托福', 'supplant', '/sə\'plænt/', ' 取代， 代替', 'vt', 'Barker was soon supplanted as party leader. (巴克在党内的领导地位很快就被人取代了。)', 4),
