('en', 'SAT', 'rationalization', '/,ræʃənəlaɪ\'zeɪʃən/', '合理化', 'n', 'One, for example, is we have a remarkable capacity for rationalization. (例如，其一，每个人都具有非凡的合理化能力。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'accuse', '/ə\'kjuːz/', '控告，指控；谴责；归咎于', 'v', 'The professor stands accused of (=  has been accused of  ) stealing his student’s ideas and publishing them. (那位教授被指控剽窃学生的观点拿去发表。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'chronometer', '/krə\'nɒmɪtə/', '[天] 精密记时表；高度精确的钟表；航海经线仪', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'implication', '/ɪmplɪ\'keɪʃ(ə)n/', '含义；暗示；牵连，卷入；可能的结果，影响', 'n', 'This election has profound implications for the future of U.S. democracy. (对于美国民主的未来而言，这次选举影响深远。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'imperious', '/ɪm\'pɪərɪəs/', '专横的；迫切的；傲慢的', 'adj', 'She raised her hand in an imperious gesture. (她傲慢地扬起手。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'prescient', '/\'preʃɪənt/', '预知的；有先见之明的', 'adj', '...an eerily prescient comedy about a populist multimillionaire political candidate. (...围绕一位身价数百万的民粹主义政治候选人的一部喜剧，其预见性近乎诡异。)', 3),
