('en', 'SAT', 'impale', '/ɪm\'peɪl/', '刺穿；钉住；使绝望', 'v', 'Researchers observed one bird impale a rodent on a cactus. (研究人员观察到，一只鸟把一个啮齿动物钉到了一棵仙人掌上。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'reclusive', '/rɪ\'kluːsɪv/', '隐居的；隐遁的', 'adj', 'All that neighbours knew about the reclusive man was that he had lived in the building for about 20 years. (关于那名隐居者邻居们所知道的就是他已经在那栋楼里住了大约二十年了。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'jingoism', '/\'dʒɪŋɡoɪzəm/', '侵略主义；沙文主义；武力外交政策', 'n', 'a mood of warlike jingoism (好战的沙文主义情绪)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'ratify', '/\'rætɪfaɪ/', '批准；认可', 'v', 'The parliaments of Australia and Indonesia have yet to ratify the treaty. (澳大利亚和印度尼西亚议会还未批准该条约。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'collier', '/\'kɒlɪə/', '矿工；运煤船', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'brooch', '/brəʊtʃ/', '（女用的）胸针，领针', 'n', '“No birthday, ” she repeated, fingering the brooch on her breast. (“没有生日”，她复述道，一边玩弄着胸口的胸针。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'bemoan', '/bɪ\'məʊn/', '惋惜；为…恸哭', 'v', 'He was bemoaning the fact that lawyers charge so much. (他抱怨律师收费太高。)', 4),
