('en', 'SAT', 'incorrigible', '/in\'kɔridʒəbl/', ' 无药可救的； 不能被纠正的', 'adj', '"Sunita, you are incorrigible!" he said. (“苏尼塔，你真是屡教不改啊！”，他说道。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'secant', '/\'siːkənt/', ' 割线', 'n', 'Then the numerical results show that new algorithm effectively overcomes the shortcomings of secant method, and evidently improves the convergent speed, convergent range and algorithm stability. (数值实验结果表明，这种算法不仅有效克服了割线法的缺陷，而且收敛速度、收敛范围和算法的稳定性也得到明显提高。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'precipitation', '/priˌsipi\'teiʃən/', '降水；降水量', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'consummate', '/\'kɔnsəˌmeit/', '完成，完整，圆满； 圆满的； 至上的； 完美的', 'v', 'His wife divorced him for failing to consummate their marriage. (他的妻子因为他未能完婚而跟他离婚了。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'reassure', '/ˌriːə\'ʃuə/', ' 使放心， 使安心， 安慰', 'vt', 'Teachers reassured anxious parents. (老师们安慰焦急的父母。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'divulge', '/dai\'vʌldʒ/', ' 泄露； 暴露', 'v', 'Officials refuse to divulge details of the negotiations. (官员们拒绝透露谈判的细节。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'bane', '/bein/', ' 有害的； 使人苦恼的', 'adj', 'University reform had long been his bugbear, and now was his bane. (大学改革早就是使他头痛的事情， 如今更成为他的祸害了。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'crass', '/kræs/', ' 粗鲁的； 愚钝的', 'adj', 'a crass remark (粗鲁的言语)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'addendum', '/ə\'dendəm/', ' 附录； 补遗', 'n', 'The quantum theory is not just an esoteric addendum . (量子理论并不只是一个深奥的附录。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'palette', '/\'pælit/', ' 调色板', 'n', 'The painter\'s right hand holds the brush, the left the palette. (那位画家的右手握着画笔，左手拿着调色盘。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'orbit', '/\'ɔːbit/', ' 轨道', 'n', 'Mars and Earth have orbits which change with time. (火星和地球的轨道随着时间而发生改变。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'beneficent', '/bi\'nefisnt/', ' 有益的， 受益的', 'adj', 'the beneficent properties of natural remedies (自然疗法的益处)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'salutary', '/\'sæljutəri/', ' 有益健康的； 有益的', 'adj', 'I notice we have janitors and janitresses now in offices, and our young men unfortunately miss that salutary branch of business education. (我注意到现在的办公室都配备了工友，这使我们的年轻人不幸丢掉了这个有益的企业教育的一个内容。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'vexation', '/vek\'seiʃən/', ' 恼怒； 烦恼； 苦恼的原因', 'n', 'He kicked the broken machine in vexation. (他懊恼得踢了这台坏机器一脚。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'comprise', '/kəm\'praiz/', ' 包含， 包括， 构成', 'v', 'The house comprises two bedrooms, a kitchen, and a living room. (这座房子有两间卧室、一间厨房和一间起居室。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'height', '/hait/', ' 高', 'n', 'Sam’s about the same height as his sister now. (萨姆现在身高和他姐姐差不多了。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'moderate', '/\'mɔdərət/', '中等的，适度的，温和的，稳健的； 缓和', 'adj', 'Even moderate amounts of alcohol can be dangerous. (喝酒即使不多也会有危险。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'upheaval', '/ʌp\'hiːvəl/', ' 举起， 抬起， 隆起； 动乱， 大变动', 'v', NULL, 5),
