('en', 'SAT', 'athirst', '/ə\'θəːst/', ' 渴望的', 'adj', 'I am athirst for faraway things. (我渴望着遥远的事物。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'simultaneous', '/ˌsaiməl\'teinjəs/', ' 同时的， 同时发生的', 'adj', 'They grabbed each other’s hands in simultaneous panic. (他们俩同时惊慌起来，相互抓住对方的手。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'predation', '/pri\'deiʃən/', ' 掠夺； 掠食', 'n', 'The importance of predation as an exploitation strategy may be summarized under four main categories. (捕食作用作为一种掠夺性的对策其重要意义可归纳为四个主要方面。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'guarantee', '/ˌgærən\'tiː/', ' 保证， 担保；保证，保证书', 'v', 'The bank will only lend me money if my parents guarantee the loan. (只有我父母作担保，银行才会给我贷款。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'nebula', '/\'nebjulə/', ' 星云', 'n', 'Fine dust in the nebula reflects the light. (星云中细致的尘埃反射了星光。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'literal', '/\'litərəl/', ' 文字的； 照字面上的， 无夸张的', 'adj', 'In many cases, the people there are fighting, in a literal sense, for their homes. (多数情况下，那里的人们实际上都是在为他们的家园而战斗。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'prodigious', '/prəu\'didʒəs/', ' 庞大的； 惊异的； 奇妙的', 'adj', 'the artist’s prodigious output (那位艺术家惊人的高产)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'amorous', '/\'æmərəs/', ' 多情的， 恋爱的， 表示爱情的', 'adj', 'She resisted his amorous advances . (她拒绝了他的挑逗。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'commingle', '/kɔ\'miŋgl/', ' 混合', 'v', 'Many towns allow recyclable items to be commingled for collection in a single container. (在许多城镇，可回收物品可以混放在一个容器里统一收走。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'indolent', '/\'indələnt/', ' 懒惰的； 不痛的', 'adj', 'The former investment banker has not been indolent: his department has been a factory for acronyms since the crisis began. (这位前投资银行家并非懒惰，自危机开始以来，他的部门已成为加工厂的代称。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'vendor', '/\'vendə/', ' 小贩； 【律】卖主', 'n', 'the shouts of street vendors (街头小贩的吆喝声)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'mawkish', '/\'mɔːkiʃ/', ' 令人作恶的； 无味的', 'adj', 'a mawkish love story (无病呻吟的爱情故事)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'attribute', '/ə\'trɪbjuːt/', ' 把…归于； 认为…是…所为； 属性； 品质； 特征', 'v', 'Women tend to attribute their success to external causes such as luck. (女性往往把她们的成功归因于外因，如运气。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'repentant', '/ri\'pentənt/', ' 后悔的， 悔改的； 有后悔表现的', 'adj', 'He was feeling guilty and depressed, repentant and scared. (他现在觉得既内疚又沮丧，既悔恨又害怕。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'genetic', '/dʒi\'netik/', ' 基因的， 遗传  的', 'adj', 'genetic defects (遗传性缺陷)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'triumph', '/\'traiʌmf/', ' 狂喜； 胜利， 成功', 'n', 'Winning the championship is a great personal triumph . (赢得冠军是伟大的个人成就。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'cataract', '/\'kætərækt/', ' 大瀑布； 白内障', 'n', 'In one study, light smokers were found to be more than twice as likely to get cataracts as non-smokers. (一项研究表明，轻度烟民患白内障的比例是不吸烟者的两倍以上。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'ratification', '/ˌrætifi\'keiʃən/', ' 批准； 承认', 'n', 'We welcome this development and we look forward to early ratification of the treaty by China. (我们欢迎这一进展并期望中国早日批准本条约。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'bauxite', '/\'bɔːksait/', ' 铝氧石', 'n', 'They have developed a new process for extracting aluminium from bauxite. (他们开发了一种从铝氧石中提炼铝的新工艺。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'tout', '/taut/', ' 吹捧', 'v', 'his much touted musical (他那出备受推崇的音乐剧)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'palpable', '/\'pælpəbl/', ' 可触知的； 明显的', 'adj', 'There was a palpable sense of relief among the crowd. (众人显然都感到如释重负。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'fortunate', '/\'fɔːtʃənət/', ' 幸运的； 侥幸的', 'adj', 'By a fortunate coincidence, a passer-by heard her cries for help. (所幸正巧有个过路人听到了她的呼救。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'tour', '/tuə/', ' 旅行， 游览；  巡回演出， 巡回医疗；  任期', 'n', 'We met on a coach tour in Italy. (我们是在意大利乘长途客车旅游时相识的。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'persuade', '/pə\'sweid/', ' 说服， 劝说', 'v', 'He was fairly easily persuaded . (他很轻易就被说服了。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'consensus', '/kən\'sensəs/', ' 一致同意； 多数人的意见； 舆论', 'n', 'The EU Council of Finance Ministers failed to reach a consensus on the pace of integration. (欧盟财政部长会议未能就一体化的进度达成共识。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'exacting', '/ig\'zæktiŋ/', ' 苛求的， 严格的； 吃力的， 需付出极大耐心', 'adj', 'She was an exacting woman to work for. (她是一位对下属要求严格的女性。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'irresolute', '/i\'rezəluːt/', ' 犹豫不决的', 'adj', 'The worst reason to launch an attack would be a fear of seeming irresolute. (发起攻击最坏的理由就是因为害怕看起来犹豫不决。)', 4);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', 'SAT', 'judicature', '/\'dʒuːdikətʃə/', ' 司法', 'n', 'Can you explain to me the function of judicature? (你能给我解释一下司法系统的功能吗？)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'embellish', '/im\'beliʃ/', ' 装饰， 美化； 添加细节', 'v', 'She gave an embellished account of what had happened. (她添油加醋地把发生的事描述了一番。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'retract', '/ri\'trækt/', ' 缩回， 缩进； 收回， 取消， 撤销', 'v', 'He confessed to the murder but later retracted his statement. (他承认谋杀，但后来又翻供了。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'blazon', '/\'bleizən/', '广布，宣布；夸示； 细致准确地绘制或描述', 'v', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'swerve', '/swəːv/', ' 突然转向', 'v', 'Drivers coming in the opposite direction swerved to avoid the bodies. (从反方向过来的司机们突然转向以避开这些尸体。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'gossip', '/\'gɔsip/', ' 传播流言蜚语； 说长道短；闲话，聊天；非议，流言', 'v', 'We spoke, debated, gossiped into the night. (我们交谈、争论、闲聊到夜间。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'sarcasm', '/\'sɑːkæzəm/', ' 挖苦， 讽刺', 'n', '‘Good of you to arrive on time,’ George said, with heavy sarcasm (= very clear sarcasm ) . (“你到得真准时啊。”乔治不加掩饰地挖苦道。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'antecedent', '/ˌænti\'siːdənt/', ' 先行的；先辈', 'adj', 'Some patients state that lesions develop at the site of antecedent trauma. (一些患者指出，病灶出现在先前的创伤部位。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'didactic', '/di\'dæktik/', ' 说教的； 教诲的', 'adj', 'His novel has a didactic tone. (他的小说有一种道德说教的口吻。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'colloquial', '/kə\'ləukwiəl/', ' 口语的； 通俗语的', 'adj', '...a colloquial expression. (…一个口语表达法。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'sterling', '/\'stəːliŋ/', ' 纯正的', 'adj', 'Those are sterling qualities to be admired in anyone. (那些优秀品质在任何人身上都值得称道。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'granular', '/\'grænjulə/', ' 由小粒而成的， 粒状的', 'adj', '...a granular fertilizer. (...一种粒状化肥。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'fatuous', '/\'fætjuəs/', ' 愚昧的； 昏庸的', 'adj', 'fatuous questions (愚昧的问题)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'incorporate', '/in\'kɔːpəreit/', ' 合并， 纳入， 结合', 'v', 'The agreement would allow the rebels to be incorporated into a new national police force. (该协议将允许叛军并入一支新的国家警察部队。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'recapture', '/riː\'kæptʃə/', ' 取回， 夺回', 'n', 'The armed forces have launched offensives to recapture lost ground. (这支武装部队已发动进攻要夺回失去的阵地。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'clemency', '/\'klemənsi/', ' 温和； 仁慈， 和蔼', 'n', 'The republican party has vociferously opposed any clemency for convicted terrorists. (共和党已经高声反对给被判有罪的恐怖分子以任何仁慈。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'benediction', '/ˌbeni\'dikʃən/', ' 祝福', 'n', 'The minister pronounced the benediction. (牧师做了赐福祈祷。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'reiterate', '/riː\'itəreit/', ' 反复地说， 重申； 重做', 'v', 'Let me reiterate the most important points. (我来把最重要的几点重申一遍。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'segment', '/\'segmənt/', ' 弓形； 部分', 'n', 'Decorate with orange segments. (用几瓣橙子作点缀。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'sinister', '/\'sinistə/', ' 左边的； 险恶的', 'adj', 'There is a sinister side to these events. (这些事件有邪恶的一面。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'menacing', '/\'menəsiŋ/', ' 威胁的； 险恶的', 'adj', 'dark menacing clouds (可怕的乌云)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'pendulum', '/\'pendjuləm/', ' 钟摆； 摆锤', 'n', 'The political pendulum has swung in favour of the liberals. (政治的钟摆已经摆向了自由派。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'aerosol', '/\'eərəusɔl/', ' 气溶胶', 'n', 'The mission will also observe clouds and aerosol particles in the troposphere. (此次任务还将观测对流层中的云和气溶胶粒子。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'termination', '/ˌtəːmi\'neiʃən/', ' 结局； 末端， 终点', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'superb', '/sju\'pəːb/', ' 极好的， 高质量的', 'adj', 'The food was superb. (食物好吃极了。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'regress', '/ri\'gres/', ' 复原； 逆行； 使倒退', 'v', 'If your child regresses to babyish behaviour, all you know for certain is that the child is under stress. (如果你的孩子退步到幼稚的行为，你可以肯定的是孩子正处在压力之下。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'duplicate', '/ˈdjuːplɪkeɪt/', ' 复制的， 二重的， 二倍的； 复写， 复制， 使加倍；复制品，副本', 'adj', 'A duplicate copy should be made for the county record office. (应该制作一个副本呈交县档案室。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'affable', '/\'æfəbl/', ' 和蔼可亲的', 'adj', 'an affable guy (一个平易近人的人)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'decrease', '/diː\'kriːs/', '（使）变小，（使）减少；减少；减少的量', 'v', 'The number of people who have the disease has decreased significantly in recent years. (近年来，这种病的患者人数明显下降。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'engrossing', '/in\'grəusiŋ/', ' 引人入胜的， 极有趣的', 'adj', 'He is an engrossing subject for a book. (他是非常有趣的写书题材。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'surmise', '/səː\'maiz/', '推测，猜测； 推测， 猜测', 'v', 'There\'s so little to go on, we can only surmise what happened. (几乎没有什么可继续进行的，我们只能猜测发生过的事。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'eradicate', '/i\'rædikeit/', ' 根除， 灭绝', 'v', 'an attempt to eradicate inflation (为消除通货膨胀所作的努力)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'germinate', '/\'dʒəːmineit/', ' 使发芽； 使发展', 'v', 'Some seed varieties germinate fast, so check every day or so. (有一些品种的种子发芽快，所以差不多每天都要察看一下。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'conservationist', '/ˌkɔnsəː\'veiʃənist/', '  保护管理论者', 'n', 'Conservationists say the law must be strengthened. (环保主义者称必须加强法制。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'patriotism', '/\'pætriətizəm/', ' 爱国心， 爱国精神', 'n', 'He was a country boy who had joined the army out of a sense of patriotism and adventure. (他是个乡下小伙子，出于爱国心和冒险精神参了军。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'abdominal', '/æb\'dɔminəl/', ' 腹部的', 'adj', '...vomiting, diarrhoea, and abdominal pain. (…呕吐、腹泻和腹部疼痛。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'hackneyed', '/\'hæknid/', ' 陈腐的； 常见的', 'adj', 'Power corrupts and absolute power corrupts absolutely. That\'s the old hackneyed phrase, but it\'s true. (权力导致腐败，绝对权力导致绝对腐败。这虽是老生常谈，但无半点虚言。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'despondent', '/di\'spɔndənt/', ' 垂头丧气的； 沮丧的', 'adj', 'Gill had been out of work for a year and was getting very despondent. (吉尔失业一年了，开始变得非常消沉。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'trifle', '/\'traifl/', ' 玩忽， 不认真对待；少量，少许；小事，琐事，微不足道的东西', 'v', 'There’s no point in arguing over trifles. (为琐事争吵毫无意义。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'accomplice', '/ə\'kʌmplis/', ' 同盟者， 帮凶', 'n', 'Witnesses said the gunman immediately ran to a motorcycle being ridden by an accomplice. (证人们说该枪手立即向由一名同犯驾驶的摩托车跑去。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'apogee', '/\'æpədʒiː/', ' 远地点', 'n', 'If this is an ellipse around the Earth, then this would be perigee and this would be apogee . (如果这是一个围绕，地球的椭圆形轨道，那么这是近地点，这是远地点。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'string', '/striŋ/', ' 缚， 捆； 悬挂；弦，线，细绳；一串，一行', 'v', 'Her key hung on a string around her neck. (她的钥匙穿了根绳子挂在脖子上。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'submit', '/səb\'mit/', ' 使服从， 屈服； 呈送， 提交', 'v', 'In desperation, Mrs. Jones submitted to an operation on her right knee to relieve the pain. (绝望中，琼斯夫人不得已接受了一次她右膝的手术以减轻疼痛。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'affluent', '/\'æfluənt/', ' 丰富的； 富裕的', 'adj', 'affluent families (富裕的家庭)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'garble', '/\'gɑːbl/', ' 断章取义； 混淆', 'v', NULL, 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'macabre', '/mə\'kɑːbə/', ' 恐怖的， 令人毛骨悚然的', 'adj', 'a macabre tale (令人毛骨悚然的故事)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'redundant', '/ri\'dʌndənt/', ' 多余的', 'adj', 'the removal of redundant information (多余信息的删除)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'racy', '/\'reisi/', ' 有活力的； 有原来风味的， 天然的， 地道的', 'adj', 'He listened to David Bright\'s racy stories about life in the navy. (他听戴维·布赖特讲有关海军生活的生动有趣的故事。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'contrition', '/kən\'triʃən/', ' 悔悟， 后悔', 'n', 'In contrition she expatiated on the beauty of the garden. (在后悔中，她反复谈论着花园的美丽。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'admissible', '/əd\'misəbl/', ' 容许的； 可采纳的', 'adj', '{"COLLOINEXA":["admissible evidence"]} (可采信的证据)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'mellifluous', '/mə\'lifluəs/', ' 嗓音如蜜般的； 甜美的； 流畅的', 'adj', 'I grew up around people who had wonderful, mellifluous voices. (我是在一群有着悦耳动听嗓音的人周围长大的。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'condensation', '/ˌkɔnden\'seiʃən/', ' 凝结', 'n', 'He used his sleeve to wipe the condensation off the glass. (他用袖子擦去眼镜上凝结的水滴。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'statement', '/\'steitmənt/', ' 声明， 陈述', 'n', 'In an official statement, she formally announced her resignation. (在一份官方声明中，她正式宣布辞职。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'factor', '/\'fæktə/', ' 将…分解因子；因子', 'v', 'The rise in crime is mainly due to social and economic factors. (犯罪率上升主要由社会和经济因素造成。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'asinine', '/\'æsinain/', ' 愚笨的', 'adj', 'What an asinine remark! (多么愚蠢的话！)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'respiratory system', NULL, '[解剖] 呼吸系统', '', 'The main function of the respiratory system is to provide passages and room for gaseous exchange. (呼吸系统的主要功用是提供空气到肺的通路及气体交换的场所。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'carbon dioxide', NULL, '二氧化碳', 'n', 'An unavoidable by-product of burning oil is carbon dioxide, and carbon dioxide harms the environment. (使用石油不可避免的副产品就是二氧化碳，这是对环境有害的气体。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'mischievous', '/\'mistʃivəs/', ' 恶作剧的； 淘气的', 'adj', 'Their sons are noisy and mischievous. (他们的几个儿子又吵又淘气。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'dumbfound', '/dʌm\'faund/', ' 使人哑然失声； 使发愣', 'v', 'This suggestion dumbfounded Joe. (这个建议使乔伊惊呆了。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'aural', '/\'ɔːrəl/', ' 听觉的', 'adj', 'an aural stimulus (听觉刺激)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'barometer', '/bə\'rɔmitə/', ' 气压计', 'n', 'A man in camp took a barometer reading at half-hour intervals. (营地里的一个人每半小时看一次气压计。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'triennial', '/trai\'eniəl/', ' 每三年一度的', 'adj', 'We signed a triennial contract yesterday. (昨日签了一项三年的合约。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'sensation', '/sen\'seiʃən/', ' 感觉， 知觉', 'n', 'Jerry realized that he had no sensation in his legs. (杰里意识到自己双腿都没有了知觉。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'brightness', '/\'braitnis/', ' 亮度', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'refer', '/ri\'fəː/', ' 提交， 谈及', 'v', 'In his speech, he referred to a recent trip to Canada. (在他的讲话中，他提到了最近的加拿大之行。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'stellar', '/\'stelə/', ' 星的； 星形的； 主要的； 主角的', 'adj', 'the company’s stellar growth (这家公司辉煌的发展)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'flame', '/fleim/', ' 火焰', 'n', 'Flames poured out of the windows of the building. (火焰从大楼窗口冒出来。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'occupant', '/\'ɔkjupənt/', ' 占有者； 居住者', 'n', 'The furniture had been left by the previous occupants. (家具是先前的住户留下的。)', 5),
