('en', 'SAT', 'inestimable', '/in\'estiməbl/', ' 无价的， 无法估计的', 'adj', 'a painting of inestimable value (一幅价值连城的画)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'illusion', '/i\'ljuːʒən/', ' 错觉， 幻觉； 假象', 'n', 'She was under no illusion that he loved her. (她不再幻想他爱她了。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'whine', '/wain/', ' 哭诉， 发牢骚， 发呜呜声', 'v', NULL, 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'considerable', '/kən\'sidərəbl/', ' 相当大  的， 可观的； 值得考虑的， 重要的', 'adj', 'Michael has already spent considerable time in Barcelona. (迈克尔在巴塞罗那已经待了相当长的时间了。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'toxin', '/\'tɔksin/', ' 毒素', 'n', 'Tests showed increased levels of toxin in shellfish. (测试表明贝类中的毒素级别上升了。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'subsist', '/səb\'sist/', ' 生存， 生活； 供养', 'v', 'The prisoners subsisted on one mug of the worst quality porridge three times a day. (犯人一天三次靠一杯最差的粥维持生活。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'brief', '/briːf/', ' 简短的； 短暂的；摘要，大纲；简短介绍；简要汇报', 'adj', 'We stopped by Alice’s house for a brief visit. (我们顺路在艾丽斯家小坐片刻。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'recover', '/ri\'kʌvə/', ' 重新获得； 痊愈， 复原', 'v', 'Four paintings stolen from the gallery have been recovered. (美术馆的四幅被盗画作已经失而复得。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'influx', '/\'inflʌks/', ' 流入', 'n', '...problems caused by the influx of refugees. (…难民大量涌入所造成的问题。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'devastate', '/\'devəsteit/', ' 毁坏', 'v', 'The city centre was devastated by the bomb. (市中心被这枚炸弹摧毁了。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'prodigy', '/\'prɔdidʒi/', ' 天才  ； 奇观， 奇事', 'n', 'The Russian tennis prodigy is well on the way to becoming the youngest world champion of all time. (这位俄罗斯网球奇才已很有望成为历史上最年轻的世界冠军。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'exonerate', '/ig\'zɔnəreit/', ' 免罪； 免除', 'v', 'The official report basically exonerated everyone. (该官方报告基本洗脱了所有人的干系。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'surfeit', '/\'səːfit/', ' 使饮食过度', 'v', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'disavow', '/ˌdisə\'vau/', ' 不承认， 否认； 否定， 抵赖', 'v', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'maple', '/\'meipl/', ' 枫树', 'n', '...a solid maple worktop. (…一张结实的枫木工作台。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'compliant', '/kəm\'plaiənt/', ' 顺从的； 适应的', 'adj', 'For years I had tried to be a compliant and dutiful wife. (多年来我都在努力做一个顺从尽职的妻子。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'obsequies', '/\'ɔbsikwiz/', '葬礼，丧礼', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'diagonal', '/dai\'ægənl/', '对角的，对角线的', 'adj', 'diagonal parking spaces (斜线停车位)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'prophetic', '/prə\'fetik/', ' 预言的', 'adj', 'It turned out to be a prophetic piece of journalism. (事实证明那则新闻作出了正确的预言。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'aroma', '/ə\'rəumə/', ' 芳香， 香气， 香味', 'n', 'the aroma of fresh coffee (新煮咖啡的香味)', 5);
INSERT IGNORE INTO word_bank (language, category, word, phonetic, translation, part_of_speech, example, difficulty) VALUES
('en', 'SAT', 'transmute', '/træns\'mjuːt/', ' 改变', 'v', 'A radioactive atom could transmute itself into an entirely different kind of atom. (放射性原子本身能嬗变为性质完全不同的另一种原子。)', 4),
