('en', 'SAT', 'preeminence', '/priː\'eminəns/', ' 卓越， 杰出', 'n', 'Now some believe that the clan\'s preeminence is already being challenged. (现在，一些人相信党派的卓越性正受到挑战。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'succulent', '/\'sʌkjulənt/', ' 多汁的， 多水分的', 'adj', 'a succulent steak (美味多汁的牛排)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'accompany', '/ə\'kʌmpəni/', ' 陪同， 伴随； 为…伴奏', 'v', 'Children under 14 must be accompanied by an adult. (14岁以下儿童必须有成人陪同。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'obviate', '/\'ɔbviˌeit/', ' 消除； 排除； 预防', 'v', 'The new treatment obviates the need for surgery. (新的疗法免除了手术的必要。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'probity', '/\'prəubiti/', ' 正直； 诚实', 'n', 'I have always found Bentner to be a model of probity in our dealings. (在我们的交往中，我一贯认为班特纳是诚实的典范。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'perspicuous', '/pə\'spikjuəs/', '  明白易懂的， 清楚的', 'adj', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'immediate', '/i\'miːdiət/', ' 直接的； 立即的， 即刻的', 'adj', 'Our immediate response to the attack was sheer horror. (我们对攻击的第一反应就是非常惊恐。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'excerpt', '/\'eksəːpt/', ' 摘录， 选录， 节录', 'n', '...an excerpt from Tchaikovsky\'s Nutcracker. (…柴可夫斯基的《胡桃夹子》选段。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'abet', '/ə\'bet/', ' 教唆， 煽动； 帮助， 支持', 'vt', 'His wife was sentenced to seven years imprisonment for aiding and abetting him. (他的妻子因与他同谋被判决关押七年。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'minnow', '/\'minəu/', ' 鲤类小鱼', 'n', 'The minnow too had grown and had become a full-fledged fish. (此时的小鲦鱼也已长大，长成了一条年轻健康的鲦鱼。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'platitude', '/\'plætitjuːd/', ' 陈词滥调； 陈腐', 'n', 'His excuse was the platitude ‘boys will be boys.’ (他还是那一套理由:“男孩总归是男孩。”)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'subtlety', '/\'sʌtlti/', ' 微妙， 敏锐， 细微的区别', 'n', 'The play lacks subtlety. (这部戏不够精细。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'upbraid', '/ʌp\'breid/', ' 责备， 叱责', 'v', 'His mother summoned him, upbraided him, wept and prayed. (他母亲把他叫来，责骂了他。然后母亲哭着做了祷告。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'landlord', '/\'lændlɔːd/', ' 房东， 地主', 'n', 'His landlord doubled the rent. (他的房东把房租提高了一倍。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'factious', '/\'fækʃəs/', ' 闹派别的； 好捣乱的', 'adj', NULL, 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'ingratiate', '/in\'greiʃieit/', ' 使迎合， 使讨好', 'v', 'Many politicians are trying to ingratiate themselves with her. (很多政客都在试图讨她的欢心。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'introductory', '/ˌintrə\'dʌktəri/', ' 引导的， 介绍的', 'adj', 'as the chairman said in his introductory remarks (正如主席在开场白中所说的)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'buffoon', '/bə\'fuːn/', ' 小丑', 'n', '"They are drawing their inner buffoon, " explains the teacher. (“他们在描绘自己内心的丑角，”老师解释说。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'caitiff', '/\'keitif/', ' 卑劣的； 胆小的', 'adj', NULL, 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'apiece', '/ə\'piːs/', ' 每人， 每个', 'adv', 'The pictures are worth about £10,000 apiece. (这些画每幅价值约一万英镑。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'lurid', '/\'luːrid/', ' 苍白的， 可怕的； 血红的； 耸人听闻的', 'adj', 'lurid headlines (骇人听闻的标题)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'preempt', '/pri\'empt/', ' 预先制止； 抢在…之前做或说', 'v', 'The law would preempt stronger local rules. (该法律将预先制止更强硬的地方性法规。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'hone', '/həun/', '  磨， 把…放在磨石上磨；细磨刀石', 'v', 'He set about honing his skills as a draughtsman. (他着手提高自己的绘画技艺。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'cursory', '/\'kəːsəri/', ' 仓促的， 草率的', 'adj', 'Because be loved, proud Lin Lan cannot bear the grievance after be being misunderstood, cursory under put forward to part company. (因为被爱，骄傲的林岚不能忍受被误解后的委屈，草率之下提出分手。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'insouciance', '/in\'suːsjəns/', ' 漫不经心， 不在乎', 'n', 'He replied with characteristic insouciance: "So what?" (他用特有的漫不经心的口吻答道：“那又怎么样？”)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'primp', '/primp/', ' 细心打扮， 过分装饰', 'v', 'She spends hours primping in front of the mirror. (她总是花很长时间在镜子前梳妆打扮。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'corroborate', '/kə\'rɔbəreit/', ' 使坚固； 确证', 'v', 'We now have new evidence to corroborate the defendant’s story. (我们现在有新的证据来证实被告人的说法。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'bland', '/blænd/', ' 温和的， 柔和的； 乏味的； 冷漠的', 'adj', 'a few bland comments (不痛不痒的几句评语)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'atone', '/ə\'təun/', ' 弥补', 'vi', 'He felt he had atoned for what he had done to his son. (他觉得他已弥补曾对儿子所做的错事。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'disparage', '/dis\'pæridʒ/', ' 蔑视， 贬损； 使失去信誉', 'v', 'Matcham’s theatres were widely disparaged by architects. (马彻姆设计的剧院遭到了建筑师的普遍抨击。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'yummy', '/\'jʌmi/', ' 美味的； 赏心悦目的', 'adj', 'Yes, thanks. It\'s yummy! (是的，谢谢。它是美味的！)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'bursar', '/\'bəːsə/', '  会计', 'n', NULL, 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'outlast', '/ˌaut\'lɑːst/', ' 比…长久， 比…活得长', 'v', 'Smith outlasted his rivals in the council to become leader in 1996. (史密斯比对手坚持得更久，于1996年成了委员会的领导人。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'utopian', '/juː\'təupiən/', ' 乌托邦的， 理想化的', 'adj', 'His was a utopian vision of nature in its purest form. (他对大自然的看法是一种最纯粹的乌托邦式看法。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'tangible', '/\'tændʒəbl/', ' 确实的， 触摸得到的， 具体的', 'adj', 'The scheme must have tangible benefits for the unemployed. (这个计划一定要对失业者有实实在在的好处。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'impend', '/im\'pend/', ' 即将发生', 'v', 'Crucial events impend in Europe. (欧洲即将发生具有决定意义的事变。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'pious', '/\'paiəs/', ' 虔诚的', 'adj', 'He was a quiet, pious man. (他是个文静、虔诚的人。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'congest', '/kən\'dʒest/', ' 使充满， 使拥塞', 'v', NULL, 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'mordent', '/\'mɔːdənt/', ' 【音】 波音', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'witticism', '/\'witisizəm/', ' 妙语； 俏皮话', 'n', 'Once in a while, after witticism, he would look down, and his eyes would meet hers. (每隔一小会儿， 说了什么俏皮话以后， 他就低下头， 和她目光相交。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'approximately', '/ə\'prɔksimitli/', ' 近似地， 大约地', 'adv', NULL, 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'diplomat', '/\'dipləmæt/', ' 外交官', 'n', 'French diplomats (法国外交官)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'monocracy', '/mɔ\'nɔkrəsi/', ' 独裁政治', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'incubus', '/\'iŋkjubəs/', ' 梦魇； 沉重的负担', 'n', 'Joyce regarded his US citizenship as a moral and political incubus. (乔伊斯认为他的美国公民身份在道德上和政治上是很大的负担。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'hut', '/hʌt/', ' 小屋， 棚屋', 'n', 'a wooden hut (小木屋)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'artifice', '/\'ɑːtifis/', ' 巧办法； 欺骗', 'n', 'Weegee\'s photographs are full of artfulness, and artifice. (维加的照片充满了奇技妙想。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'collaborate', '/kə\'læbəreit/', ' 协作， 合作', 'v', 'Much later he collaborated with his son Michael on the English translation of a text on food production. (后来他和儿子迈克尔合作，把一个有关食品生产的文本翻译成英语。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'superficial', '/ˌsjuːpə\'fiʃəl/', ' 表面的； 肤浅的， 浅薄的', 'adj', 'They only have the most superficial understanding of prison life. (他们对监狱生活只有最粗浅的了解。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'opprobrium', '/ə\'prəubriəm/', ' 耻辱； 责骂', 'n', 'His political opinions have attracted the opprobrium of the Left. (他的政治观点遭到左派的抨击。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'mirage', '/mi\'rɑːʒ/', ' 海市蜃楼； 幻想', 'n', 'Perhaps we are just chasing a mirage. (也许我们只是在追逐一个梦。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'impasse', '/\'impæs/', ' 僵局', 'n', 'Negotiations seemed to have reached an impasse. (谈判似乎陷入了僵局。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'subterranean', '/ˌsʌbtə\'reiniən/', ' 地下的', 'adj', 'subterranean passage (地下通道)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'lacerate', '/\'læsəreit/', ' 割裂', 'v', 'His fingers were badly lacerated by the broken glass. (他的手指被碎玻璃严重割伤。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'demolition', '/ˌdemə\'liʃən/', ' 毁坏', 'n', 'The project required the total demolition of the old bridge. (这项工程要求那座旧桥的彻底拆除。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'displacement', '/dis\'pleismənt/', ' 位移', 'n', 'To calculate the field, an assumption of displacement charge is introduced. (为计算这一径向电场，引入了位移电荷的假定。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'oration', '/ɔː\'reiʃən/', ' 演说', 'n', '...a brief funeral oration. (...一篇简短的葬礼悼词。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'casualty', '/\'kæʒjuəlti/', ' 伤亡事故； 人员伤亡', 'n', 'Our aim is to reduce road casualties . (我们的目标是减少交通事故的伤亡人数。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'whimsical', '/\'hwimzikəl/', ' 异想天开的； 反复无常的', 'adj', 'He has a wonderful whimsical sense of humour. (他怪异的幽默感令人惊叹。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'prism', '/\'prizəm/', ' 棱镜', 'n', 'White light can be split by a prism into a whole spectrum of wavelengths . (白光可以用棱镜分解成具有各种波长的整个光谱。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'penury', '/\'penjuri/', ' 贫困， 贫穷', 'n', 'He died in penury in 1644. (1644年他穷困潦倒而死。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'cartographer', '/kɑː\'tɔgrəfə(r)/', ' 地图制作者', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'valedictory', '/ˌvæli\'diktəri/', '告别的； 告别词', 'adj', 'Mr. Walker made his valedictory address after two years as chairman. (在担任主席职务两年后，沃克先生发表了告别演说。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'idolatry', '/ai\'dɔlətri/', ' 偶像崇拜； 盲目崇拜', 'n', 'Their affection for her soon increased almost to idolatry. (他们对她的喜爱几乎发展成了盲目崇拜。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'studious', '/\'stjuːdiəs/', ' 好学的； 刻苦的， 勤奋的', 'adj', 'a quiet, studious young man (一个文静好学的年轻人)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'ridicule', '/\'ridikjuːl/', ' 嘲笑， 奚落', 'v', 'At the time, his ideas were ridiculed. (当时他的观点被人讥笑。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'propulsion', '/prəu\'pʌlʃən/', ' 推进力', 'n', 'research into liquid hydrogen as a means of propulsion (对液态氢作为一种动力方式进行的研究)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'butte', '/bjuːt/', '  孤山， 孤峰', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'sensitive', '/\'sensitiv/', ' 敏感的； 灵敏的', 'adj', 'a very sensitive child (一个很敏感的小孩)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'scintillate', '/\'sintileit/', ' 发出火花', 'v', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'singe', '/sindʒ/', ' 烧焦， 烤焦', 'v', 'The flames had singed her hair. (火焰燎了她的头发。)', 4);
