('en', 'SAT', 'expatriate', '/eks\'pætrieit/', ' 逐出国外', 'v', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'estrange', '/i\'streindʒ/', ' 疏远', 'v', 'The more the physical causes incline mankind to inaction, the more the moral causes should estrange them from it. (所以，物质的因素越使他们趋于懈怠时，精神的因素就越使他们远离物质的因素。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'embrace', '/im\'breis/', ' 拥抱； 包含', 'v', 'Jack warmly embraced his son. (杰克热情拥抱他的儿子。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'intersect', '/ˌintə\'sekt/', ' 直线相交', 'v', 'How many times do the road and railway intersect (with one another) on this map? (在这张地图上公路与铁路（彼此）相交共有多少次?。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'breech', '/briːtʃ/', ' 臀部', 'n', 'If your baby is breech, may need thirty-seven weeks in vitro rotary surgery, obstetrics and gynecology doctors will hand on your belly, try to put the baby upside down. (如果妳的宝宝是臀位，三十七周时可能需要体外回转术，妇产科医生会将手放在妳的腹部，试着把宝宝倒转过来。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'assailant', '/ə\'seilənt/', ' 攻击者', 'n', 'Other partygoers rescued the injured man from his assailant. (其他参加聚会的人从攻击者手中救出了这名受伤的男子。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'nitrogen', '/\'naitrədʒən/', ' 氮', 'n', 'All of these from the group one and two through the group five and six elements, but what about elements, what about molecules like hydrogen, or nitrogen, or maybe oxygen? (所有的这些都是来自于第一主族和第二组主族，到第五主族和第六组主族的悬殊，那么元素呢，比如氢气，氮气或氧气那样的分子呢？)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'judicious', '/dʒu\'diʃəs/', ' 明智的； 审慎的', 'adj', 'a judicious choice (审慎而明智的选择)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'denude', '/di\'njuːd/', ' 使裸露； 剥夺', 'v', 'a hillside denuded in a fire (被一场火烧得光秃秃的山坡)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'vermin', '/\'vəːmin/', ' 害虫， 害兽， 寄生虫', 'n', 'The beds were filthy and full of vermin. (那些床铺肮脏不堪，而且爬满了虫子。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'modify', '/\'mɔdifai/', ' 更改， 修改， 改造， 修饰', 'vt', 'The feedback will be used to modify the course for next year. (这些反馈意见将用于修改明年的课程。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'steadfast', '/\'stedfɑːst/', ' 稳定的； 坚定的， 忠实的', 'adj', 'her father’s steadfast love for her (她父亲对她永不改变的爱)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'effusive', '/i\'fjuːsiv/', ' 过分热情的', 'adj', 'Our host gave us an effusive welcome. (主人热情地欢迎我们。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'mariner', '/\'mærinə/', ' 水手', 'n', 'A smooth sea never makes a skillful mariner. (平静的大海造就不出熟练的水手。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'villainous', '/\'vilənəs/', ' 恶毒的， 缺德的', 'adj', 'He was branded by the press as "villainous" and "diabolical." (他被媒体贴上了“恶棍”和“魔鬼”的标签。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'detest', '/di\'test/', ' 厌恶， 憎恨', 'v', 'The two men detested each other. (两个男人互相厌恶。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'exempt', '/ig\'zempt/', ' 被免除  的， 被豁免的；免除，豁免', 'adj', 'Men in college were exempt from military service. (在校男大学生免服兵役。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'theorize', '/\'θiəraiz/', ' 建立理论， 理论化', 'v', 'Police are theorizing that the robbers may be posing as hitchhikers. (警方推测那些劫匪可能会装成搭便车的人。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'reservoir', '/\'rezəvwaː/', ' 水库， 蓄水池', 'n', 'The waste can be fatal if swallowed. Police are investigating what caused the reservoir to break. (如果吞咽这些废水可以致命。警方正在调查导致水库破堤的原因。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'fawn', '/fɔːn/', ' 奉承， 讨好', 'v', NULL, 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'albeit', '/ɔːl\'biːit/', ' 虽然', 'conj', 'He accepted the job, albeit with some hesitation. (尽管有些犹豫，他还是接受了那份工作。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'aesthetic', '/iːs\'θetik/', ' 美学的， 艺术的； 审美的', 'adj', 'From an esthetic point of view, it’s a nice design. (从美学角度看，这是个不错的设计。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'incongruous', '/in\'kɔŋgruəs/', ' 不调和的； 不适宜的', 'adj', 'The new theatre looks utterly incongruous in its setting. (这座新剧院和周围的环境格格不入。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'tendency', '/\'tendənsi/', ' 趋向， 趋势', 'n', '...the government\'s tendency to secrecy in recent years. (…近年来政府的保密倾向。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'furbish', '/\'fəːbiʃ/', ' 擦亮； 磨光', 'v', 'If you furbish up these old chairs you\'ll have a better chance of selling them. (你要是把这些旧椅子擦亮，就会更好卖些。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'caption', '/\'kæpʃn/', '标题； 加上标题； 加上说明', 'n', 'A single ampersand is displayed in the caption and no characters are underlined. (这样，在标题中显示单个“&”符，并且没有带下划线的字符。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'arithmetic', '/ə\'riθmətik/', ' 算术', 'n', '...teaching the basics of reading, writing and arithmetic. (…教授读、写、算的基本知识。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'knighthood', '/\'naithud/', ' 骑士身份， 骑士风格， 侠义精神', 'n', 'When he finally received his knighthood in 1975 Chaplin was 85. (当他最终在1975年得到爵士封号时，卓别林已经85岁了。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'variation', '/ˌveəri\'eiʃən/', ' 变化， 变动； 变种， 变异', 'n', 'Most of his poems are variations on the theme of love. (他的大部分诗作都是有关爱情主题的形式不同的作品。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'subconscious', '/ˌsʌb\'kɔnʃəs/', ' 下意识的', 'adj', 'a subconscious fear of failure (对失败下意识的恐惧)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'carbohydrate', '/\'kɑːbəu\'haidreit/', ' 糖类', 'n', NULL, 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'chateau', '/\'ʃætəu/', ' 城堡； 别墅', 'n', 'There is no grand chateau, no marble staircase. (他们没有宏伟的庄园别墅，没有大理石阶梯。)', 3),
