('en', 'SAT', 'rebut', '/ri\'bʌt/', ' 反驳； 揭穿', 'v', 'He spent most of his speech rebutting criticisms of his foreign policy. (他大部分的演讲都用来反驳他在外交政策上受到的各种批评。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'morass', '/mə\'ræs/', ' 沼泽； 困境', 'n', 'We’re trying to drag the country out of its economic morass. (我们在尽力使国家摆脱经济困境。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'rhombus', '/\'rɔmbəs/', ' 菱形', 'n', 'There is a small network of rhombus in tokyo astronomical observatory . (在东京天文台有一个小的菱形台网。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'telepathy', '/ti\'lepəθi/', ' 心灵感应， 感应', 'n', 'You never tell me what you\'re thinking. Am I supposed to use telepathy? (你从来不告诉我你在想什么。我是不是该用心灵感应术呢？)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'captious', '/\'kæpʃəs/', ' 吹毛求疵的； 挑剔的', 'adj', 'Terry: Oh, Ben. I was assigned to see that captious client this afternoon. He is really the most ticklish client I have ever met. Seeing is believing! (泰瑞：噢，本，今天指派我去会见那个吹毛求疵的客户，他真是我见过最难对付的客户了，真是百闻不如一见啊！)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'frenetic', '/frə\'netik/', ' 发狂的； 狂热的', 'adj', 'She rushes from job to job at a frenetic pace. (她发疯似的不停地跳槽。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'nonchalant', '/ˌnɔnʃə\'lɑːnt/', ' 冷淡的', 'adj', 'Clark\'s mother is nonchalant about her role in her son\'s latest work. (克拉克的母亲对她在儿子最新作品中的角色反应平淡。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'shrubbery', '/\'ʃrʌbəri/', ' 灌木林', 'n', 'a tangled mass of overgrown shrubbery (枝蔓交错、疯狂生长的灌木丛)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'script', '/skript/', ' 剧本， 广播稿； 文字体系； 笔迹， 手迹', 'n', 'a diary entry written in neat black script (用工整的黑色字写下的一则日记)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'guise', '/gaiz/', ' 外观， 装束； 伪装， 假装', 'n', 'It’s the same idea in a different guise. (还是一样的观点，只是形式不同。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'likelihood', '/\'laiklihud/', ' 可能， 可能性', 'n', 'If I refused, it would in all likelihood mean I’d lose my job. (如果我拒绝，那我十有八九会丢掉工作。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'reactionary', '/ri\'ækʃənəri/', ' 反作用的， 反动的', 'adj', 'reactionary attitudes (反动的态度)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'imprudent', '/im\'pruːdənt/', ' 不谨慎的； 轻率的', 'adj', 'The banks made hundreds of imprudent loans in the 1970s. (20世纪70年代那几家银行轻率地发放了几百笔贷款。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'drastic', '/\'dræstik/', ' 激烈的；  猛烈的', 'adj', 'drastic cuts in government spending (政府开支的急剧削减)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'venial', '/\'viːniəl/', ' 可宽恕的', 'adj', 'a venial sin  (可赦之罪)', 4),
