('en', 'SAT', 'metabolic', '/ˌmetə\'bɔlik/', ' 变化的； 新陈代谢的', 'adj', 'Exercise can increase your metabolic rate. (运动可以提高新陈代谢率。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'tremor', '/\'tremə/', ' 震动； 颤动', 'n', 'News of 160 lay-offs had sent tremors through the community. (裁员160人的消息在社区中引起了波动。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'plummet', '/\'plʌmit/', ' 垂直落下；铅锤', 'v', 'The plane plummeted towards the Earth. (那架飞机直坠向地面。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'set', '/set/', ' 集合', 'n', 'The set (x, y) has two members. (（x, y）这个集里有两个项。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'punctuate', '/\'pʌŋktjueit/', ' 加标点于； 不时打断； 强调', 'v', 'The silence was occasionally punctuated by laughter. (寂静间或被笑声打破。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'column', '/\'kɔləm/', ' 列； 圆柱', 'n', 'Seven massive columns rise up from a marble floor. (七根巨大的圆柱从大理石地面拔地而起。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'portent', '/\'pɔːtent/', ' 征兆', 'n', 'The savage civil war there could be a portent of what\'s to come in the rest of the region. (那里的野蛮战争可能预示着该地区将要发生什么事情。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'procedure', '/prə\'siːdʒə/', ' 手续， 步骤', 'n', 'On board, we were given the usual talk on safety procedures (= what to do if an accident happens, or to prevent an accident ) . (在飞机上，我们听了例行的飞行安全讲解。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'biography', '/bai\'ɔgrəfi/', ' 传记', 'n', '...recent biographies of Stalin. (…近年的斯大林传记。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'integrate', '/\'intigreit/', '  成为一体，  结合在一起，  合并', 'v', 'He didn\'t integrate successfully into the Italian way of life. (他没有成功融入到意大利的生活方式中去。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'pique', '/piːk/', ' 不满， 生气', 'n', 'He stormed out in a fit of pique . (他气呼呼地冲了出去。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'pompous', '/\'pɔmpəs/', ' 华而不实的； 自命不凡的； 浮华的', 'adj', 'He seems rather pompous. (他看上去相当自负。)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'decry', '/di\'krai/', ' 谴责', 'v', 'They rightly decry the unhealthily close ties of some European politicians to their counterparts in Russia. (他们谴责了一些欧洲和俄罗斯政客之间过分亲密的关系。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'validity', '/və\'lidəti/', ' 有效性， 正确性', 'n', 'We should question the validity of those figures. (我们应当查询那些数字的正确性。)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'earnest', '/\'əːnist/', ' 热心的， 诚挚的， 认真的', 'adj', 'a rather earnest young man (相当认真的一个年轻人)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'shrinkage', '/\'ʃriŋkidʒ/', ' 收缩', 'n', 'Pollution led to a shrinkage of grasslands. (污染导致草原面积缩小。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'spider', '/\'spaidə/', ' 蜘蛛', 'n', 'What should I find but an enormous spider! (我居然发现了一只巨大的蜘蛛！)', 5),
('en', 'SAT', 'inordinate', '/i\'nɔːdinit/', ' 紊乱的； 过分的', 'adj', 'Testing is taking up an inordinate amount of teachers’ time. (测验占去了教师们太多的时间。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'testimonial', '/ˌtesti\'məuniəl/', ' 证明书', 'n', 'She could hardly expect her employer to provide her with testimonials to her character and ability. (她几乎不指望老板会给她写证明她的人品和能力的证明书。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'precede', '/ˌpriː\'siːd/', ' 领先 ， 在  前； 优先， 先于', 'v', 'a type of cloud that precedes rain (下雨前出现的一种云)', 3),
('en', 'SAT', 'disillusion', '/ˌdisi\'ljuːʒən/', ' 觉醒； 幻灭', 'v', 'I hate to disillusion you, but I don’t think she’s coming back. (我真不愿意让你失望，但我想她是不会回来了。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'humorous', '/\'hjuːmərəs/', ' 幽默的， 诙谐的', 'adj', 'humorous stories (诙谐的故事)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'deride', '/di\'raid/', ' 嘲弄， 嘲笑', 'v', 'You shouldn’t deride their efforts. (你不应该嘲笑他们的努力。)', 4),
('en', 'SAT', 'vehement', '/\'viːimənt/', ' 激烈的， 猛烈的；  热烈的', 'adj', 'She suddenly became very vehement and agitated, jumping around and shouting. (她突然变得十分激动和不安，四处暴跳并大喊大叫。)', 4);
